window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"title":"Chapter 137","paragraphs":["Disaster (2)","The sight of my completely devastated yard left me disheartened, but I tried to think positively.","I would treat this as a learning experience and prepare more thoroughly next time.","There was nothing I wouldn’t do to survive in this damned forest.","I could ask the dwarf to replace the barricade, and I could begin by gathering the materials needed to rebuild the furnace and oven.","I had already built them once, so as long as I retained access to the Gallery, restoring them should not be difficult.","Yet that sapling survived.","Everything else had been swept away, but the sapling given to me by Let’s Grow a Tree remained firmly rooted.","I was extremely curious about what kind of tree it was, but I decided not to dwell on it. Its survival was a good thing.","I should focus on preparing for disasters first.","These could not be called mere changes in climate. Each one was closer to a full-fledged natural disaster.","This was a place where an avalanche could occur despite the terrain seemingly making one impossible.","As someone had said, spring might bring not yellow dust, but an outright sandstorm.","I need to build an emergency exit too, and postpone any crafting projects until winter ends.","This was my first winter, and it was taking place in the Forest of Four Seasons. I had a mountain of work ahead of me.","I sighed at the overwhelming prospect and turned my head.","In that direction stood the grave where my senior had been buried.","How did that man survive here?","He had clearly lived here longer than I had. The sheer length of his diary made that obvious.","The diary should contain everything he experienced before his conflict with the gorillas led to his death.","They must have finished translating it by now, right?","I had entrusted the translation to All-Father and Necromancy Is Love .","Yet aside from information about the Immortal King and the gorillas, I had learned nothing from it.","It would have been nice if the diary had warned me that winter could arrive early.","I should ask.","I planned to remain holed up in the cave until the season changed.","This was as good an opportunity as any to ask about it.","I contacted All-Father first.","[Wild Grylls: All-Father, are you there?]","[All-Father: What is it?]","[Wild Grylls: Do you remember those records from the Balkan Kingdom that I sent you? Have you finished translating them?]","[All-Father: Not all of them. The Balkan royal family used certain unique expressions, so the translation is taking longer than expected.]","That was understandable.","I had never asked him to report his progress in real time, and rushing people was not in my nature.","Still, he should have uncovered some important facts by now.","I immediately asked my question.","[Wild Grylls: Did the records mention the seasons changing abruptly?]","[All-Father: They did. It appears winter arrived in an instant for him as well, just as it did for you.]","Just as I had expected.","My senior had experienced the same phenomenon.","This proved that even this godforsaken forest followed certain rules.","[Wild Grylls: Were there any warning signs?]","[All-Father: The diary says that large numbers of animals migrated the day before. He wrote that he warmly welcomed them.]","[Wild Grylls: Does it say how long winter lasted?]","[All-Father: Yes. Winter itself did not last long. The weather warmed after approximately five days.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s a relief.]","[All-Father: It also contains a description suggesting that all four seasons occur within a single month. You should keep that in mind.]","I felt strangely embarrassed.","Still, after what had happened with the raccoons slaughtered by the fast sloth, I could hardly be blamed.","Besides, the group I had encountered had been prepared to seize my shelter if the opportunity arose.","At any rate, I now knew the warning sign.","All that remained was to learn how long this winter would last.","Several months would already have been despair-inducing. If it lasted for years, it would have been horrifying.","Thankfully, that did not seem to be the case.","What kind of premature four-season cycle was this?","It was absurd.","Still, every season except winter had been relatively livable, so I was not too worried.","So this weather is why unintelligent animals can’t survive here.","They either possessed exceptional instincts like Wonmo or were intelligent like the raccoons.","It had to be one or the other.","Otherwise, surviving in this forest would be impossible.","The greatest danger here was not its predators, but the environment itself.","[All-Father: Ah, there is also some information you should take to heart. It concerns the gorillas in the jungle.]","[Wild Grylls: The gorillas?]","[All-Father: Yes. It appears one of them has separated from the group. The gorilla you encountered merely warned you, but the one that attacked this man did so without any provocation.]","[Wild Grylls: That sounds ominous.]","[All-Father: I do not know where it is now, but you should remain cautious. According to the records, unlike the other gorillas, its fur is white. Its eyes are also said to be as red as blood.]","White fur and red eyes immediately brought albinism to mind.","I should consider the possibility that it was an albino.","Albino animals stood out more than others, so their survival rates were likely lower.","If such an animal had survived until now, it must possess incredible strength.","It might have an even worse temper than the gorilla leader.","As a mutant, it might have developed unusually high aggression.","If this one had also learned martial arts, I would be in serious trouble.","It would be a difficult fight.","The problem is that I have no idea where it might appear.","So far, I had not seen anything with white fur.","I nodded as I processed the information All-Father had provided, then decided to ask whether there were any other dangers.","[Wild Grylls: Is there anything else I should be wary of?]","[All-Father: It is less a warning than an unusual detail. This man originally suffered from mana insensitivity and was incapable of using mana.]","[Wild Grylls: Mana insensitivity?]","[All-Father: Yes. It is a congenital condition that prevents a person from accumulating mana. However, while living in the Forest of Four Seasons, he gradually began accumulating it.]","[Wild Grylls: Does that mean he evolved too?]","[All-Father: I cannot say for certain. Apparently, he ate anything he could find in order to survive, and at some point discovered that he could use mana.]","All-Father’s explanation was as follows.","My senior had been unable to accumulate mana because of a medical condition, whereas I had been unable to accept mana in the first place because I came from another world.","Regardless, it proved that the medicinal plants scattered throughout the Forest of Four Seasons possessed astonishing effects.","Of course, poisonous plants were probably mixed among them, so I would have to proceed cautiously.","[Wild Grylls: Does the diary say which medicinal plant he ate? That seems like important information.]","[All-Father: Unfortunately, I do not know. He ate random plants in an attempt to kill himself, so he neither identified nor properly recorded them.]","[Wild Grylls: Yikes.]","[All-Father: If he wanted to die, he could simply have eaten a mushroom. What a peculiar man. Hohoho.]","[Wild Grylls: Sir?]","[All-Father: It was a joke. In any event, even the weeds appear comparable to medicinal herbs. Pulling up a few at random and testing them might not be a bad idea.]","The possibility that even ordinary weeds might be medicinal filled me with hope.","[Wild Grylls: I see. Could I ask you to analyze some weeds? I’ll send you several varieties.]","[All-Father: My apologies, but I expect to become rather busy from now on. I intend to begin participating in external affairs.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh, I see. Then I’ll ask someone else.]","Even if All-Father was unavailable, I still had the Starlight Princess.","If she was too busy as well, then...","I would have to figure it out myself.","Once I identified their effects, I intended to send them directly to the Heavenly Demon.","That should help him finish the fast sloth’s food sooner.","After ending my conversation with All-Father, I was casually browsing the Gallery when—","[Necromancy Is Love: Save me.]","[Wild Grylls: What?]","[Necromancy Is Love: Keep talking to All-Father.]","[Wild Grylls: Did something happen?]","I received that strange message from Necromancy Is Love .","Even when I asked what was wrong, I received no response.","I wondered whether I should contact All-Father again, but ultimately decided against it.","If it were truly urgent, he would have made a public post on the Gallery instead of sending me a message.","There really are all kinds of strange people here.","I brushed it aside and focused on my own situation.","The seasons changed approximately once a week, so I merely had to prepare accordingly.","Besides, this was already the second day of winter.","I should only have to endure another three or four days.","Does this mean farming will be difficult?","I had planned to begin farming if necessary, but it seemed impractical.","The seasons did not change monthly, but weekly. Ordinary plants would have difficulty surviving that.","Then again, perhaps crops would grow rapidly, like the sapling that had undergone a sudden growth spurt before.","Even if I stockpile crops, I’ll need to preserve them properly...","Storage was the greatest problem.","Meat could simply be salted and smoked.","Crops, however, would rot easily if left unattended.","I could not help worrying about it.","I’d need something like a refrigerator, but that’s impossible. Maybe I could use ice instead...","The instant the word ice crossed my mind, my head snapped up.","At the same time, I checked the time through the Gallery.","It was only two o’clock, so I still had plenty of time.","I hurriedly rose, armed myself, and rushed outside.","The fast sloth was taking good care of Wonmo, so there was no need to worry about him.","My destination was the river.","The abrupt change of season had frozen it solid.","Why had I failed to realize that there was a convenient source of ice right in front of me?","I can’t just collect it without preparing first. I need to build a storage container—or an icehouse.","Wait. Ice?","My ancestors had collected ice every winter and stored it inside icehouses.","I intended to do the same.","The animals were less active during winter, so as long as I remained vigilant, I should be able to gather the ice without much difficulty.","I leaned forward to check how thickly the river had frozen.","The abrupt drop in temperature had transformed it into a river of transparent ice.","At most, I have four days. I need to build an icehouse—or at least a storage container—before then.","No matter how effective salting was for preservation, it could not compare to refrigeration.","Crops and fruit would also keep better in a cool place, so this was the perfect opportunity to build one.","With my decision made, I returned to the shelter and wrote a post on the Gallery.","I knew that my ancestors had used stone icehouses, but I knew nothing about how they actually worked.","Title: Does anyone know how to build a stone icehouse?","Wild Grylls","(A photo of the frozen river)","I’m thinking about building one of those stone icehouses our ancestors used. There’s a frozen river right in front of me, so it seems like a good idea.","└ SwordMaster: An icehouse? Would you like me to give you a well-insulated box? You could probably fill it with ice.","└ Wild Grylls: That would work too, but I think building an actual icehouse would be better.","└ SwordMaster: It is not a bad choice, but could you not build it slowly?","└ Wild Grylls: The diary said the seasons change every week. That’s why I should make the most of what I can only do during winter.","└ SwordMaster: What a half-baked cycle of seasons.","└ Passing Dwarf: Damn, it’s been ages since I heard anyone mention an icehouse. Refrigerators were invented around my father’s time.","└ Wild Grylls: Do you know how to build one?","└ Passing Dwarf: The principle itself is simple. It’s just difficult to construct. I’ll make a post about it soon.","└ Wild Grylls: Thanks, thanks.","└ Aren’t icehouses still fairly common?","└ There are plenty in rural areas that haven’t been urbanized. Refrigerators have been spreading there recently, though.","The dwarf had promised to explain how to build one, so all I could do now was wait.","The disaster had dealt me a tremendous blow, but it had also presented me with an opportunity.","I was beginning to understand that winter was not merely a season to endure.","The avalanche came from behind the cave, so I should build the entrance on this side.","Until the dwarf explained the structure and construction process of a stone icehouse, I began working on what I could.","First came logging.","If I wanted to survive the winter, firewood was indispensable.","\"Hm?\"","It happened while I was diligently cutting down trees.","Something behind a fallen tree caught my eye.","All the smaller plants had been buried beneath the snow, yet this one stood upright by itself.","It was a blue flower that looked as though ice crystals had blossomed into petals.","I could not tell whether it had frozen solid or simply looked that way naturally.","What is this?","Whenever I was curious, the Gallery was the obvious place to ask.","I immediately took a picture and uploaded a post.","Title: Found a strange flower.","Wild Grylls","(A plant resembling a flower made from ice crystals)","Found this while cutting down trees. Does anyone know what it is?","└ Starlight Princess: Oh! I think that’s a Frostbloom.","└ Wild Grylls: What’s that?","└ Starlight Princess: If you absorb all of it, you should gain resistance to cold.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh...!","└ Starlight Princess: But if you eat it as it is, your entire body will freeze solid.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh.","└ Starlight Princess: And it melts almost immediately once the weather changes, so it would be difficult to ask someone else to process it.","What is it, a goddamned sunfish?","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 138","paragraphs":["Combination (1)","The Frostbloom would freeze your entire body as solid as the ice inside a stone icehouse if consumed raw.","If moved elsewhere and exposed to even the slightest change in temperature, it would melt like snow.","But if properly processed and consumed, it could grant powerful resistance to the cold.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there a way to process it?","└ Starlight Princess: I could probably do it with the technology in my workshop, but I’m not sure it would be possible in your environment. And even if you brought it to my workshop, it would melt immediately.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there any way I could do it by myself?","└ Starlight Princess: The important part is controlling the cold energy... For reference, you can’t simply boil it like soup.","└ Wild Grylls: Tsk...","I wanted to consume it somehow.","Resistance to cold would provide an enormous advantage.","It was so cold that even thick clothing barely kept me warm enough to avoid freezing to death.","You’d need fire energy to counteract the cold energy.","Could she at least explain the basic principle?","If I could absorb the Frostbloom, it would greatly improve my chances of survival.","At the very least, I’d be far less likely to die of hypothermia.","Even simply no longer shivering in the cold would be worthwhile.","Accumulating advantages like this one by one was how I became stronger.","The Starlight Princess did not reply for some time, seemingly lost in thought.","Just when I began wondering whether she had gone off to do something else, she posted another comment.","└ Wild Grylls: Didn’t people in ancient times eat these and record their effects? They wouldn’t have had extraction devices back then.","└ Starlight Princess: Why would anyone do something like that? It could kill them.","└ Wild Grylls: Then why do people eat pufferfish?","└ Starlight Princess: Oh.","└ That’s a damn good example. LOL","└ Who was the first lunatic to think of eating pufferfish? LOL","└ One mistake while preparing it and the poison kills you immediately.","└ I’m more curious about the first person who thought of drinking milk. How did they come up with the idea of sucking on an animal’s teat...?","└ All those attempts accumulated over time and gave us the ingredients we have today. Let’s show them some respect.","└ Not admiration, but \"respect.\" LOL","└ Starlight Princess: You place the Frostbloom in an extractor, then infuse fire energy into the extracted liquid. The principle itself is simple.","└ Wild Grylls: Is that extractor something I could use?","└ Starlight Princess: It needs to be connected to a mana circuit, like a refrigerator. If I gave it to you, wouldn’t it become nothing more than an empty metal shell?","└ Wild Grylls: T_T","└ Starlight Princess: I hate to say this, but I think you should give up.","└ Wild Grylls: I really can’t just boil it in a pot?","└ Starlight Princess: Hmm... I’ve never attempted such a primitive method, so I’m not sure. The extractor is the only method I know.","Humans were fascinating.","We had eaten all manner of plants and animals.","We had even discovered methods of preparing the poisonous ones.","Pufferfish, for example, must have required an arduous process of trial and error before people discovered how to prepare it safely.","The same logic applied to the Frostbloom.","The Starlight Princess had not realized it, but this was the detail that caught my attention.","The Frostbloom was an extremely delicate medicinal herb that melted the instant the temperature changed even slightly.","Yet records existed of people consuming it and documenting both its effects and side effects.","In other words, people living in cold regions must have discovered those properties through repeated testing.","Even if there’s no record of anyone extracting it, someone must have found a way to consume it.","It was highly likely that someone had extracted it without specialized equipment or consumed it after it had been refined through some other process.","Still, this was only my hypothesis.","They said that someone who had read only one book was more dangerous than someone who had read none at all.","└ Wild Grylls: What if I post updates in real time while I experiment? If you notice anything strange, please tell me immediately.","└ Starlight Princess: That’s not a bad idea. But you must follow everything I say without question. Understood?","└ Wild Grylls: Of course. The stone icehouse takes priority, so I’ll contact you about this later.","└ Starlight Princess: Please don’t push yourself too far.","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey. That stone icehouse needs to be built underground. Don’t you have mithril inside your home?","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t have to build it inside the cave. I can build it outside. There’s no mithril out there.","└ Passing Dwarf: Then do you know which direction the wind blows? Not in winter—in summer.","└ Wild Grylls: Why does that matter?","└ Passing Dwarf: From what I can tell, you’ll need to use convection. Cold air sinks to the floor while hot air rises.","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t know. I’m only building a temporary one anyway, so just explain the basic principles. It only needs to last one month. The seasons here apparently change every week.","└ Passing Dwarf: What kind of ridiculous place is that? Anyway, got it. I’ll make a post soon.","Now I had to learn the direction of the wind as well.","This was getting absurd.","Fortunately, the seasons here changed weekly. If they lasted an entire month each, this would have been far more troublesome.","It seemed best to build the stone icehouse as a prototype and use a storage box for everything else.","SwordMaster had offered to give me a box made from well-insulated materials, so I could simply accept that.","But it would feel wrong to receive it without giving her anything in return...","What should I give her?","SwordMaster was actually the most difficult person to repay.","The Heavenly Demon would happily accept anything I gave him, but SwordMaster was different.","She refused medicinal herbs because she did not want to become stronger, and she barely cared about food.","She was someone who focused solely on my growth, which made it difficult to decide how to repay her.","Would she like a sword?","She did not merely like swordsmanship—she loved it.","Following that logic, perhaps she would like swords as well.","A master did not blame their tools, but that did not mean they were entirely indifferent to them.","Perhaps she would even enjoy a beautiful sword.","I can think about that slowly. First, I need to understand the icehouse’s structure.","I had plenty of time to think, but not much time to build.","The avalanche had swept everything away, leaving me with a long list of things to reconstruct.","Should I rebuild the furnace and oven more sturdily from the beginning? Or should I put them inside the cave?","While considering it, I sent SwordMaster a message.","I proposed giving her an exceptionally fine sword later in exchange for an insulated storage box.","[SwordMaster: She sent me a picture just to brag about hers. ;;]","[Wild Grylls: ;;]","The Heavenly Demon was acting awfully childish for someone her age.","Still, at least she had not made a public post about it.","And the fact that she had bragged specifically to SwordMaster suggested that she regarded SwordMaster as a friend.","SwordMaster would probably fly into a rage if she heard me say that, but it should be fine.","[Wild Grylls: In any case, I’ll give it to you later. Would you accept it?]","[SwordMaster: It’s fine. A master does not blame their tools.]","[Wild Grylls: It glows when you channel mana into it, though.]","[SwordMaster: I suppose there’s nothing wrong with keeping one as an ornament rather than using it in battle.]","[SwordMaster: Did you give that sword to the Heavenly Demon?]","[Wild Grylls: Huh? Did I mention that before?]","It was an outstanding sword, yet she intended to use it merely as decoration.","Still, I was relieved that she was willing to accept it.","Trading a Misricon sword for an insulated box could hardly be called an equal exchange, but that did not matter.","I only had to consider all the help SwordMaster had given me.","Until now, she had assisted me almost entirely without compensation.","The Heavenly Demon might feel neglected, so I should prepare something separately for her.","With that thought, I examined the box SwordMaster had sent me.","Perhaps because plastic had not yet been invented in her world, it looked like an ordinary wooden box from the outside.","Its interior walls, however, were surrounded by multiple materials, including marble.","Given how many layers it had, it should function well as an icebox.","Now I merely needed to fill it with ice.","I moved the box inside and thanked SwordMaster.","\"The dwarf... posted it.\"","Perfectly timed, the dwarf had uploaded his instructions.","I opened the post immediately.","Title: Here’s the structure of a stone icehouse. Take a look.","Passing Dwarf","(An image of a stone icehouse’s structure)","(A cross-sectional diagram of a stone icehouse)","(An image of a stone icehouse surrounded by brick walls)","(An image of a brick-vaulted ceiling)","It looks roughly like this.","Building it properly will take a long time, so take it slowly.","When you put the ice inside, pack snow or straw into the gaps between the blocks. Buy a straw mat from the auction house and pull it apart.","└ Wild Grylls: Wait. The ceiling has to be built from bricks too? How am I supposed to do that?","└ Passing Dwarf: What do you mean, how? Use your ingenuity.","└ Wild Grylls: Damn. This is going to be brutal.","└ Where did you take those pictures? The cross-section aside, the others look like actual photographs.","└ Passing Dwarf: They were in a museum.","└ Grylls is the only bastard here living in a museum. LOL","└ Everyone else uses refrigerators while he’s stuck using a stone icehouse. LOL","People whose civilizations had barely reached the modern era were mocking me as a primitive.","I’ll have you know that I once enjoyed the pinnacle of modern civilization.","These people would wet themselves if they witnessed the destructive power of a nuclear bomb, yet they dared make fun of me.","So how am I supposed to build this?","There’s nothing else I can do, so I should shut up and build the stone icehouse.","Grumbling inwardly, I gathered my pickaxe and shovel.","Given how late it was, I had no intention of completing the work in a single day.","It’s supposed to be partially underground, right?","Ordinarily, I would have needed to account for the direction of the wind, but this one was merely experimental.","It would serve as a foundation for testing whether ice could be preserved for an entire month.","I planned to keep it small to reduce the labor involved, while still building it carefully.","The frozen ground isn’t making this easy.","Even digging the ground took a long time.","It would be better to light a campfire and work on something else while it thawed the frozen earth.","I continued digging until around four o’clock, then stopped.","I had other tasks to handle, including extracting the Frostbloom.","I’ll spend thirty minutes harvesting ice, then prepare the Frostbloom.","Carrying the insulated box, I headed toward the river.","With winter’s arrival, animal activity had dropped considerably.","Unless I encountered something that remained active during winter, such as a wolf, I was unlikely to be attacked.","I was staying vigilant just in case, so I would not be caught helplessly off guard either.","I’ll need to cut it with a saw, right?","Upon reaching the frozen river, I purchased a saw from the auction house.","I tapped the ice’s surface with the small hammer I had brought, then inserted the saw into it.","Scrape! Scrape! Scrape!","I began sawing out a precise square.","Now that I was cutting through it, I realized the river had not frozen all the way to the bottom. At a certain depth, the saw suddenly broke through.","Keeping that in mind, I continued cutting carefully.","\"Heave-ho!\"","Splash!","I extracted a neatly cut rectangular block of ice, and river water immediately filled the empty space.","Crackle!","Before long, even that water froze solid in the brutal cold.","Just how cold did it have to be for water to freeze almost instantly?","With considerable effort, I carried the transparent block of ice to the box and placed it inside.","I had noticed it while cutting, but the ice was incredibly thick.","Could I go ice fishing too?","The idle thought crossed my mind, but I dismissed it.","I continued harvesting ice while remaining alert in case something like a golden frog suddenly emerged.","Fortunately, there was no reaction from beneath the ice. Either all the frogs had frozen to death or they were hibernating.","Apparently, winter was the season in which I could live with relatively little fear.","\"Ugh. My hands sting.\"","That did not change the fact that my hands were freezing.","I wore another pair of gloves over the World Tree gloves, making two layers in total, yet my hands were still cold.","The icy moisture had seeped through both layers.","At this rate, I might end up with frostbite.","I hurriedly finished the work and returned to the cave.","I had collected four blocks of ice in total.","For now, I placed them inside the box, but once the stone icehouse was complete, I intended to store them there.","\"There’s... plenty of time.\"","Now that I had finished collecting the ice, all that remained was the Frostbloom.","One might ask why I did not simply extract it inside the cave, but I had an idea.","The mature mandrake.","The mature mandrake was a plant that contained yang energy.","And I had heard that yang energy represented heat.","Therefore, wouldn’t boiling the cold-energy-filled Frostbloom together with the mature mandrake work?","Thud! Smack! Thump!","\"Squeak! Skree! Gweck!\"","And so, I beat the mature mandrake senseless.","This thing had to be beaten before it would behave.","Carrying the limp mature mandrake, I returned to the cave.","I then prepared a suitable pot and lit the campfire.","As soon as the fire was burning, I made a post on the Gallery.","Title: Combining a Frostbloom with a mature mandrake","Wild Grylls","(A photo of the battered mature mandrake)","(A photo of the Frostbloom before harvesting)","Wouldn’t combining these two work?","└ Heavenly Demon: The theory itself does not seem unsound. It is an appropriate combination of yang and yin.","└ Wild Grylls: Right?","└ Starlight Princess: As the Heavenly Demon said, the theory isn’t bad. Although it does seem a little... crude.","└ Wild Grylls: Should I put them both in a pot and boil them together?","└ Starlight Princess: That would probably be best. Extracting their essences would somewhat weaken their energies, so boiling them raw may actually work better.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood.","Now that I had received permission from an expert, I harvested the Frostbloom.","Fortunately, human body heat did not appear to affect it, and it retained its original shape.","Now I put them in together...","I added a little water as well. That should allow their properties to seep out like a broth.","Once I covered the pot with its lid, all the preparations were complete.","Now I merely had to wait.","I did not forget to check periodically for anything unusual.","└ Wild Grylls: (Video showing the Frostbloom and mature mandrake still unchanged) Nothing has changed yet. The Frostbloom hasn’t even melted.","└ Starlight Princess: That’s probably because they’re both rare medicinal plants. You should wait patiently.","If I opened the lid, the mandrake’s screams would fill the entire cave.","I left it as it was and hurriedly asked the Gallery for advice.","How long would I have to simmer them before something changed?","I added another piece of firewood.","I wanted to work on something else, but I had no idea what might happen if I left the pot unattended.","And so I sat there, staring into the fire.","Clatter!","The pot’s lid suddenly began rattling.","\"Skreeeeeeee!!\"","The mandrake’s scream rang out from inside it.","Had it awakened after enough time had passed?","That would be a serious problem.","Do I need to beat it unconscious again?","I pressed down on the lid to prevent the mature mandrake from bursting out.","└ Wild Grylls: (Video of screams coming from the pot) I think the mandrake woke up. What should I do? I’m holding the lid shut for now.","└ Starlight Princess: Letting it continue screaming isn’t good either. Even if it’s risky, you should knock it unconscious again.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood.","After receiving the expert’s advice, I took a deep breath.","I would have to time this perfectly.","The mature mandrake did not scream continuously. It only shrieked intermittently.","It would fall silent and then begin screaming again.","Therefore, I had to act during one of the quiet intervals.","\"Skreeeeeeee!!\"","Before long, the mandrake screamed once more.","I waited until it fell silent, then immediately removed the lid.","And what I saw was—","\"What the hell is this?\"","The mature mandrake had turned completely blue.","Its face was so blue that it looked dead, yet it was clearly alive and thrashing around.","It had originally been red, so its sudden transformation into blue was even more bewildering.","Did they fuse instead of combine?","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 139","paragraphs":["Combination (2)","The mature mandrake had turned blue, apparently after absorbing the Ice Blossom.","Mature mandrakes really did resemble humans, which only made them more frightening.","Its eyes were wide open, and its mouth opened and closed like a goldfish’s. It genuinely looked as though it were moments away from freezing to death.","I wondered what I should do with it, then decided to leave a comment first.","The Starlight Princess would probably know at least something about this phenomenon.","└ Wild Grylls: (Video of the blue mandrake) It turned out like this. What happened to it?","└ Starlight Princess: Huh? Why did it end up like that? Why is it blue?","└ Wild Grylls: Excuse me?;;","└ Uh. Why’d that thing turn blue?","└ Did it get a blue badge too?","└ Looks like it just died. What blue badge are you talking about?;;","Even the Starlight Princess seemed bewildered.","If that was the case, I was screwed.","But as they said, even when the sky collapsed, there was always a hole to escape through.","Not long afterward, the Starlight Princess posted another comment explaining the probable cause.","└ He’s seriously trying to turn everything in the Forest of the Four Seasons into liquor, lol.","└ He’ll be making snake wine next, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: From the looks of it, the mature mandrake seems to have absorbed the Ice Blossom... First, we need to check whether it’s still alive. Could you poke it with a chopstick or a twig?","└ Wild Grylls: I poked it, but all it did was open and close its mouth.","└ Starlight Princess: Does it scream?","└ Wild Grylls: It does, but the screaming keeps cutting out instead of continuing steadily.","└ Starlight Princess: Then the mature mandrake really must have absorbed the Ice Blossom. I never expected this to happen.","└ Wild Grylls: What should I do now?","└ Starlight Princess: Surprisingly, this isn’t a bad situation. It means their energies have blended. Eating it raw would be dangerous, so I’ll tell you how to extract its essence.","└ Wild Grylls: Can’t I just send it to you as it is? You should be able to extract it right away.","└ Starlight Princess: That wouldn’t be a bad option either, but I’m worried the Ice Blossom’s effects might disappear if something goes wrong.","└ Passing Dwarf: Can’t you just make liquor out of it? Honestly, I think that’d be better.","└ Wild Grylls: Be honest. You only said that because you want it, right?","└ Passing Dwarf: Was it that obvious? If you have another one, give me one.","└ Wild Grylls: Good grief, lol. You’re so predictable.","I casually ignored the alcoholic dwarf’s suggestion and waited for the Starlight Princess to explain the method.","The combination of an Ice Blossom and a mature mandrake was practically a first for even her.","Both were herbs that money couldn’t buy, and I had combined them.","It was an idea—and a method—that only I, someone living in the Forest of the Four Seasons, could attempt.","’Putting mature mandrakes aside, Ice Blossoms must be extremely difficult to obtain.’","In truth, if this experiment failed, even I had no idea when I would be able to acquire another Ice Blossom.","Unlike mandrakes, they didn’t grow in colonies.","I prayed that it wouldn’t fail.","This might be my first and last opportunity.","└ Starlight Princess: (Image of a mandrake’s anatomy) As you can see in the picture, mandrakes resemble humans, so their vital points are similar too. You still have a syringe, right?","└ Wild Grylls: The one you gave me before?","└ Starlight Princess: Yes. Fill it with elixir and stick it straight into the mandrake’s mouth.","└ Wild Grylls: That sounds like torture.","└ Starlight Princess: Exactly. Force-feed it until its stomach is completely swollen.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood.","└ Poor mandrake.","└ Humanity is sorry.","└ He’s shoving it so deep that it can’t even scream, lololol.","└ Couldn’t he just crush it and turn it into juice? I seriously feel sorry for it, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: After that, put it in a mortar and grind it finely. That should extract a highly concentrated essence.","└ Wild Grylls: That’s an extremely primitive method.","└ Starlight Princess: There’s no other way. Do you need a mortar?","└ Wild Grylls: No. I can buy one from the auction house.","I knew nothing about the process, so I had no choice but to do as I was told.","Following the Starlight Princess’s instructions, I filled the syringe with elixir.","Then I jammed it into the blue mature mandrake’s mouth.","Shnk!","\"Kkueok?! Kkuuk! Kkueoooeok!\"","The instant I inserted the syringe, the mandrake thrashed around, trying to scream.","But since I was forcibly holding its mouth shut, its struggle was futile.","Still, perhaps because it looked human, it even flailed its arms and legs.","It went so far as to grab the needle with its hands, trying to pull the syringe out of its mouth.","Whack! Smack!","\"Kkuyolk?! Kkuup!\"","So I hit it a few times and told it to stay still.","It was troublesome, but this was part of the process of extracting its essence, so I endured it.","In the end, I injected all the elixir into the mature mandrake.","Its body remained blue, but it gradually began to glow.","It seemed to be absorbing the elixir’s energy.","\"Kkiyo...!\"","Whack!","\"Gguek! Kkiyoooo...!\"","Thwack! Smack!","\"Kueek! Kkiyoooot...!\"","\"Kkiyooooot! Kkiyoooo!!\"","\"Ah, come on.\"","Had this thing taken drugs instead of absorbing an Ice Blossom?","The moment I removed the syringe from its mouth, it began making a bizarre noise.","It wasn’t a mandrake’s characteristic scream.","Instead, it sounded like something that had gotten ridiculously high. Even punching it didn’t calm it down.","It was probably recovering in real time because I had injected it with elixir.","Even its face looked completely blissed out, making it react like a genuine drug addict.","Elixir was technically a \"medicine,\" so it seemed to have had a strange effect on the mandrake.","Whack! Smack! Thump!","\"Kueek! Keek! Kkueek!\"","So I hit it a few more times.","Thanks to that, the mandrake went limp like a corpse.","I had used half a bottle of elixir, so I prepared the mortar.","For hygiene’s sake, I didn’t forget to wash both the mortar and the mandrake with water.","’She told me to grind it finely and collect the juice, right?’","According to the Starlight Princess, the juice itself was the essence.","Incidentally, although I was only mentioning it now, her method prioritized safety.","Apparently, there was a more reliable method, but it would place a burden on my survival. That was why she had chosen the safer option.","I had absolutely no intention of risking my life just to gain strength, so I obediently followed her instructions.","Thud! Thump! Thud!","I finely pounded the mature mandrake inside the mortar.","It wasn’t a small bowl-shaped mortar, but a full-sized mortar traditionally used for pounding grain.","I had bought it so I could extract as much essence as possible.","’Is this enough?’","After being pounded for quite some time, the mature mandrake had been completely pulverized.","It was still blue.","I tilted the mortar slightly and poured the essence into the empty elixir bottle, which I had washed thoroughly.","Only a few drops came out, but I wasn’t finished yet.","Squeeze!","I grabbed the finely crushed mandrake with my hand and wrung it out with all my strength.","I applied the maximum grip strength I could muster, to the point that the veins stood out on the back of my hand.","Drip! Drip!","Juice trickled down.","After repeating the process several times, I managed to fill about half the bottle.","The elixir bottle was extremely small, so it couldn’t be called a large amount, but it was enough.","Shwaaaa—","Perhaps because the essence contained elixir as well, it wasn’t an ordinary shade of blue.","It was an incredibly beautiful color, a perfect blend of ice-white and blue.","It glowed like an elixir, making it look like a precious medicine at first glance.","└ Wild Grylls: (Photo of the glowing blue essence) I’ve extracted all of it. I can drink it now, right?","└ Starlight Princess: Yes. Still, just in case, I’ll give you another elixir. It contains plenty of yang essence, so it should be sufficient for emergencies.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you.","Now that I had even received an emergency elixir from the Starlight Princess, all that remained was to drink this.","I stared at the blue, glittering essence and took a deep breath.","Essence was a liquid containing powerful energy.","It would be easiest to think of it as an inner core in liquid form.","Therefore, I only needed to calmly control the energy while reciting the second mnemonic chant the Heavenly Demon had taught me.","’It should be fine. I even mixed in elixir to make it safer.’","Everything was difficult the first time.","I swallowed nervously, then drank all the essence in one gulp.","From my mouth down to my throat, I felt a coldness so intense that it stung.","On top of that, it was unbearably bitter.","The bitterness was so extreme that my entire face twisted.","It was so much stronger than the cold that I nearly failed to circulate the heart method.","’Th-The heavens become me... Wait, that’s not it.’","As if I had eaten ice cream too quickly, a sharp ache rang through my head as well.","The double blow of bitterness and brain freeze made my consciousness grow hazy, but I somehow managed to recite the chant.","There was no pain, but the sensations assaulting me were intense enough to rival it, making the process far from easy.","Even so, I kept trying.","Rather than losing consciousness and being overwhelmed by the energy, I worked to accept it.","As the Heavenly Demon had taught me, to control the energy of the heavens, I first needed to understand that energy.","I concentrated on sensing every strand of energy contained within the essence.","Whoosh!","The results of the safety-focused production method combined with my efforts gradually began to appear.","The essence started flowing along the same pathways through which my mana circulated according to the heart method.","If I continued circulating it steadily, it wouldn’t take long to absorb the entire essence.","Although the inside of my body felt as cold as if it contained a solid block of ice, it was bearable.","Whoooosh!","I had no idea how much time passed after that.","Eventually, I absorbed the essence completely.","I continued circulating the heart method for a little longer before slowly opening my eyes.","The tree sloth was there, staring blankly at me.","\"Phew...\"","The fact that I could see the tree sloth meant I was still alive.","I let out a long sigh.","As I exhaled, white breath escaped my mouth.","\"Did it... work?\"","Having absorbed all the essence, I examined every part of my body.","Nothing had visibly changed.","The same was true of the cold.","I still felt chilly.","It appeared that I hadn’t gained the cold resistance that had originally been my goal.","What a shame.","’There’s nothing I can do about it. Even the Starlight Princess wasn’t certain.’","That didn’t mean I could have disregarded safety.","To report the results, I made a post in the gallery.","Title: Results of the First Attempt","Wild Grylls","Nothing seems to have changed. I guess the energies were completely neutralized.","└ Starlight Princess: That’s unfortunate. I’m truly sorry that my knowledge was inadequate.","└ Wild Grylls: No, it’s all right. You didn’t do anything wrong, Princess. It would have been strange if we succeeded on the very first try, wouldn’t it?","└ Starlight Princess: Even if we set the Ice Blossom aside, I think I need to conduct more research on mature mandrakes. Could you give me the remains later?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. You gave me an elixir too, so I’ll send them to you.","└ Passing Dwarf: See? I told you making liquor would’ve been better.","└ Wild Grylls: Nonsense.","└ Starlight Princess: It isn’t entirely nonsense. Snake wine and ginseng wine are essentially ways of drinking extracted essence too.","└ Passing Dwarf: See that? Heh.","└ Wild Grylls: Even so, alcohol is a bit...;;","└ Passing Dwarf: Just give it a try. If you make some, I’ll give you something amazing.","└ Wild Grylls: If I can make it, lol.","I would need another Ice Blossom before I could even think about making it again.","I soothed my disappointment and checked the time.","I still had a little time left.","Building the ice storage house would take too long, but I seemed to have enough time to cut firewood for the night.","Fwoosh!","\"Hm?\"","I had just coated my axe in aura to make the logging easier when I noticed something strange.","My aura had originally been nearly colorless.","But not now.","It was a vivid blue—a frigid blue that looked cold enough to sting.","’No. It really is cold.’","Although it still flickered like flames, it gave off cold air instead of heat.","Curious, I placed my hand against the aura, but it didn’t harm me at all.","’Did it just make my aura cooler?’","What was this supposed to be, all style and no substance?","I chuckled.","What mattered right now was cutting wood.","Even if its color had changed, aura was still aura.","I swung the axe, putting my back into the blow.","Thunk!","The axe blade struck precisely into the center of the tree.","Crackle—crack, crack, crack!","Starting from the point of impact, the entire tree froze solid.","My jaw dropped at the unbelievable sight.","’Just what the hell did I drink?’","I couldn’t decide whether I should be pleased or worried.","In any case, one thing was certain.","’Th-This is freaking awesome...!’","I had unintentionally obtained an incredible ability.","An Ice Blossom, a mature mandrake, and finally, an elixir.","Every single ingredient was extraordinarily rare.","Perhaps such a result was only natural after mixing all three together.","’...What would happen if I combined this with a sword?’","A completely pointless thought suddenly crossed my mind.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 140","paragraphs":["Combination (3)","I purchased some water from the auction house to properly test the effects of my aura.","One might ask why I didn’t simply melt the ice stored in the box, but if my theory proved wrong, I would have to go out and cut more ice.","I didn’t want to go through that hassle, so I decided to buy water just this once.","I poured the water into a metal bucket and submerged my sword in it.","All I had to do was manifest my aura as before and wait to see what happened.","Crackle!","The moment I manifested my aura, the water began cooling at a tremendous rate.","But the water wasn’t the only thing freezing solid. Ice started spreading across the entire metal bucket.","At this rate, I would lose the whole bucket, so I hurriedly put it away.","Apparently, the effect only applied to the area in contact with my aura, because the ice didn’t trap the sword.","’Can’t I control this?’","Freezing water was all well and good. I had obtained an incredible ability, after all.","But if I couldn’t control it, it would become a poison rather than a blessing.","I didn’t know whether my mana itself had changed, but this clearly required a thorough investigation.","’At least it seems like I can control the intensity by adjusting the amount of aura...’","Through experimentation, I discovered that I could regulate its strength by changing the amount of aura.","However, I had no idea how to turn the cold attribute on and off.","I didn’t even know whether this change was permanent or would eventually disappear.","After thinking it over repeatedly, I finally decided to ask the gallery.","Title: Let It Come...","Wild Grylls","(Video of a bucket of water freezing after an aura-coated sword is submerged in it)","My sword hungers.","Just kidding. Does anyone know why this is happening?","I froze an entire tree while logging, so I tested it and found out that my aura has gained a cold attribute.","I can’t turn it on or off at will, either. Anyone know how?","└ Heavenly Demon: What beautifully colored sword energy. It even sparkles. It is more beautiful than what those fellows from the North Sea use.","└ Wild Grylls: Do the people of the North Sea control cold energy?","└ Heavenly Demon: Most of them do. However, they control cold energy through martial arts. You know no martial art for controlling cold energy, do you?","└ Wild Grylls: No. I only know the mnemonic chants you taught me.","└ Heavenly Demon: How fascinating. Perhaps your internal energy itself has taken on the properties of cold.","└ SwordMaster: I agree with the Heavenly Demon. Elemental aura isn’t entirely unheard of, but it usually requires the user to master a special heart method. In your case, Mr. Grylls, it seems as though your mana itself has taken on the properties of cold.","└ Wild Grylls: Is there no way to turn it on and off?","└ Heavenly Demon: I do not know. As I said, even the North Sea Ice Palace produces cold energy through its martial arts.","└ SwordMaster: This is my first time seeing anything like it, so I don’t know either. I’ve seen people control fire and lightning, but I’ve never encountered mana that was itself elemental.","└ With performance like that, doesn’t he basically not need an ice storage house or anything else anymore?","└ For real. He wanted a refrigerator so badly that he became one himself, lol.","└ Why does this guy always get stronger in such bizarre ways?;;","└ The fact that he keeps getting stronger through such novel methods is ridiculous, lolol.","└ Starlight Princess: As the others said, it seems the essence blended with your mana and gave it the properties of cold. I never anticipated this either.","└ Wild Grylls: It isn’t necessarily a bad thing, is it?","└ Starlight Princess: If your body had been unable to withstand the cold, your mana would have frozen first. In the worst case, you could develop something similar to the Severed Meridian Syndrome I suffer from, so you should prepare for that possibility in advance.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll keep that in mind.","└ All-Father: There have been a few recorded cases of mana acquiring the properties of a particular element later in life. They were mentioned in ancient texts.","└ Wild Grylls: Did those people undergo a process like mine?","└ All-Father: No. In most cases, the elemental essence was injected directly into their mana circuits. The results were not particularly favorable.","└ Wild Grylls: What do you mean, \"not particularly favorable\"?","└ All-Father: Those injected with cold essence had their organs freeze solid, as though they had contracted Severed Meridian Syndrome. Those injected with fire essence were unable to withstand the heat, and their mana circuits quickly melted.","└ Wild Grylls: Sh-Sh-Shiver me timbers...","└ All-Father: Just in case, it would be wise to obtain mature mandrake essence, as the Starlight Princess suggested.","└ Wild Grylls: Why didn’t you warn me about this before?","└ All-Father: Because you used an elixir alongside it. An elixir is hardly some common potion. It healed your body until it could absorb and adapt to the essence, making it an ideal safeguard. The cases I mentioned involved injecting pure essence alone.","So this ability wasn’t something I could celebrate unreservedly.","I had only been able to absorb it thanks to the mnemonic chant the Heavenly Demon had taught me. Without that, it could have been extremely dangerous.","Only time would tell, but side effects might appear later, so I needed to be prepared.","└ PraiseTheSun: With just one of those, you’d never have to worry about ice again. Can you give me one? I bet selling ice would be sweet.","└ Wild Grylls: Sorry, but I made this with the only Ice Blossom I had. Besides, I have no idea what side effects it might cause.","└ PraiseTheSun: I’m not going to eat it myself anyway, so I don’t care about the side effects. It’s a shame you don’t have another Ice Blossom.","└ Wild Grylls: Just who were you planning to feed it to?","└ PraiseTheSun: I have someone in mind. If you find another one later, would you be willing to trade?","└ Wild Grylls: Let’s talk after I find one. I still haven’t obtained the ability I wanted.","I might have gained the cold attribute, but I hadn’t acquired resistance to the cold.","Moreover, it could easily become an awkward, practically useless ability if I wasn’t careful, so training was essential.","Too much of anything was never good.","’But can I use this with my bare hands?’","Would the cold manifest if I channeled aura into my hand rather than a sword?","Curious, I shattered the ice inside the metal bucket with a hammer and filled it with water again.","Then I submerged my hand in the water.","Crackle!","As expected, the water froze solid.","It seemed I could use the ability perfectly well with my bare hands.","’This could come in handy when I don’t have a weapon.’","I was the type who relied heavily on weapons. I knew almost nothing about unarmed combat.","This ability might help me overcome a worst-case scenario.","Of course, as I had repeatedly mentioned, there was no telling what danger it might cause if I couldn’t properly control it.","’For the time being, I should focus on controlling it.’","Between practicing swordsmanship, circulating my heart method, and training this ability, I had a lot to do.","Was this why people said it was better to focus on mastering one discipline?","I thought it would be best to train the cold only until I could control it properly.","’It’s not like I’m planning to unleash an Ice Age.’","Even in a fantasy world, something on that scale should be impossible.","Well, there were people who could casually slice through mountains with their swords, but I was an exception.","After cleaning up, I resumed logging.","I couldn’t use my sword energy because of the cold attribute, so I had no choice but to do it with brute strength.","Still, my body had become sturdy enough that I could gather the wood without much difficulty.","’It’s about time for dinner.’","Was it because it was winter?","The sun seemed to set unusually early.","As far as I knew, the time of sunset was influenced by revolution rather than rotation.","If the sun truly was setting earlier, it meant the change was occurring on a planetary scale, not merely within this region.","’I’ve heard of the midnight sun, where daylight lasts all day.’","I wasn’t sure.","Since this was the Forest of the Four Seasons, I had no choice but to accept it and move on.","Afterward, I ate smoked tiger meat and warmed myself by adding more firewood to the fireplace.","Even after everything that had happened, our adorable Wonmo was still sleeping.","It seemed that once winter arrived, he spent all his time asleep to conserve energy.","’Well, he’s still a cub...’","The other animals had become less active anyway.","The only dangers I had encountered so far were the blizzard and avalanche.","Besides, while I had lacked experience, both of those disasters were things I could prepare for.","’I absolutely need an emergency exit... I should probably build it like the chimney.’","Considering the force of an avalanche, it would definitely need to be built from bricks.","The chimney had remained intact even when the avalanche struck. At the very least, it wouldn’t be swept away.","Still, some damage would be unavoidable, so I would have to inspect it periodically.","’What’s better than mud...? Cement, I suppose.’","Did cement exist in this world?","Or was there something different that served the same purpose?","Even on Earth, many ancient structures had remained standing for countless years.","Fortress walls in particular were so sturdy that they could barely be demolished even with cannon fire.","Despite the technological limitations of their era, people in ancient times built civilizations by using every resource available to them.","The same applied to me.","I would use everything at my disposal and survive until the very end.","’I should ask the dwarf... No, I should ask the entire gallery. This might not be his field of expertise.’","The dwarf mentioned that often. If something fell outside his field, even he wouldn’t know about it.","He had personally researched the things he had taught me so far.","Title: Anyone Know How to Bind Bricks More Firmly?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the chimney)","So far, I’ve just been slathering mud between the bricks to hold them in place. Does anyone know a better method?","I’m asking because I want to build it more sturdily if it collapses later. Mud seems like it has its limits.","└ Starlight Princess: From what I’ve heard, castles were built using a paste made by mixing lime and sand.","└ Passing Dwarf: Yeah, the verified user above is right. More precisely, there’s something called cement. Mix that with sand.","└ Wild Grylls: Cement? The same cement I know?","My eyes widened.","Cement existed in this world too?","I hadn’t used the word because I assumed it wouldn’t exist here, yet the dwarf brought it up immediately.","Even if the substance was the same, I had never imagined it would have the same name.","└ Wild Grylls: I never imagined it would exist here;; When was cement invented?","└ Passing Dwarf: Dunno. It’s been around for freaking ages. One thing’s for sure, though: we invented cement.","└ Wild Grylls: You’re not lying, are you?","└ Passing Dwarf: Wanna bet?","└ All-Father: He is not lying. It is said that the discovery of cement was one reason dwarven technology advanced so rapidly. Of the three necessities—food, clothing, and shelter—it made their shelters considerably sturdier.","└ Passing Dwarf: Ah, why’d you tell him? I could’ve squeezed something out of him.","└ Wild Grylls: You would’ve only asked me for alcohol anyway, lol.","└ All-Father: However, there are some suspicious aspects to its history. It was considered far beyond the technology of its era, so scholars debated the matter extensively. That is why I called it a discovery rather than an invention.","└ Wild Grylls: Are you saying it simply appeared out of nowhere?","└ All-Father: Yes. If you think about it, the gift I gave you is a similar case. It cannot be manufactured even with modern technology.","└ Passing Dwarf: What kind of cement are you thinking of?","└ Wild Grylls: Something you mix with other stuff and slather on. Then it hardens over time.","└ Passing Dwarf: You know exactly what it is. You’re loaded, so why haven’t you been using it all this time?","The gift All-Father had given me was the subspace backpack.","Although it couldn’t ignore mass, it completely disregarded spatial limitations.","It was an excellent tool that allowed me to save an enormous amount of space.","└ All-Father: Scholars hypothesize that an ancient artifact happened to survive in storage.","└ Wild Grylls: An ancient artifact?","└ All-Father: Yes. It dates back to the age when the gods still descended upon the mortal world—a civilization beyond the reach of even modern humanity.","Was he talking about the sort of ancient civilization commonly found in novels and comics?","Something like lost technology?","A civilization that had disappeared for some unknown reason, leaving only traces behind.","Earth had similar cases, so I wasn’t surprised that the same thing had happened in this world.","One needed to look no further than ancient Egypt. We still had no idea exactly how they had built the pyramids.","’Although once you’ve served in the military, you start believing humans really could have built them.’","Anyway, I set that aside and returned to the main topic.","Now that I knew cement existed, all I needed was the proper method.","The dwarf seemed to know the basics and explained them to me.","└ Passing Dwarf: If you’re spreading it between bricks, mix it with sand, not soil.","└ Wild Grylls: Why?","└ Passing Dwarf: Dunno. My father told me to do it that way.","└ Wild Grylls: Okay, lol.","└ For some reason, that sounds strangely trustworthy, lolol.","└ Isn’t that exactly the same as doing whatever your academy professor tells you?","└ Yep. Undergraduates just do what their professors tell them. Nobody knows the underlying principles, lol.","’Do I need to go downstream or to the sea?’","Everything around here was soil rather than sand.","I would only find sand downstream or at the seashore.","Even though it was winter, I wanted to avoid the sea if possible.","Going downstream would be much better.","I wasn’t going to build it immediately. I merely intended to start gathering the materials now.","’They don’t sell sand at the auction house.’","After briefly checking the auction house, I left another comment for the dwarf.","Putting cement aside, there was something else I wanted to ask him.","└ Wild Grylls: Hey. Are there weapons imbued with elemental properties?","└ Passing Dwarf: Yeah, they exist. Hammers with the lightning attribute, swords that blaze with fire, things like that. Why?","└ Wild Grylls: How are they normally created? Does it happen naturally?","└ Passing Dwarf: Usually, I guess? The Lightning Hammer gained its power after being struck by a bolt from the sky. Its original owner got struck too and died, though, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: What about the fire weapon? Did its owner burn to death?","└ Passing Dwarf: Nope. I heard it was a sword found embedded in the middle of a volcanic crater. Why are you asking?","└ Wild Grylls: I was wondering whether one could be made artificially. For example, by adding the essence I drank to a sword while it’s being forged.","└ Passing Dwarf: There you go talking nonsense again, lol. Find another Ice-Whatever-Blossom first, then we’ll talk.","└ A cold-attributed sword would be freaking awesome, though, lolol.","└ But even if you made one, it’s not like you’d sell it.","└ Wild Grylls: It’d just be for decoration, lol.","\"Oh. There’s another one?\"","While gathering wood, I discovered another Ice Blossom.","\"There’s one here, and another one over there... Why are there so many?\"","There wasn’t merely one. There were several.","I could find them simply by searching carefully between the trees.","’Are they like seasonal produce?’","What were they, wild spring greens?","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 141","paragraphs":["Combination (4)","The Ice Blossom was an herb found only in cold regions—and even there, it was exceedingly rare.","Moreover, it tended to melt as soon as the temperature rose even slightly, and it remained in bloom for only a short time.","It could grow only during the limited season of winter, had a short lifespan, and possessed the durability of an ocean sunfish.","Most importantly, it required land abundant in mana.","All those conditions combined to make it an exceptionally rare herb.","As always, however, the Forest of the Four Seasons seemed to be an exception.","There was no need to explain how much mana existed here.","The seasons changed every week, so its short lifespan wasn’t a problem either.","If I searched around the shelter, I could find Ice Blossoms with relative ease.","Therefore, to me, Ice Blossoms were nothing more than seasonal flowers.","Flowers that came into season once every four weeks, at that.","Title: Found More Ice Blossoms","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an Ice Blossom)","(Photo of Ice Blossom 2)","(Photo of Ice Blossom 3)","Are these like seasonal wild greens or something? There are quite a lot of them.","└ Heavenly Demon: You must be the only person who would describe such a precious medicinal herb as seasonal wild greens.","└ SwordMaster: All kinds of supposedly rare herbs seem to be gathered there. Those really are incredibly valuable.","└ Does this mean he’ll be able to find Ice Blossoms every winter from now on?","└ Seems like it. Wouldn’t the same apply to other herbs? Different herbs grow in different seasons.","└ What herbs grow in spring again? All sorts of medicinal herbs grow between spring and summer.","└ For real? At this point, anything he picks up will probably be considered medicinal, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: You found several rather than just one! Are","The Ice Blossom was a medicinal herb found only in cold regions—and even there, it was extremely rare.","Moreover, it would often melt away if the temperature rose even slightly, and its blooming period was short.","A single limited season called winter, a short lifespan, and the durability of a sunfish.","Above all, it could only grow in soil with an abundance of mana.","All these conditions combined to make it an extraordinarily rare medicinal herb.","But as always, the Forest of the Four Seasons appeared to be an exception.","There was no need to explain how plentiful the mana was here.","The seasons changed every week, so its short lifespan wasn’t a problem either.","I could easily find Ice Blossoms simply by searching around the shelter.","Therefore, as far as I was concerned, the Ice Blossom was nothing more than a seasonal flower.","One that came into season once every four weeks.","Title: Found More Ice Blossoms","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an Ice Blossom)","(Photo of Ice Blossom 2)","(Photo of Ice Blossom 3)","Are these like seasonal herbs or something? There are quite a lot of them.","└ Heavenly Demon: You must be the only person who would describe a precious medicinal herb as seasonal greens.","└ SwordMaster: It’s like every supposedly rare herb has gathered there. Those are genuinely precious.","└ So does this mean he’ll be able to find Ice Blossoms every winter from now on?","└ Seems like it. Wouldn’t the same apply to other herbs? Different medicinal herbs grow in different seasons.","└ What medicinal herbs grow in spring again? All kinds of them grow from spring through summer.","└ For real? But anything he picks up will probably be considered a medicinal herb, lol.","└ Starlight Princess: You found several, not just one! Are you going to use those to make more essence?","└ Wild Grylls: I’d like to gain cold resistance. I have plenty of ingredients now, so I think it should be fine.","└ Starlight Princess: All right. But could you give me the mature mandrake you mentioned yesterday?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll give you a mature mandrake and make another blue mandrake using yesterday’s method. That should make your research easier.","└ Starlight Princess: I’ll be sure to repay your trust!","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you.","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey, what about me? Give me one too.","└ Wild Grylls: You reek of alcohol, so go away. Besides, I don’t have enough to spare for making liquor. I’ll consider it once I obtain the ability I want.","└ Passing Dwarf: Okay, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: If necessary, I’ll make the liquor myself, lol.","└ Passing Dwarf: You little bastard!","└ Don’t worry. There are probably plenty of other medicinal herbs besides those, lolol.","└ What if he finds Sun Herbs in summer?","└ Sun Herbs only grow in deserts. It’s like how Snow Ginseng only grows on snowy mountains.","└ By that logic, shouldn’t Ice Blossoms only grow on snowy mountains too?","└ He’ll find something. We just need to sit back and watch, lol.","Now that I had found more Ice Blossoms, I ate a light breakfast and began the production process.","The first thing I needed to do was gather mandrakes.","This time, I collected several rather than just one.","I gave one of them to the Starlight Princess and processed another using the same method as yesterday.","I started by boiling the mature mandrake together with an Ice Blossom, dyeing it blue.","\"Kkuyolk?! Kkueok!!\"","Once again, I forcibly poured elixir into its mouth.","It suddenly reminded me of foie gras, the dish made from goose liver.","Apparently, they force-feed geese by inserting funnels into their beaks to enlarge their livers.","A mandrake was a plant, so it wasn’t quite as bad, but its reactions still made the process unpleasant.","Although in my case, I was forcing medicine—elixir—into it rather than food.","\"Kkiyoooooot!!\"","Whack! Smack!","The moment the elixir took effect, I beat the thrashing mandrake until it calmed down.","’Now I just need to send these.’","I sent her three mandrakes in total.","One was an ordinary mandrake, another was a mandrake combined with an Ice Blossom, and the last was a mandrake that had absorbed both an Ice Blossom and an elixir.","If she researched them one by one, the Starlight Princess should be able to figure something out.","I would have liked to give All-Father some samples and ask him to conduct research too, but I didn’t have enough.","[Starlight Princess: Thank you. I’ll send you my findings by lunchtime.]","[Wild Grylls: Understood. Is the mandrake combined with the Ice Blossom still intact?]","[Starlight Princess: Perhaps because the Ice Blossom was absorbed into the mandrake, it’s still blue. If I’d known this would happen, I would’ve asked you to send it yesterday.]","[Wild Grylls: Neither of us knew. I’ll wait for your findings, then.]","Now that I had entrusted the research to the Starlight Princess, I needed to attend to my own work.","My first priority was controlling the ability.","As I had repeatedly emphasized, it would cause all sorts of trouble if I couldn’t control it.","I used aura not only in combat but also for various kinds of labor.","Logging, mining, digging, processing materials, and so on.","It was useful in countless ways.","But if everything became covered in frost—or froze solid—whenever I used it, that would be an enormous headache.","’Let’s determine why my mana is giving off cold. Has the mana itself really changed?’","I quietly closed my eyes and circulated my heart method.","I could clearly feel the mana inside me flowing through every corner of my body.","At the same time, I felt an intensely frigid sensation.","The mana itself had taken on the properties of cold.","However, contrary to the Starlight Princess’s fears, my circuits hadn’t frozen solid as they would with Severed Meridian Syndrome.","As though my body had completely adapted, the mana circulated easily without placing any strain on me.","’How should I put it...?’","Was it similar to how the waters of the Arctic and Antarctic didn’t freeze easily?","I didn’t mean that my mana contained salt.","I was merely speculating that the essence I had consumed yesterday had caused a similar phenomenon.","It wasn’t a bad thing, but I had only avoided the worst-case scenario. The ability remained troublesome.","’It would be perfect if it just had an on-and-off switch.’","How could I separate the cold energy from my aura?","As I pondered the problem, a thought suddenly occurred to me.","’Wait. All my mana gathers in my dantian, doesn’t it?’","An internal energy heart method accumulated mana within the dantian through breathing.","In other words, even if mana spread throughout my entire body, it would eventually return to the dantian.","Then what if I separated the cold energy every time the mana returned and stored it independently?","’My dantian won’t freeze solid, will it?’","That possibility was frightening too.","I stopped circulating the heart method for a moment.","This was when I needed an expert’s opinion.","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, may I ask you a question?]","[Heavenly Demon: What do you wish to know?]","[Wild Grylls: Well, the thing is...]","I gave the Heavenly Demon a general explanation.","I wanted to separate the cold energy from my mana and store it inside my dantian.","However, I was worried that the cold energy might adversely affect my dantian.","I asked her to tell me whether my concern was baseless or if there was a genuine risk.","The Heavenly Demon seemed to contemplate my question for some time before replying.","[Heavenly Demon: I understand what you mean. Your concern is not unreasonable.]","[Wild Grylls: Is it dangerous?]","[Heavenly Demon: It would be dangerous if you separated them incorrectly. As you fear, your dantian could freeze solid. However, if you use the proper method, you should be able to separate them safely.]","[Wild Grylls: Could you teach me how?]","[Heavenly Demon: Of course. The principle is to create another dantian within your dantian.]","[Wild Grylls: That sounds incredibly difficult.]","[Heavenly Demon: It is nothing extraordinary. If your existing dantian is meant for pure energy, the new dantian you create will be exclusively for cold energy. Wait a moment.]","After leaving that message, the Heavenly Demon disappeared for a while.","I tilted my head, unable to understand what she meant by creating a dantian inside my dantian.","I didn’t doubt her, since she was the expert in this field.","I simply couldn’t grasp the concept.","’Maybe I’ll have to perform manual labor without aura for a while.’","This strange ability was making my body suffer.","I could only laugh hollowly.","I had no idea how long I waited, but after a while, the Heavenly Demon sent me another message.","[Heavenly Demon: (Image depicting the human body and an inner core) Can you see it clearly? You should notice a small circle inside this inner core. You must gather the essence into a mass and create another inner core in this manner.]","[Wild Grylls: Ah. So it’s like a mathematical set.]","[Heavenly Demon: Is \"set\" not simply a word used when things are gathered together?]","[Wild Grylls: It’s also a mathematical term. It isn’t used very often.]","[Heavenly Demon: I see. In any case, it is enough that you understand. Now that you know the principle, you should practice.]","[Wild Grylls: Don’t you have any other advice?]","[Heavenly Demon: The second mnemonic chant I taught you will be of great assistance. I would like to teach you the third chant, but I fear it may cause you to grow stronger in yet another bizarre direction, so it would be best to postpone it. That is especially true now that your energy has acquired the properties of cold.]","[Wild Grylls: Understood. Thank you very much, even if it’s only advice.]","[Heavenly Demon: This lady shall always be waiting. If you require assistance, you need only ask.]","No matter how I looked at it, the Heavenly Demon was a precious connection.","She had given me invaluable advice without the slightest hesitation.","The Heavenly Demon added that it would be better for me to learn the third mnemonic chant only after I could easily control both my cold energy and aura.","Ideally, I should wait until I could use sword force—in other words, an Aura Blade.","I agreed with her.","’If I become stronger in some stupid-ass way again, I’ll be the one who suffers.’","As someone had joked, my aura might end up piercing the heavens.","Praying that nothing like that would happen, I resumed circulating my internal energy heart method.","I recited the second mnemonic chant the Heavenly Demon had taught me and visualized the image she had shown me, separating my mana from the cold energy.","Shwaaaaa—","The cold energy gradually separated as though undergoing a chemical reaction.","Following the Heavenly Demon’s instructions, I positioned that energy in the center of my inner core.","As if creating another circle within an existing circle, I slowly forced the energy together into a compact mass.","Crackle—","Perhaps because the principle resembled that of an Aura Blade, it wasn’t easy.","Whenever I finally managed to gather the energy, it would often crumble apart.","Moreover, the circulating mana flowed as rapidly as crashing waves, making even the separation process difficult.","’I can’t give up.’","An Aura Blade manifested outside the body, whereas this process took place inside me.","Relatively speaking, this should be easier.","I refused to become discouraged and continued separating the two energies.","I had no idea how much time passed.","Eventually, my efforts bore fruit.","Shortly before lunchtime, I managed to form an essence core the size of a grain of millet.","’Now, if I want to use the cold energy...’","When I touched it as though popping a balloon, the essence core immediately burst.","Reforming it wasn’t difficult either.","After all, I had already traveled that path once.","If I gradually increased its size, I would eventually be able to use ordinary aura in daily life again.","Until then, I would have to avoid using aura while working whenever possible.","’I’ll just think of it as exercise.’","I checked the time.","Before I knew it, hours had passed and it was already lunchtime.","At that exact moment, the Starlight Princess sent me a message.","Her timing was impeccable.","She had promised to share her research findings by lunchtime, so this was right on schedule.","[Wild Grylls: What did you find?]","[Starlight Princess: I have good news and bad news. Which would you like to hear first?]","[Wild Grylls: Please tell me the bad news first.]","[Starlight Princess: It seems practically impossible to gain cold resistance using an Ice Blossom. It might be possible if we disregarded safety, but no matter how hard I thought about it, every method carried significant risks.]","To acquire cold resistance, I would have to consume an Ice Blossom despite the danger.","I was disappointed for a moment, but then a question occurred to me.","’Then what about the people who gained cold resistance in the past? Were they simply lucky?’","The moment the thought occurred to me, I asked her.","[Wild Grylls: What about the people from the past? You said some died after eating Ice Blossoms, but others gained cold resistance.]","[Starlight Princess: Do you remember the pufferfish you mentioned before? This is a completely different situation.]","[Wild Grylls: A different situation?]","[Starlight Princess: Yes. With pufferfish, people generally discovered which parts were safe to eat after countless attempts. But Ice Blossoms are different. Those people simply ate them.]","[Wild Grylls: They just ate them? Then how did they survive?]","The Starlight Princess gave me an intuitive explanation of the difference.","[Starlight Princess: To use the pufferfish analogy, it was eaten by people who could chew up an entire raw pufferfish and remain perfectly fine. In other words, the people who ate Ice Blossoms were simply exceptionally strong.]","[Wild Grylls: ;;;;]","So only natural-born powerhouses could eat them.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 142","paragraphs":["Combination (5)","I was dumbfounded to hear that only naturally born powerhouses could gain cold resistance, but it was still too early to give up.","What the Starlight Princess had just told me was the bad news.","There was still good news left.","I sincerely hoped it would give me some hope.","[Wild Grylls: What’s the good news?]","[Starlight Princess: There’s no risk of you developing Severed Meridian Syndrome. The ability is permanent too. And one more thing—you probably won’t ever freeze to death.]","[Wild Grylls: Didn’t you say I hadn’t gained cold resistance?]","[Starlight Princess: This is separate from that. If you progress beyond hypothermia and reach the point where you’re about to freeze to death, your body will react. You’ll probably enter hibernation on your own, then revive once the weather becomes warmer.]","[Wild Grylls: Wonmo is hibernating right now. Does it work on the same principle?]","[Starlight Princess: It’s slightly different. In your case, how should I put this...? The ability is focused entirely on survival. Ordinarily, you would die from hypothermia, but instead, you’ll continue surviving.]","[Wild Grylls: I should consider that... a good thing, right?]","[Starlight Princess: It’s better than having nothing, isn’t it? But be careful. If you collapse somewhere the weather or seasons never change, such as a snowy mountain, you could remain alive but asleep forever.]","That would be a hopeless situation.","I wouldn’t be alive or dead.","Still, as the Starlight Princess had said, it was an extremely useful survival ability.","For someone like me, who always had to consider the worst-case scenario, it couldn’t have been more suitable.","It was disappointing that I hadn’t gained cold resistance, but I was grateful nonetheless.","[Wild Grylls: What would have happened if I’d eaten the blue mandrake?]","[Starlight Princess: You most likely would’ve become an ice human. Like that mandrake, your skin would’ve turned blue rather than merely pale, and your hair would’ve turned white. You would’ve looked no different from an undead.]","[Wild Grylls: Sh-Sh-Shiver me timbers. Good thing I added the elixir.]","[Starlight Princess: I gave you the safest method available, after all.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you so much for teaching me.]","[Starlight Princess: It’s all right. My knowledge increased thanks to you too. If there’s anything else you’re curious about, you can ask me anytime.]","[Wild Grylls: What does ordinary mandrake essence do?]","[Starlight Princess: Since it contains yang energy, it warms the body. In particular, it increases the body’s regenerative abilities, making it an ideal ingredient for elixirs.]","[Wild Grylls: Then can liquor be made using the blue mandrake?]","[Starlight Princess: It wouldn’t be impossible... but the liquor would probably freeze first. It would also be dangerous.]","[Wild Grylls: Understood.]","Since the subject had come up, the Starlight Princess gifted me some elixirs.","Two of them, no less.","I thanked her and began cleaning up.","\"Now that I’ve more or less finished here...\"","It was time to handle the remaining work.","Building an ice storage house had become pointless, so I started designing improvements to the shelter instead.","I wanted to make it sturdy enough to withstand any natural disaster.","Of course, that wouldn’t be easy.","A disaster even worse than the avalanche might strike in the future.","’Should I reinforce the drainage channel with cement too?’","Now that I knew cement existed, I could think of all kinds of places to use it.","However, I had never worked in construction.","I had only used cement a few times during my military service.","Even then, the officers had handled most of the actual application. I had merely assisted them.","’Come to think of it, I did all sorts of things in the military.’","I chuckled as I searched through the auction house for cement.","Since cement was commonly used in various fields—particularly construction—quite a large amount had been listed.","After assuming cement didn’t exist at all, discovering so much of it felt strangely anticlimactic.","If I had learned about it just a little sooner—or had at least tried searching for it—my oven and furnace might never have been swept away.","’I need to erect another barricade too... I have a lot to do.’","The avalanche had swept away an enormous amount.","The situation made me sigh.","Whatever else I did, I definitely needed a barricade. The difference between having one and not having one was immense.","Even during the saber-toothed tiger attack, the barricade had bought me valuable time.","’I should ask the dwarf to make it. Although I can’t give him any liquor.’","The Starlight Princess had warned that the liquor could be dangerous, so I intended to postpone that idea.","After designing the shelter’s reinforcements, I immediately prepared my equipment.","I needed to gather sand to mix with the cement.","If I remembered correctly, there was sand downstream.","\"Fast Sloth, look after Wonmo.\"","\"...\"","I left Fast Sloth at the shelter to watch over the hibernating Wonmo.","Perhaps he didn’t want to move either, because he was simply zoning out in front of the fireplace.","It seemed neither humans nor animals wanted to go outside in cold weather.","For me, however, this was an excellent opportunity.","Considering that Wonmo had fallen asleep, other animals were probably less active or hibernating too.","Even the snakes that had always appeared at the worst possible moments to irritate me should pose less of a threat.","’I need a shovel and some sacks. The ground might be frozen, so I should take the ignition stone and firewood too.’","How wonderful it was that I could fit all of this into the subspace backpack.","Even the weight wasn’t much of an issue. Since everything took up so little space, it felt considerably lighter to carry.","After checking several times to ensure I hadn’t forgotten anything, I headed for the river.","’It feels like it’s been a long time since I went downstream.’","I followed the frozen river downstream.","Since I was already heading in that direction, it might not be a bad idea to continue to the lake and gather some food.","It wasn’t that I disliked smoked food.","The problem was Fast Sloth’s food supply.","’It’s becoming dangerous to keep feeding him nothing but inner cores.’","He ate inner cores at every meal, so my supply was steadily dwindling.","The sudden arrival of winter had prevented me from storing food that Fast Sloth could eat.","Fortunately, I had accumulated a considerable stockpile beforehand. Otherwise, I would have run out already.","’And I have no idea when the Heavenly Demon will give me more fasting pills.’","On top of that, the gorillas kept stealing every fasting pill she sent.","I would have to endure somehow until the Heavenly Demon gave me more.","’The sand is... Wow. It’s frozen solid.’","When I reached the lower reaches of the river, I discovered that even the sand had frozen.","That was unavoidable, considering it was constantly exposed to the water.","With no other option, I took out the firewood I had prepared in advance.","I only needed to keep a fire burning until the sand thawed.","Crackle! Pop!","The warm campfire, which I had lit to melt the sand, made me feel pleasantly drowsy.","I stared idly into the flames for a while before a thought suddenly occurred to me.","’Wait. Couldn’t I just break it apart with a pickaxe and thaw it later?’","Now that I thought about it, that would be a much better method.","I was going to mix it with cement anyway, so there was no need to thaw it first.","I could simply mix it with heated water later.","People said human intelligence often kicked in too late.","I was the perfect example.","’Sigh. Let’s just consider this a learning experience.’","Grumbling inwardly, I checked the sand.","It was still hard.","I could probably make a quick trip to the lake while I waited for it to thaw.","Still, I remained alert to my surroundings just in case.","There was no telling what might appear.","’I don’t see anything in particular.’","There were no giant crabs in sight, while the ordinary crabs were frozen solid.","If anyone asked whether they were still edible, I would simply call it natural frozen storage.","I placed several crabs in a sack and looked around.","The entire lake had frozen over, forming what looked like a vast road.","’I suppose I could scout the area if necessary...’","There was no reason to take an unnecessary risk.","I collected the crabs and returned downstream.","The moment I arrived, I encountered an extraordinary sight.","\"Prrr.\"","\"...\"","It was a deer.","A deer was resting beside the campfire I had built.","Could it be the same deer that had knocked out the bull shark with a single kick?","I silently stared at the deer before slowly beginning to move.","That kick could have been aimed at me if I made a wrong move, so I needed to be careful.","’What is it, some kind of gangster?’","I never imagined it would take over my campfire while I was briefly away.","Even its appearance gave off the distinct aura of a thug. If I messed with it, I would probably regret it.","However, I needed the sand.","To show that I meant it no harm, I approached slowly.","Even when I came closer, the deer merely sat beside the campfire and did nothing.","Scrape! Scrape!","It didn’t react even when I began digging up the sand with my shovel.","I couldn’t tell whether the warmth of the campfire made it unwilling to move or if it had realized I wasn’t a threat.","’Is this the composure of the strong?’","Herbivores were unusually powerful in this forest.","Sloths, gorillas, and now deer.","If carnivores were predators, then these creatures were simply gangsters.","’I’ve collected about enough sand...’","Just how long was this thing planning to stay here?","It was staring straight through me too, which made me extremely uncomfortable.","Still, it hadn’t attacked me, so everything was probably fine.","I had already accomplished my objective.","Clatter! Crackle!","Before leaving, I added a few more pieces of firewood.","It was my way of signaling that I had absolutely no intention of fighting it.","The campfire grew stronger.","Perhaps the deer understood what I meant, because although it had been watching me the entire time, it finally turned its head away.","’This should be enough, right?’","I threw the remaining firewood onto the campfire and returned to the shelter.","The deer showed no intention of leaving the fire until the very end.","Despite that minor incident, I managed to return with what I needed.","’I’ll leave the sand in the sacks and put the crabs in the icebox.’","The \"icebox\" was simply the insulated box containing the ice.","I had decided to call it that for convenience.","The moment I stepped inside the shelter, however, I noticed something strange.","Fast Sloth was still staring idly into the fire, and Wonmo was still hibernating.","Then who was the creature sitting beside Fast Sloth?","’What? I’m sure I put up the metal fence and the tarp.’","There were no signs that either the tarp or the fence had been disturbed.","That meant it had entered through another route.","However, considering that Fast Sloth wasn’t on guard, it probably wasn’t dangerous.","Still, I couldn’t afford to let my guard down.","I slowly approached and checked its identity.","\"Keeeng...\"","\"...\"","Once I came closer, I recognized it.","It was a familiar creature.","This was the raccoon that had approached me when I lit a campfire in the yard before.","The raccoon that had stuck its hand into the fire, then put the flames clinging to its hand into its mouth.","’Why is this thing here?’","I stared at the raccoon in confusion.","Then I noticed wounds on its legs and back.","There were no signs that it had entered through the entrance, so it couldn’t have arrived here while fleeing from a predator.","\"Hey. Where did you come from?\"","\"Keeeng...?\"","Unable to figure it out, I quietly approached and asked.","The raccoon looked puzzled when I came closer, then slowly rose from its seat.","I briefly wondered whether it intended to fight me, but it did something completely unexpected.","\"Keeeng... Keng...\"","It clasped its hands neatly together with a truly apologetic expression.","Anyone could tell that it was apologizing.","Its already adorable appearance, combined with that gesture, naturally stirred my sympathy.","It was far more polite and well-behaved than a certain bunch of gorilla bastards.","\"Keng... Keeeng...\"","The raccoon then pointed toward the fireplace, still wearing an extremely aggrieved expression.","Thanks to that, I could roughly understand what had happened.","Apparently, it had crawled into the chimney and fallen straight down.","It was a miracle that it had only suffered scrapes and hadn’t been burned.","’That really is unfair.’","It had even apologized, so I couldn’t bring myself to kill it.","If it had acted shamelessly like that raccoon dog, I would have treated it coldly.","Moreover, Fast Sloth appeared to understand the raccoon’s predicament, which was why he had remained still.","I patted the raccoon’s head to assure it that there was nothing to worry about.","Once I showed it some kindness, the raccoon seemed relieved and relaxed.","\"Wait here for a moment.\"","\"Keeeng?\"","It was injured, so I should at least apply some elixir.","I used the animal-grade elixir to treat the raccoon’s wounds.","When they healed in an instant, the startled raccoon began touching different parts of its body.","It was cute in a completely different way from Wonmo.","\"How is it? Feeling better?\"","\"Keeeng! Keng, keng!\"","The raccoon repeatedly clasped its hands together to express its gratitude.","Why did the Forest of the Four Seasons seem to contain nothing but intelligent animals?","It was truly fascinating.","As I watched it with a satisfied smile, the raccoon looked around and then headed toward the fireplace.","Just as I began wondering what it was doing, its bizarre behavior started.","Swoosh—","It thrust its hands directly into the blazing fire.","Unlike last time, it didn’t insert only one hand.","It clasped both hands together and placed them into the flames.","I stared, wondering what on earth it was doing.","\"Keeeng!\"","\"...What is this?\"","The raccoon eventually held out its cupped hands toward me.","Both hands were blazing with fire, yet the flames didn’t appear to be hot.","I had no idea how I was supposed to react.","Perhaps sensing my confusion, the raccoon let the fire gathered in its hands fall to the ground.","Fwoosh!","The flames fell like water and soon faded away.","I focused on the fact that the fire had fallen like \"water.\"","If fire could fall like water, couldn’t it be stored in a bottle?","With that thought, I prepared an empty bottle.","As before, the raccoon gathered fire in its cupped hands and poured it into the bottle I held out.","Fwoosh! Flicker!","The fire inside the empty bottle didn’t go out. It maintained its shape.","It continued burning even after I sealed the bottle with a stopper and cut off its oxygen supply.","When I examined it closely, I discovered that the flames were burning around a small spherical core.","’What is this?’","It was a fire that burned without fuel or oxygen, completely defying conventional scientific knowledge.","What could that mean?","Unable to figure it out, I looked at the raccoon.","Understanding the meaning behind my gaze, the raccoon placed its hands in the campfire again.","\"Nom.\"","It then put its burning hands into its mouth.","\"Fwooooo!\"","Whoooosh!","A massive torrent of fire erupted from its mouth.","The flames were bright enough to illuminate the entire cave in an instant.","My jaw dropped at the sight.","’Why the hell is there a ninja living in this forest?’","While I stood there in shock—","Smack!","\"Kegeng!\"","Fast Sloth slapped the raccoon across the back.","His stern attitude seemed to say that it shouldn’t play with fire.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 143","paragraphs":["Neighbors (1)","A raccoon that breathed fire from its mouth like some kind of ninja.","As if breathing fire weren’t impressive enough, it was even capable of storing flames inside a bottle.","I had no idea what the bottled fire could be used for, but it was such a unique ability that it was bound to prove useful somewhere.","More than anything, though, I liked its personality.","’That’s the biggest reason.’","It wasn’t merely gentle—it was polite, too. There was no way I could dislike it.","Even the Swift Sloth, who was highly sensitive about its territory, had merely smacked it on the back and done nothing more.","That alone showed just how nice this raccoon was. It made me like the little guy even more.","’Should I let it live with me? It seems perfectly capable of looking after itself.’","Whatever else might be true, there was no doubt this raccoon was highly skilled at handling fire.","Just as I had until now, I would continue to have plenty of uses for fire in the future.","If this fire-wielding raccoon lent me a hand, perhaps I would become capable of doing things I couldn’t manage before.","Even if I didn’t yet know what use it had, I might also get some of that bottled fire as an added benefit.","It had probably fallen down the chimney because it was attracted by the flames, so surely we could come to some kind of agreement.","I would provide it with shelter, and the raccoon would use its abilities for me.","I immediately made the raccoon an offer, using a mixture of words, hand gestures, and body language.","\"Keng.\"","However, the raccoon rejected my offer.","It was surprising enough that it understood me, but it even held out a paw to make its intentions unmistakably clear.","No matter how extraordinary its ability might be, the fact that it had come all the way here surely meant it had no home of its own.","In a forest as hellish as this one, a safe place to live was extremely important.","When I asked why it was refusing, the raccoon picked up a twig lying near the firewood.","Scritch, scritch—","It then began drawing a picture on the ground. I carefully studied it.","Just as its intelligence was exceptional, its drawing skills were nothing to scoff at either.","’First the Swift Sloth, and now this guy. Is drawing a basic skill for animals living in the Forest of Four Seasons?’","Somehow, it seemed better at drawing than I was.","While I was thinking that, the raccoon finished its picture. It had drawn three raccoons in total.","At a glance, they looked like a family. Did raccoons normally live in groups?","\"Keng!\"","\"Oh. This one is you?\"","The raccoon pointed at the largest member of the family.","In human terms, it was the head of the household. In other words, the father.","The two smaller raccoons appeared to be its mate and child.","’Then there’s nothing I can do.’","Whether human or animal, the head of a family had important responsibilities.","I nodded to show the raccoon that I understood.","I would have liked to give it some food as a gesture of friendship, but unfortunately, I barely had enough for myself.","The only food I had was extremely salty smoked meat, so it wasn’t suitable.","\"Keng. Keeeng.\"","\"Huh? You want some fire?\"","\"Keng.\"","\"If you want it, go ahead.\"","Instead, the little guy asked for some fire. I readily gave it permission.","I could start another fire whenever I wanted, and it was hard to even call fire a resource.","The raccoon bowed its head after receiving my permission, then held the twig it had used for drawing against the fireplace.","Whoosh!","A flame blazed to life at the end of the twig.","The twig was tiny to me, but when the raccoon held it, it looked like a torch.","Normally, it should have burned up quickly, but somehow, it burned steadily like a candle.","The raccoon gazed at its brightly burning torch with a satisfied expression.","\"Keeeng!\"","\"Yeah. Goodbye. Take care of yourself. If you ever change your mind, come back here.\"","With the torch in its paw, the raccoon went on its way.","It was a shame, but perhaps we would meet again someday.","It might have lacked strength, but it was smart. It would find some way to survive.","’Unlike certain others, it’s polite and well-mannered.’","Some bastard had stolen all my Fasting Pills and then tried to settle the debt with bananas.","If possible, I wanted to maintain a steady relationship with the raccoon. First, though, I needed to figure out exactly what the fire inside the bottle was.","I watched until the raccoon disappeared from sight, then accessed the gallery.","Title: Met a fire-wielding raccoon","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the raccoon bowing politely)","(Photo of the raccoon scooping up fire from the fireplace)","(Photo of the raccoon breathing fire)","(Photo of fire inside a bottle)","(Video of the raccoon leaving with a torch in one paw)","I went outside for a little while, and when I came back, there was a raccoon in my house. It was the one that visited my house before, and apparently it fell down the chimney.","I was wondering what kind of ability it had, and it turned out to be insanely good at handling fire;;","Are there any raccoons with fire-related abilities? If there are, let me know.","Oh, and I wanted to recruit it as a companion, but it refused because it’s the head of its family. Bit of a shame.","└ Heavenly Demon: What a rare and remarkable trick. It is accomplishing something that would be difficult even with Daoist arts.","└ SwordMaster: I’ve never seen a raccoon like that in my life. What is it, a dragon? It’s breathing fire;;","└ Wild Grylls: It ate the fire and then breathed it out. Can mages do that too?","└ SwordMaster: I’m not sure. I don’t know much about that.","└ Starlight Princess: If someone tried that, their mouth and tongue would burn to a crisp.","└ Wild Grylls: Even if they just ate the fire?","└ Starlight Princess: This isn’t some strongman sideshow. Why would anyone eat fire?;;","└ The very act of eating fire is bizarre, you know;;","└ Aren’t there monsters that eat fire?","└ There are, but raccoons don’t, lololol.","└ All-Father: Fascinating. I could understand water, but a raccoon with an affinity for fire...","└ Wild Grylls: Do raccoons shoot water from their mouths?","└ All-Father: No, but they do have a habit of washing their food in water. Perhaps this one roasts its food over a fire instead.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh;;","└ All-Father: But what exactly is that fire inside the bottle? It has piqued my interest.","└ Wild Grylls: It may be hard to believe, but the raccoon scooped up the fire and put it inside the bottle. It scooped flames from the campfire like someone cupping water in both hands.","└ All-Father: Hmm... I would like to study it, but unfortunately, I don’t believe I have enough time at present. If it would not be too much trouble, could you wait two days?","└ Wild Grylls: Understood. It’s nothing urgent.","└ All-Father: Thank you.","└ Don’t tell me that’s some kind of essence too.","└ Who knows? It might also be nothing special, lol.","└ By the way, do raccoons live in groups?","└ I think it depends on the individual.","Everyone found the raccoon fascinating.","They seemed particularly skeptical about the part where it ate fire.","Well, this was the Forest of Four Seasons. It was probably best to simply accept it and move on.","’It probably won’t visit often.’","I had never seen the raccoon until winter arrived.","During the other seasons, it had probably remained within its own territory and the surrounding area.","Now that winter had come, food nearby must have grown scarce, naturally forcing it to venture farther away.","Would such a tiny creature really be able to continue surviving in this forest? I was a little worried.","’It has a special ability, so it should manage.’","It had already adapted well to the Forest of Four Seasons. It might even have a better chance of surviving here than I did.","In any case, now that the raccoon had left, I counted the Iceblooms I had remaining.","I still had about two left, so I could probably use them for something.","I might also find more if I searched the surrounding area.","’I should probably postpone gaining cold resistance, right?’","If I mixed one with something and ate it without the Starlight Princess’s help, I could end up in serious trouble.","But simply leaving them unused also felt like a waste.","’Mixing one with mandrake and giving it to Praise the Sun might not be a bad idea...’","I checked how much elixir I had left.","After mixing some with the mandrake, I had about three and a half bottles remaining.","Since there was always a chance that Wonmo, the Swift Sloth, and I could all be injured at the same time, that amount was the absolute minimum I needed to keep.","’It feels like mixing it with that fire would work perfectly.’","The fire the raccoon had put inside the bottle.","Couldn’t I mix that with an Icebloom?","However, that was merely a guess. I couldn’t be certain. I absolutely needed an expert’s opinion.","Unfortunately, even the All-Father was currently unavailable, which made things difficult.","’I’ll just get some next time.’","I still had plenty of time, so there was no need to rush.","More importantly, didn’t I need to train myself to control cold energy first?","That wasn’t all. Once winter ended, the number of things I needed to do would increase exponentially.","’The bricks, cement, and sand can go here...’","I made preparations in advance for when the weather warmed.","As soon as the thaw began, I planned to build an oven and a furnace.","I also had an emergency exit to consider, so there was a lot of work ahead of me.","’How should I build it so it won’t get swept away by an avalanche?’","An avalanche would probably occur about once a month.","And it wasn’t just avalanches. I had no idea what other kinds of natural disasters might strike.","I would need to survive another two weeks or so before I could understand the rules of this damned forest.","’It has to be extremely sturdy. Should I just construct a small building?’","Since I had bricks and cement, I could erect a building for the oven and furnace.","It would take a long time, but its durability would be guaranteed.","Of course, it would be a different story if some abnormal monster like the Boss Gorilla appeared.","There was truly nothing I could do about something like that. As long as the structure could withstand natural disasters, that would be enough.","’I need to use the space as efficiently as possible and build a separate drainage channel... This is giving me a headache.’","It might have been different if I had gone to university, but unfortunately, I had only graduated from high school.","I hadn’t had enough money, and I had been too busy struggling to survive from one day to the next.","At least I had learned a few useful things in the military. That was some consolation.","I bought a large sheet of paper and drew the cave and the surrounding area on it.","’A rectangular design would probably be the safest choice.’","If I wanted to do that, I would need to cut down more trees.","I planned to clear the path that the Boss Gorilla had personally created.","I spent the entire day working on the design, and before I knew it, the dark night had arrived.","Snow began falling after nightfall, but it wasn’t a blizzard. It was just ordinary snow.","’Is this another sign that the weather is warming?’","According to the journal my Great Senior had left behind, the weather should warm up in another two or three days.","I needed to accomplish everything I could before then. If I was lucky, perhaps I could even go hunting.","I added more firewood to the flames and sat beside the Swift Sloth.","Except when it was eating, this guy seemed to spend all its time in front of the fireplace.","’Winter has its advantages, but I still hate it.’","The most inconvenient part was that the sun set early and rose late.","The reduced activity of the other animals was certainly beneficial, but the same applied to me.","I sat silently before the fireplace until something suddenly occurred to me, prompting me to stand.","’This isn’t the time to sit around. More snow could accumulate overnight.’","So I diligently scattered salt around. Since I didn’t have calcium chloride, I had no choice but to use salt as a substitute.","The emergency exit was still only in the design phase, so it was better to prepare in advance.","With that, I finished preparing for the end of the day. The night was long, and there was nothing else to do.","’At least the gallery has found something new to talk about.’","Thanks to the recent sporting events, discussions about El Dorado had almost completely died down.","In other words, the subject was on the verge of being buried.","I didn’t particularly care, but that probably wasn’t good news for the people outside.","’The people outside can handle that themselves.’","All I could do was wait for winter to end.","I quietly passed the time after uploading a post to the gallery to conclude the day.","\"Hey. Aren’t you going to sleep?\"","\"Forget it.\"","The Swift Sloth could continue staring blankly into the fire if it wanted.","Hoping that another blizzard wouldn’t arrive before dawn, I quietly closed my eyes.","I had no idea what would happen next, but whatever came, it would certainly be difficult rather than easy.","’Knowing this would happen, should I have forced the raccoon to stay?’","With that thought in mind, the next morning dawned.","\"Keeeng!\"","\"Uh...\"","The moment I woke up, the raccoon greeted me from outside the cave.","And it wasn’t alone. It had brought its family with it.","There was a raccoon that appeared to be its mate, as well as a baby raccoon hiding behind them.","The family radiated an unmistakable We’ve moved in atmosphere.","\"Keng!\"","\"...What’s this?\"","The father raccoon held something out to me.","At a glance, it resembled an ordinary balloon flower root or wild ginseng, but its color was extraordinary.","It was as white as snow, practically advertising to the world, I am a miraculous medicinal herb.","\"Keeeng! Keng!\"","Still bewildered, I accepted the herb. The raccoon bowed deeply at the waist.","Its mate and baby did the same. The shy greeting from the baby raccoon was especially adorable.","’...Did they come to hand out rice cakes to their new neighbor?’","It seemed I had unexpectedly acquired some new neighbors.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 144","paragraphs":["144","Neighbors (2)","The unexpected arrival of new neighbors.","I didn’t know why the raccoon family had moved here, but it certainly wasn’t bad news.","For starters, the raccoon was intelligent and polite. That alone was enough to make it far more likable than the gorillas.","Moreover, it was skilled at handling fire, so if we cooperated while living here, it would be a great help.","To make that happen, I first needed to understand what this family wanted.","’The most basic thing would be food...’","Regardless of how difficult hunting might be, the Forest of Four Seasons was abundant in food.","I didn’t know exactly what raccoons ate, but they were probably omnivores.","Besides, they were my \"neighbors,\" not \"family\" who lived with me like the Swift Sloth and Wonmo. They should be able to take care of themselves to some extent.","’That shouldn’t be a problem... right?’","It would be enough for us to help one another in genuine emergencies.","\"Keng. Keeeng.\"","\"That’s your home?\"","The raccoon family showed me where their home was.","It was in a tree not far from the cave—no, it would be fair to say it was right nearby.","There was a large hollow in the middle of the thick trunk.","Apparently, they lived inside it.","’Fortunately, I wasn’t planning to cut down any trees around here.’","It would have been slightly troublesome if their home had overlapped with the area I planned to clear.","Thankfully, not only was it outside that area, but it was also close enough for us to visit each other frequently.","I watched as the raccoon family entered the hollow.","A moment later, one raccoon poked its head back out. The baby raccoon appeared beside it.","There was no way I could resist taking a picture of this. I immediately snapped one for the gallery.","Title: A raccoon family moved in","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the raccoon family appearing before me)","(Photo of the medicinal herb the raccoon gave me)","(Photo of the raccoon family poking their heads out of their home)","(Photo of the raccoon waving happily)","The family of the raccoon that visited my cave moved into the neighborhood. I don’t know if this is their version of handing out rice cakes to celebrate moving in, but they gave me a medicinal herb.","Their home is a hollow in a nearby tree. Looks like we’ll be visiting each other pretty often from now on.","At least these guys are far more sociable than those gorilla bastards. I’m happy to have neighbors too.","└ Heavenly Demon: What adorable neighbors. I hope you get along well.","└ SwordMaster: Wow, I’m jealous. I don’t even have any neighbors.","└ Heavenly Demon: You never leave your home anyway. What use would you have for neighbors?","└ SwordMaster: Tch. Do you have neighbors, then? You never go outside either.","└ Heavenly Demon: They are not neighbors, but this lady’s subjects. Like that raccoon, they occasionally bring me valuable gifts. Have you ever exchanged anything with your neighbors?","└ SwordMaster: ...","└ ...No?","└ Heavenly Demon: You should at least show your face occasionally. Some people would be delighted simply to see you. Of course, if you possess an ugly countenance, it may have the opposite effect.","└ SwordMaster: I’m pretty, you know—","└ Pics or it didn’t happen.","└ Can’t believe it without proof, lol.","└ Heavenly Demon, you should post proof too. Who are you to call anyone uglier than you? Lol.","└ Heavenly Demon: As this lady has said before, I was once given the title of the Greatest Beauty Under Heaven.","└ SwordMaster: If that’s what counts, then I’m widely renowned as a beauty too, haha.","└ What a clash of titans, lololol.","└ Who’s considered the Greatest Beauty Under Heaven in the Central Plains?","└ In the previous generation, it was Yang Seolhwa. Now it’s the Heavenly Demon, though the rumors about her are a little terrifying.","└ What rumors?","└ Something like, \"Even drenched in another’s blood, her beauty could not be concealed.\" It’s chilling, but that’s what I heard.","└ Before people realized she was the Heavenly Demon, wasn’t her alias the Blood Flower?","└ A flower soaked in blood, da-da-da!","└ CCCC","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Hmm! How adorable! Unfortunately, I must ban you for one hour!","└ Wild Grylls: ??? Why? What did I do wrong?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: There’s no video! No video! If you upload one, I may let you off!","└ Wild Grylls: (Video of the raccoon family) Is this enough?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: I’ll let it slide just this once!","└ Just this once...","└ The admin tells the mods not to abuse their authority, but now he’s abusing it himself, lololol.","└ Hypocrisy is a built-in passive skill for anyone with a badge, lol.","└ They really are cute, though, lol.","└ Is that one a baby? I want to hold it.","└ What happens if Grylls takes the baby away?","└ It’s just visiting the house next door, lol.","└ Ah, I see.","└ More importantly, wouldn’t Wonmo eat it?","└ Wonmo: Why is there more emergency food than there was before I went to sleep?","└ Who was the original emergency food? Don’t tell me it was Grylls.","└ Of course he’s emergency food, lololol.","We joked about it, but I couldn’t dismiss the matter as nothing more than a joke.","Even if I accepted the raccoons as neighbors, would Wonmo acknowledge them?","The Swift Sloth appeared to have accepted them, but I had no idea what Wonmo’s appetite might drive him to do.","’The weather seems to be warming up, so Wonmo should wake up soon.’","I looked up at the sky instead of the tree and exhaled.","The temperature had risen enough for me to feel the difference. Even the cloud of breath leaving my mouth had grown fainter.","By tomorrow, the weather would either change completely or begin showing clear signs of doing so.","’I’ll know once Wonmo wakes up.’","Wonmo had started hibernating as soon as winter began, so the reverse should also be true.","After staring at the raccoon family for a while, I returned to the cave.","Since they were good at handling fire, I planned to keep a campfire burning in the yard for them.","Crackle! Pop!","I made a campfire for the raccoons to use, then went inside the cave.","First, I needed to identify the medicinal herb they had given me instead of rice cakes.","’The Heavenly Demon is usually good with things like this, right?’","The Heavenly Demon was knowledgeable about inner cores and medicinal herbs of this kind.","Even if she didn’t recognize it, she could quickly determine what sort of energy it contained.","After examining the snow-white ginseng from different angles, I sent her a message.","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, are you there?]","[Heavenly Demon: Speak.]","[Wild Grylls: You know the picture from the post I uploaded? The one that looks like white ginseng.]","[Heavenly Demon: I was examining it. It appeared to be no ordinary medicinal herb. This lady suspects it is Snow Ginseng saturated with yin energy.]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll send it to you. Would you mind examining it? I’m a little hesitant to eat it immediately.]","[Heavenly Demon: Very well. I shall contact you after inspecting it.]","I sent the white ginseng to the Heavenly Demon. She would probably reply before long.","In the meantime, I considered how I could maintain a good relationship with the raccoon family.","Simply keeping a campfire burning might not be enough.","’If they’re good at finding medicinal herbs, they might become a huge help.’","What if the white ginseng proved highly effective?","I would make them a direct offer: I would provide them with food, and in exchange, they would bring me medicinal herbs.","I could either consume the herbs myself or give them to the Heavenly Demon so she could make Fasting Pills.","This was mutual aid—the very principle that kept an economy moving.","It was debatable whether it could be called an economy without any currency, but never mind that.","[Heavenly Demon: Sir, are you still there?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes, I am. Have you identified it?]","[Heavenly Demon: That raccoon has given you an extraordinarily rare medicinal herb. It is no ordinary ginseng. It contains an amount of internal energy comparable to that of thousand-year-old ginseng.]","[Wild Grylls: So it’s extremely valuable?]","[Heavenly Demon: It may not compare to Humanoid Snow Ginseng or the Ten-Thousand-Year Ginseng King, the king of all ginseng, but it is still exceedingly rare. Its powerful yin energy poses a problem, but since you already possess cold energy, it should not cause you any great difficulty.]","[Wild Grylls: Can you use it to make Fasting Pills?]","[Heavenly Demon: It is possible, but doing so would feel wasteful. This lady believes it would be better for you to consume it.]","[Wild Grylls: Then how long until the Fasting Pills are ready?]","[Heavenly Demon: A full sack will be complete soon.]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll use that as payment instead. I already have trouble controlling my current energy. If I ate this too, I think I’d be in serious trouble.]","[Heavenly Demon: That is a reasonable argument. I shall give this to a close aide. He should be able to sell it for a high price.]","That would be far more helpful to her than giving it to me.","I asked the Heavenly Demon to wait for a moment, then headed outside.","There was something I wanted to ask the raccoon.","\"Keeeeng.\"","\"King, king.\"","When I went outside, I found the raccoon family gathered cozily around the campfire.","All three were holding out their paws to warm their chilled bodies.","The sight of the baby raccoon stretching out its tiny paws was especially adorable.","’This is nice, but...’","I was happy to have neighbors, but someday, I would have to leave this place.","Still, we would be living alongside one another until that day came.","Since they had been the first to show goodwill, I also felt more comfortable around them.","Until I left, we could cooperate and benefit one another.","\"Raccoon.\"","\"Keng?\"","Perhaps it understood that I was calling it, because it poked up its head.","The other two did the same. Its mate and baby both lifted their heads and looked at me.","’Should I give them names?’","Or perhaps calling this one Papa Raccoon would be enough.","In any case, I took Papa Raccoon aside for a moment. He followed me without showing the slightest wariness.","I brought him into the cave and led him to none other than my map—the one on which I had marked everything I had discovered during my explorations.","\"Okay, Papa Raccoon. You see this thing you gave me?\"","\"Keng.\"","\"If you find anything similar, could you bring it to me? If you do...\"","Scrape—","I showed him the white Snow Ginseng he had given me, then dragged over an iron container.","It still held fish frozen solid—naturally frozen fish kept in eco-friendly cold storage.","\"I’ll give you these fish. They’re frozen now, but the weather should warm soon, and then you’ll be able to eat them.\"","\"If you don’t like fish, I can give you something else. I’ll be receiving some Fasting Pills soon. I can give you those.\"","Pat—","As soon as I said that, I felt someone place a hand on my shoulder.","Wondering what it was, I turned my head and found the Swift Sloth staring at me.","Its expression seemed to say, We barely have enough for ourselves, and you’re giving those away?","The Swift Sloth was ordinarily almost entirely free of greed, but Fasting Pills were a different matter.","It had become especially sensitive about them after the gorilla stole them last time.","\"You already eat them one at a time. Besides, we can make more with the medicinal herbs this guy brings us.\"","\"...\"","\"He might effectively become our supplier of ingredients for Fasting Pills, so let it slide.\"","Perhaps persuaded by my argument, the Swift Sloth withdrew its hand.","The Forest of Four Seasons might have been overflowing with medicinal herbs, but I knew next to nothing about them.","Wouldn’t it be better to leave the job to an expert(?)? Naturally, the expert would receive appropriate compensation.","\"...\"","Papa Raccoon appeared to contemplate my offer for quite some time.","Perhaps he didn’t trust me. More importantly, this was essentially a business transaction.","If things went poorly, he might end up suffering a loss. He had a family to support.","Despite the risks, however, perhaps he had decided that I was trustworthy.","\"Keng!\"","The raccoon extended a paw, readily accepting my offer.","I clasped his tiny paw to signify that our deal had been concluded.","But we weren’t finished yet. There were still things I needed to tell him.","That was why I had brought him to the map.","\"Okay. See these two places? The gorillas live here. They’re hostile toward intruders, so you must never enter their territory.\"","\"Keng.\"","\"And this is the cave where the kangaroos live together. See that pig-like creature over there? It was attacked the moment it entered. They’re not friendly. And down here is the lake, but on the path leading to it, there’s a deer...\"","I carefully taught him about every dangerous area in case something happened to the raccoons.","They might have known their previous territory well, but they might not have been familiar with this area.","After concluding my agreement with Papa Raccoon, I sent the white ginseng to the Heavenly Demon.","’I’m glad I found such good neighbors.’","Although perhaps we were business partners now rather than neighbors.","Either way, it didn’t matter as long as we got along.","’That aside, should I build them a little shelter near the campfire?’","It was something worth considering.","***","Around the same time, at the Heavenly Demon Divine Cult—","\"I FOUND GINSENG!\"","A demonic practitioner clutched the snow-white ginseng and shouted loudly enough to shake the heavens.","The man was Wi Seorak. In his hand was the pristine white ginseng.","The Heavenly Demon had summoned him and abruptly given it to him as a gift.","He had been confused at first, but it hadn’t taken him long to realize that it contained an enormous amount of internal energy.","’I-I’m sure Grylls gave this to her, but... I can’t believe she’s giving me something like this...!’","Converted into money, it was worth several years of their budget.","Selling inner cores was troublesome because their origins could be identified, but ginseng was a different matter.","They could simply claim it had been buried in the mountain behind the cult and leave it at that.","In a world ruled by money and martial strength, this was worth far more to Wi Seorak than rain after a long drought.","No, rather than mere rain, it might be the first sign of an abundant harvest.","’The Heavenly Demon is a goddess. And Grylls is invincible.’","His affection for Grylls began to soar.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 145","paragraphs":["Neighbors (3)","By subcontracting the work to Papa Raccoon, I had reduced my workload and saved a great deal of time.","Right now, time was more precious to me than gold—no, even diamonds.","Therefore, I planned to manage our arrangement flexibly so that the raccoon wouldn’t become dissatisfied.","’How should I build their shelter, though?’","Since they were neighbors I would be seeing frequently, I considered building a small resting place for them in the yard.","However, I wasn’t sure what kind of structure the raccoons would like.","They had already made themselves a tidy home, so I had no intention of making them move again.","I was only planning a \"resting place\"—somewhere they could relax comfortably in front of the campfire during the cold winter.","’Building an entire house would be too much. A small shelter should be just right.’","A structure that allowed them to fully enjoy the warmth of the campfire would be enough.","Unfortunately, I had too many problems of my own to deal with, so I couldn’t build it immediately.","The furnace and oven were urgent. A resting place for the raccoon family was not.","As I had said, the raccoon family already had a home, so I could build it once I had some spare time.","’I should at least put down a mat for them.’","I checked the wind direction. With the cave entrance as the reference point, the wind blew from behind it.","Whatever else might change, the wind consistently blew in the same direction, making it easier to design the shelter.","’More importantly, I need to make sure Wonmo doesn’t perceive them as food.’","Wonmo had been plump before entering hibernation, but he had since lost a considerable amount of weight.","In less than ten days, he had rapidly gained weight and then lost it again.","In contrast, the Swift Sloth hadn’t changed at all. Perhaps it possessed some resistance to the cold.","’I’ve already been here for three weeks.’","Today marked exactly my twenty-first day here—three full weeks.","After another week passed, it would be four weeks. In other words, an entire month.","At first, time had seemed to crawl painfully slowly, but recently, the opposite had been true.","It was probably because the sun set early during winter and I spent most of my time inside the shelter. That must have made the days feel shorter.","’That isn’t necessarily a good thing.’","Gaining experience was good, but I still hadn’t acquired any information that might help me escape.","Adapting and escaping were entirely different matters.","Still, it wasn’t as though I had learned nothing at all.","I had obtained the invaluable knowledge that I shouldn’t even consider escaping during winter.","The moment I was swept away by an avalanche, my life would be in danger.","Crackle! Pop!","\"Kiing.\"","\"Kking.\"","I was working on the overall design of the shelter when Mama Raccoon and the baby gathered around the campfire.","Papa Raccoon was away working, but why had these two come here?","’What’s that stuck on the end of the stick?’","The stick in the baby raccoon’s paws particularly caught my attention. Something had been skewered on it.","While question after question arose in my mind, the baby raccoon carefully held the stick in both paws.","It glanced at me, then cautiously approached.","\"Kkiing.\"","The baby raccoon held out the stick it had been clutching so carefully.","For a moment, I wondered if it could manipulate fire like its father, but that wasn’t the case.","I could clearly see a golden-brown grub roasted on the end of the stick.","Most creatures living in the Forest of Four Seasons boasted considerable size, even when they were young.","The baby raccoon alone was about the size of a small dog.","Likewise, the grub skewered on the stick was unusually large.","\"...You want me to eat this?\"","\"Kking.\"","When I pointed at myself and asked, the baby raccoon replied affirmatively.","Wondering what was going on, I looked at Mama Raccoon. She had both paws tightly clasped together.","Her eyes seemed to plead, Please accept my child’s kindness.","What kind of raccoon could make an expression like that?","’Eating insects is a bit much, but...’","I couldn’t reject a gift given with such sincerity.","If I closed my eyes and ate it just this once, I would probably be fine.","\"Thank you. I’ll enjoy it.\"","\"...\"","The moment I thanked it, the baby raccoon scampered away.","It hid behind Mama Raccoon’s back.","Apparently, it was shy around strangers. Still, the way it poked only its head out from behind its mother suggested that it was eagerly anticipating my reaction.","I couldn’t crush a child’s(?) expectations. Besides, this was a gift from my neighbor.","After examining the grub, which appeared to have been cooked better than expected, I popped the entire thing into my mouth.","At least it was cooked, so it should taste like protein—","Squelch!","—or so I thought, but a deeply ominous sound came from inside my mouth.","At the same time, something moist and sticky began dribbling out between my lips.","Had I made a mistake by judging an animal’s cooking according to human standards? Or had the baby accidentally undercooked it because it was still young?","I desperately suppressed the disgust and nausea rising from my stomach and forced myself to chew the grub.","’...Right. In an emergency, I might have to eat these things raw anyway.’","I couldn’t disappoint the baby raccoon, so I persevered and ate it.","Swallowing was the most dangerous part. Calling its taste and texture the worst in history would still have been an understatement.","\"D-Delicious!\"","\"Kkiing! Kking!\"","\"Kiim.\"","When I raised my thumb and praised it, the baby raccoon bounced around excitedly.","Mama Raccoon stroked the baby’s head, but she kept glancing nervously at me.","Apparently, even she knew that her baby had served me an undercooked grub.","Title: The baby raccoon gave me a present","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the baby raccoon holding out a stick)","(Photo of a thick grub skewered on the stick)","That herb wasn’t the only gift I received from my neighbors. The baby raccoon personally roasted this over the fire and gave it to me, lol.","It was a little undercooked, but I endured it and ate the whole thing.","└ Heavenly Demon: I think this every time I see them, but they truly are creatures who understand courtesy.","└ SwordMaster: Ugh. Why is that grub so huge? Is it because it lives in the Forest of Four Seasons too?","└ Wild Grylls: Probably. Everything here is enormous.","└ Did the bug taste good?","└ It looks so plump that it almost seems delicious.","└ Ugh;; Are there actually people who enjoy eating bugs?","└ Don’t knife-ears eat them? They have that nature-loving image, so they probably eat insects too.","└ Let’sGrowTrees: What?! We don’t eat insects! Elves enjoy meat too!","└ Elves eat meat? I can’t imagine that.","└ That’s probably just a stereotype. Knife-ears are incredibly good at politics, and that’s how they built their nature-loving image.","└ Yeah. I heard they used that image effectively because they were positioned as the opposite of the demons. They also have the World Tree.","└ Even now, they get criticized a lot over their tree-planting campaigns, so that image still exists. But they don’t eat bugs, lol.","└ What do dark elves eat, then? They live in the desert, so meat must be scarce.","└ Praise the Sun: Why would we need meat when we have sweet dates? Lol.","└ There are so many dark elves who got diabetes from eating those, lololol.","└ They really are sweet. Dates are one of their biggest exports.","└ So, Grylls, did it taste good? It looks so plump and delicious.","└ Wild Grylls: The moment I bit into it, all its guts burst and spilled out of my mouth.","└ Gyaaaaaagh!","└ Uwaaaaah;;","└ Ugh;; Just imagining it makes me want to vomit.","└ Did you still finish it?","└ Wild Grylls: The baby raccoon was watching me expectantly. How could I refuse? I forced the whole thing down.","└ The baby raccoon did that to mess with you, lololol.","└ Pure evil, lololol.","└ So it was a devil raccoon, lololol.","└ Devilcoon, lololol.","└ Starlight Princess: That’s strange. As far as I know, raccoons normally wash their food in water before eating it. Why did this one roast its food over a fire?","└ Someone here still doesn’t understand the Forest of Four Seasons. There’s a reason for everything.","└ Starlight Princess: And what would that reason be? If you’re about to spout more nonsense, then go away.","└ Because all the raccoons that washed their food in water are already dead. Didn’t you see the river in front of Grylls’s house? A frog that sprays deadly poison jumped out of it, lol.","└ That’s... surprisingly convincing!","└ The Forest of Four Seasons is so terrifying that it forces animals to defy their instincts.","└ Starlight Princess: For once, that wasn’t a completely idiotic statement.","I had heard that before as well. Raccoons supposedly washed their food in water before eating it.","The raccoon that fell into despair after trying to wash cotton candy and watching it completely disappear had been hilarious.","Still, perhaps because raccoons were quick learners, I remembered it no longer washing the cotton candy after losing it two or three times.","Maybe the raccoons in the Forest of Four Seasons had learned something similar—that water was far more dangerous than fire.","’Is that also why they developed the ability to manipulate fire?’","As someone in the comments had said, it was strangely convincing. It wasn’t entirely implausible.","Afterward, I ate a bite of smoked meat to wash away the disgusting taste lingering in my mouth.","It was literally just to cleanse my palate, so it was closer to a snack than a meal.","’Bananas are the best snack, though.’","Thinking about snacks reminded me of the banana the gorilla had given me.","It had thrown the banana at me as if to say, Take this instead of your Fasting Pills and get lost.","It had been an utterly shameless deal, but the banana itself had been genuinely delicious.","Unfortunately, that banana was a specialty(?) found only in the jungle.","I had no desire to enter the gorillas’ territory, so no matter how much I wanted another, I had no choice but to endure the craving.","’Does this forest not have any fruit or anything?’","There were plenty of mushrooms, but almost no fruit. Even when I found some, it was never anything I particularly wanted to eat.","After entertaining those pointless thoughts for a while, I closed my eyes and circulated my heart method.","The overall design of the shelter was more or less complete. All that remained was to wait for the next season to arrive.","I had nothing else to do until then, so training was my only option.","’The cold energy is gradually gathering, little by little...’","The process of separating the cold energy from my mana was also progressing smoothly.","Everything was difficult at first, but once you gained momentum, things became easier.","That didn’t mean I was neglecting my swordsmanship training. I understood the importance of maintaining balance all too well.","\"Whew.\"","By the time I finished a reasonable amount of training, it was already lunchtime.","I was just considering getting something to eat when—","\"Keeeeeng! Keeeng!\"","The raccoon’s cry came from outside.","Rather than a shout, it sounded closer to a scream.","Judging by the voice(?), it seemed to be Papa Raccoon.","The moment I heard it, anxiety surged through me, and I hurried outside.","There was no one in the yard, but the scream had come from the raccoons’ home.","After arming myself, I headed toward the tree where they lived.","\"Rssssss—\"","\"Keeeng! Keng!\"","As expected, my neighbors were in danger.","A huge snake was slithering up the tree.","Papa Raccoon stood at the entrance to the hollow, fiercely resisting with a torch in one paw.","Mama Raccoon and the baby were probably inside.","\"You bastard!\"","I immediately charged at the snake.","Perhaps it sensed my presence.","Boing!","Incredibly, it seemed to bend its body slightly before launching itself backward like a spring.","Its elasticity was astonishing, and its movements were entirely befitting a creature from the Forest of Four Seasons.","\"Shaaaaaah!\"","After briefly landing on another tree, the snake coiled its body and launched itself at me again.","Inside its enormous maw, I saw fangs dripping with venom.","I would have panicked in the past. By now, however, my body had grown accustomed to the Forest of Four Seasons.","I lightly twisted aside to evade the snake’s charge, then slashed downward with my sword.","Slice!","The Heavenly Demon’s sword, combined with an aura-infused strike, cleanly severed the snake’s body.","As if being cut apart weren’t enough, its entire body began freezing from the wound outward.","I had fought the Steel-Scaled Snake before, so I didn’t bother holding back, just in case.","Thrash! Thrash! Crackle!","The snake thrashed violently at first, but it wasn’t long before its entire body froze solid.","I didn’t stop there. I cleanly severed its head.","That should have killed it for good.","’If a snake that should be hibernating has awakened...’","This confirmed it.","Winter truly was coming to an end.","I kicked the frozen snake’s head far away, then turned around.","Still holding the torch in one paw, Papa Raccoon wore an expression of immense relief.","\"Are you all right?\"","\"Keeeng.\"","Papa Raccoon bowed deeply as if expressing his heartfelt gratitude.","His family had also poked their heads out of the hollow and thanked me.","’Thank goodness he had that torch. Otherwise, they would’ve been eaten.’","Most animals were afraid of fire. Snakes were no exception.","Moreover, Papa Raccoon could breathe flames from his mouth, so the snake must have found him troublesome to approach.","Since the raccoon still had that hidden card to play, the two had probably been cautiously watching each other for an opening.","I briefly considered scattering snake repellent around the tree in the near future. Meanwhile, the raccoon family climbed down.","\"Keng!\"","Papa Raccoon then tapped the frozen body of the snake.","Was he suggesting that we eat it?","\"You want to eat this?\"","\"Keeeng.\"","\"Hmm...\"","I looked down at the snake.","It was quite large, so there would be more than enough for us to share.","I had never eaten snake before, but... it would be a waste to throw away prey I had already caught.","Even leftovers wouldn’t be a problem. Now that I had a refrigerator, storing them would be easy.","\"All right. Let’s eat it.\"","After receiving my permission, Papa Raccoon gestured for me to wait and returned to his home.","A moment later, he came back holding something.","\"Keeeng!\"","What Papa Raccoon had brought was a mushroom.","It looked like an ordinary brown mushroom.","I preferred to avoid mushrooms whenever possible, but he must have brought it for a reason.","The thought suddenly occurred to me that he might even know what effects it possessed.","\"What does this do? I’m a little wary of mushrooms...\"","\"Keeeng.\"","Had he understood me?","Rather than answering with words(?), Papa Raccoon demonstrated through his actions.","Thrust! Thrust!","He vigorously thrust his hips back and forth.","He even pumped both arms energetically in the same rhythm.","There was no need for an explanation. I could easily guess what it meant.","Apparently, men were all the same, whether human or animal.","’But even if I eat it, I have no one to use the effect with.’","Was he teasing me because he had a mate?","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 146","paragraphs":["Spring (1)","I didn’t put the virility mushroom Papa Raccoon had given me up for sale at the auction house.","It wasn’t that I distrusted him.","I simply thought I needed an expert’s opinion to determine whether the mushroom really had the effect he claimed and whether it was safe for humans.","After all, this was a mushroom we were talking about.","’I should ask the Starlight Princess.’","The All-Father was currently busy and rarely accessed the gallery, so he was out.","That left only the Starlight Princess. Come to think of it, hadn’t I asked her to analyze a mushroom before?","[Wild Grylls: Starlight Princess, may I ask you a favor?]","[Starlight Princess: Of course. What is it?]","[Wild Grylls: Papa Raccoon gave me a mushroom. Apparently, it’s good for virility, so I think it needs to be verified. I wouldn’t be as concerned if it were something else, but the fact that it’s a mushroom worries me.]","[Starlight Princess: All right. If it were a medicinal herb, I would need the whole thing, but since it’s a mushroom, you only need to send me a small piece.]","[Wild Grylls: Understood. By the way, what did you discover about the mushroom I sent you last time?]","[Starlight Princess: I forgot to tell you! It was poisonous. It contained all sorts of substances harmful to humans.]","[Wild Grylls: I see. Thank you.]","As expected, mushrooms that openly advertised, Do not eat me, were dangerous.","The same applied even to ordinary-looking ones. It was probably better not to eat mushrooms at all.","[Starlight Princess: Mushrooms spoil quickly. You can preserve it by freezing, but... are you planning to eat it?]","[Wild Grylls: Even if I ate it, I’d have no opportunity to use its effects. I was planning to sell it.]","[Starlight Princess: I see. I’ll examine it as quickly as possible!]","[Starlight Princess: If its effects are genuine, I recommend either selling or consuming it immediately.]","[Wild Grylls: Why?]","I had nearly gotten into serious trouble after eating eel before, so I thought it would be best to stay as far away from aphrodisiacs as possible.","It might be fine for people outside, but I had no way of predicting what would happen if I ate this mushroom.","Besides, even if Papa Raccoon had personally experienced its effects, there was no guarantee it would affect humans in the same way.","’Still, he went to the trouble of giving it to me...’","For now, I decided to roast the snake.","I ate the cooked snake together with the raccoon family.","It was my first time eating snake, but it was surprisingly palatable.","Its texture was unexpectedly pleasant, and it tasted similar to chicken.","It had a fishy odor that I hadn’t even noticed in actual fish, but I covered that with salt.","\"Keng!\"","\"Kiing! King!\"","\"Kkiing.\"","The raccoon family also seemed pleased when I sprinkled salt over their snake meat.","They alternated between salted and unsalted pieces before eventually eating only the salted ones with enthusiasm.","They had probably never sprinkled salt directly onto their food before.","It was also my way of showing them what they could enjoy if they continued helping me.","The raccoon family seemed to understand, because they began holding out pieces of meat and asking me to sprinkle more salt on them.","They were unbelievably adorable.","I filled my stomach with snake meat for lunch.","[Starlight Princess: Yes. I don’t know who the wife of the man who consumes it will be, but she’ll certainly be happy.]","I gave a bitter smile.","Whoever that man was, I envied him.","Not because he could eat something like this, but because he had someone beside him.","No matter how effective the mushroom was, didn’t you ultimately need someone with whom to share those effects?","I buried my bitterness and thanked the Starlight Princess.","Then I contacted the gallery member I had in mind.","[Starlight Princess: Mr. Grylls, the test results are ready.]","[Wild Grylls: How is it?]","[Starlight Princess: That raccoon really does seem remarkably capable. The mushroom contains many substances that would greatly benefit a man, and it has no toxicity whatsoever.]","[Wild Grylls: So it’s safe to sell?]","[Praise the Sun: You said you had something for me?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. You were the only person I could think of giving it to.]","[Praise the Sun: It sounds like something edible. Did you ask that dwarf about it? Is he planning to soak it in alcohol again?]","[Wild Grylls: I didn’t ask him because I suspected he would do exactly that.]","[Praise the Sun: Just give it to the dwarf. You’ve already given me plenty.]","[Wild Grylls: It’s been verified as extremely beneficial for men.]","[Praise the Sun: How much do you want for it?]","His country had been established in a desert, much like the Middle East on Earth.","Based on the information I had picked up from the gallery, its culture and general social tendencies also appeared similar to those of the Middle East.","Praise the Sun was obsessed with anything beneficial to his health.","In particular, if something was said to be good for men, he would accept it without hesitation.","[Praise the Sun: Thanks. Let me know if you ever need anything.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh. May I ask for something now?]","[Praise the Sun: Name it.]","[Wild Grylls: You live in a desert, correct?]","[Praise the Sun: I do. Why?]","[Wild Grylls: Do sandstorms occur frequently there?]","Setan—the nation of the dark elves and the wealthy.","[Praise the Sun: Between spring and summer, I suppose? That’s usually when most of them occur. Do you think one might hit your area too?]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t know. That’s why I wanted to ask if you have any clothing or advice that would be useful during a sandstorm.]","[Praise the Sun: We have masks that are effective against sandstorms. Still, the best option is to avoid going outside.]","[Wild Grylls: One could arrive unexpectedly, so I’d like to prepare just in case.]","[Praise the Sun: That makes sense. How many do you want?]","[Wild Grylls: Six in total. Please make one adult-sized and the remaining five smaller.]","[Praise the Sun: Are you planning to put them on your animal friends? Honestly, I don’t think they’ll need them.]","[Wild Grylls: Why not?]","[Praise the Sun: They’ve lived there their entire lives. The masks might only make them uncomfortable. Have you ever seen those videos of dogs being made to wear shoes?]","That was an extremely fitting comparison. I had seen those videos too.","The dogs felt so uncomfortable that all four of their legs moved awkwardly in different directions.","Dogs had paw pads in the first place, so they didn’t need shoes.","The same probably applied to the animals inhabiting the Forest of Four Seasons.","Just as Wonmo had prepared for hibernation in advance, they would quickly respond to any unexpected environmental changes.","’Besides, I have the Swift Sloth.’","Wonmo’s warning signs and the Swift Sloth’s advance warnings should give me enough time to prepare.","I received a mask for protection against yellow dust from Praise the Sun.","Perhaps it was also designed to protect against the desert’s intense sunlight, because the mask was pure white.","’I don’t know whether yellow dust will actually come, though.’","Even if it didn’t happen in spring, a sandstorm could occur during another season.","I had witnessed the terrain and environment across the river changing in real time.","In the worst-case scenario, a sandstorm from the opposite bank might cross the river and reach us.","’Surely the volcano won’t erupt when that area turns volcanic, right?’","If it did, I could die instantly without even understanding what was happening.","The thought was rather frightening.","Still, the ancient traces inside this cave suggested that such events were exceedingly rare.","I spent the day thoroughly preparing for the approaching change of season.","\"Kyuu...\"","\"Oh! Wonmo, are you awake?\"","Wonmo, who had been hibernating, finally woke up as well. His half-asleep expression was incredibly adorable.","He had grown so thin during his brief hibernation that I missed his former plump appearance.","So I immediately gave him something to eat. There was still some snake meat left.","I wanted to buy him a huge piece of meat from the auction house, but he had only just awakened.","If I gave him something too large right away, he might get indigestion, so I started him with a light meal.","\"Nom, nom. Nom.\"","\"Is it good?\"","\"Kyu!\"","After eating the snake meat, Wonmo began regaining his energy.","I hugged him for the first time in ages and rolled around with him. That alone filled my heart with warmth.","\"Wonmo, I’m going to introduce you to our neighbors.\"","\"Kyu?\"","After rolling around together for a while, I decided to introduce him to the raccoon family.","Although it was still chilly, the weather was gradually warming.","Perhaps because of that, Wonmo shivered slightly but didn’t retreat into the cave.","\"Okay, say hello. This is the raccoon family. This is Papa Raccoon, this is Mama Raccoon, and this is Baby Raccoon.\"","\"Kyuu?\"","\"K-Keng!\"","\"Kkiing...\"","\"...\"","Despite my friendly introduction, their reactions couldn’t have been more different.","Wonmo tilted his head in innocent curiosity, while the raccoon family trembled in fear.","Papa Raccoon at least managed to force out a greeting, but the other two couldn’t.","No matter how young Wonmo was, he was still an owlbear—a predator whose adorable appearance concealed a ferocious nature.","The raccoon family had been terrified of a mere snake. It was only natural that they would fear him.","’I just hope he doesn’t recognize them as food.’","Was that even possible?","If Wonmo perceived them as prey and attacked, I planned to stop him immediately.","I would feel terrible for the raccoon family, but I would have no choice but to make them move somewhere else.","It would be an unavoidable decision if we wanted to coexist.","And so, after they finished greeting one another—","\"Kyuuu! Kyuu!\"","\"Kkiing! Kking!\"","Wonmo ran excitedly around the yard with Baby Raccoon riding on his back.","Forget food—he seemed delighted simply because he had made a new \"friend,\" and a bright smile covered his face.","Baby Raccoon had been afraid while first climbing onto Wonmo’s back, but quickly adapted.","’Hmm. Excellent.’","As long as I kept Wonmo well-fed, a catastrophe probably wouldn’t occur.","Now that I had finished introducing the neighbors, I accessed the gallery and uploaded a post.","I couldn’t keep something this adorable all to myself.","Title: Wonmo woke up","Wild Grylls","(Video of Wonmo running around with Baby Raccoon riding on his back)","He’s already playing nicely with our neighbor. Looks like they’ll get along well from now on, haha.","└ Heavenly Demon: The sight brings peace to one’s heart.","└ Cheonggu Princess: They’re so adorable, haha.","└ Starlight Princess: I wish the gallery contained nothing but heartwarming posts like this.","└ Don’t worry. If there’s an emergency, that raccoon will be roasted alive, lol.","└ It’s emergency food, lololol.","└ Starlight Princess: You people are truly pieces of garbage.","There were occasional jokes about emergency food, but most people found Wonmo and Baby Raccoon adorable.","Satisfied, I checked the time. There was still plenty of time before evening.","[What the hell did Kadir say?]","[Fuck, this topic’s about to blow up again, lololol.]","[But if the Mage King went that far, doesn’t that mean this is seriously bad?]","[The Holy Kingdom really seems screwed;;]","[Quick summary]","While checking the time, I browsed the gallery to see if anything interesting had happened.","I noticed people discussing Kadir, so I opened the trending posts. The gallery was in flames.","’Why is Kadir being mentioned?’","Kadir, the Mage King, was a celebrity frequently mentioned in the gallery.","Moreover, hadn’t NecromancyIsLove recently spoken to me about him?","Since he had become the gallery’s latest hot topic, I naturally grew curious.","Title: Fuck, this topic’s about to blow up again, lololol","Kadir even issued an official statement. What happens if the Holy Kingdom keeps acting like this?","└ What did he say?","└ Kadir personally confronted the Pope. Then he got pissed off and secretly broadcast the entire meeting record, lololol.","└ ??? Is that even possible inside the Vatican?","└ He’s the Mage King;;","└ It isn’t that the Vatican is worthless. Kadir is just absurdly powerful.","Title: Quick summary","Kadir: Confess your sins to your god before it’s too late.","Vatican: Fuck off. We’ll handle it ourselves.","Kadir: The ones you should be looking toward aren’t your god, but the people of the Holy Kingdom.","Vatican: The commoners are livestock. Deal with it.","└ Did they really say that?","└ Of course not, lololol.","└ The livestock remark was pretty close, though, lol.","└ This isn’t going to turn into a civil war, is it?","└ Hard to say since there’s no one to rally around. If only the Hero were there...","Title: Outside the Vatican right now","(Video of a protest)","(Video of protesters shouting curses)","(Video of protesters throwing stones)","(Video of the Holy Knights blocking their path)","(Video of a bard playing an instrument to bolster the protesters’ morale)","└ Forget everything else—what the fuck is that bard doing? Lololol.","└ This perfectly demonstrates why an adventuring party needs a bard, lol.","└ Wow, the bard’s music completely changes the atmosphere, lololol.","└ Just watching it fills me with strength, lololol.","Apparently, Kadir had thrown another log onto the fire.","The Holy Kingdom had already been in turmoil over the Ludwig incident, and now the meeting records had been exposed as well.","’Livestock, huh...’","Apparently, no matter where you went, there were always people who regarded their own citizens as livestock.","I chuckled and closed the gallery.","It would probably be best to stay away from it for a while.","’I wonder if things will have settled down by the time I escape.’","Or perhaps the entire Holy Kingdom would be burning by then.","I had no way of knowing.","After closing the gallery, I turned toward the yard.","\"Kyuuung!\"","\"Kkiiiiiing!\"","Wonmo was repeatedly throwing Baby Raccoon into the air and catching him.","To Wonmo, it was merely \"fun.\" From Baby Raccoon’s perspective, however, it must have felt like facing \"death\" itself.","Papa and Mama Raccoon appeared to be pleading with Wonmo to stop, but their efforts were meaningless.","\"Hey! Park Wonmo! You can’t do that!\"","I hurriedly stopped him.","We still had a long way to go.","***","\"Prrr.\"","\"...\"","Ludwig was still riding atop the giraffe.","He stared blankly down at the animal blocking his path.","\"Prrrr.\"","\"Neigh.\"","The creature standing before him was none other than a horse.","More specifically, it was a horse covered in black and white stripes—a so-called zebra.","A Holy Knight riding a giraffe, confronted by a zebra blocking his way.","It was truly a bizarre standoff.","’It appears to be dangerous. To have such conspicuous tattoos in the middle of the grasslands...’","Tap, tap—","Ludwig lightly nudged the giraffe’s sides with his legs.","The giraffe obediently began walking.","Ludwig’s bizarre adventure was still ongoing."]},{"title":"Chapter 147","paragraphs":["Spring (2)","The Mage King, Kadir.","The story of his life was filled with tales that sounded as though they had come straight out of a children’s book.","He had single-handedly defeated a dragon, vanquished every renowned mage who challenged him, and accomplished countless other legendary feats.","But the most fairy-tale-like part of his story was undoubtedly his friendship with the Hero.","The Hero as the protagonist and a mage as his companion—it was a combination commonly found in fairy tales.","Even their achievement resembled one: together, they had defeated the Undying King.","The Undying King had appeared due to the atrocities of the Holy Kingdom, at a time when the demon race was gradually shedding its image as servants of a Demon King.","Whatever the Undying King’s past might have been, the previous Hero and Kadir had joined forces to subjugate him.","Although the previous Hero had tragically lost his life in the aftermath, his death was recorded as a noble sacrifice.","As the Hero’s closest friend, Kadir had also quietly mourned him while temporarily burying the regrettable truth.","However, after confronting the vile and dark secrets concealed by the Holy Kingdom, even that tragic truth began to feel meaningless.","’The ones who claim they have no desire for money are always the greediest.’","The same was true of justice. Those who went around proclaiming themselves righteous were never right in the head.","That was exactly what El Dorado was like now. Those who were supposed to distance themselves from greed had become consumed by it.","Outwardly, they pretended to be devout and respectable, but Kadir had noticed the truth long ago.","El Dorado’s image as a \"Holy Kingdom\" had already crumbled.","’I can hardly wait to hear what kind of nonsense they’ll spout.’","Thus, after making thorough preparations, Kadir headed for El Dorado.","He did not bother asking permission from the Kingdom of Iris, the nation in which the Magic Tower was located.","He was the Magic Tower itself, as well as a mage whose power rivaled that of an entire nation. Who could possibly stop him?","He was not called the Mage King for nothing. Even the king of Iris had to tread carefully around him.","And so, Kadir visited the Holy Kingdom of El Dorado alone.","El Dorado was greatly flustered by his sudden visit, but they immediately welcomed him as an honored guest.","He had given them some advance notice, and they also had ties dating back to the incident with the Undying King.","Before long, Kadir was allowed to enter the Holy See without any obstruction.","\"...What did you just say?\"","\"We merely follow the will of God. What will of their own could servants such as us possibly possess?\"","And within the Holy See—more precisely, during his meeting with the pope and the cardinals—Kadir could only stare at them in disbelief.","As the previous Hero’s friend, he knew perfectly well just how corrupt El Dorado’s upper echelons had once been.","However, those who held power back then were different from those who held it now. Humans had short lives, so generational changes occurred quickly.","He had assumed that things might have improved at least a little by now, but after only a brief conversation, he realized that they had become even more rotten than before.","’These bastards are genuinely beyond saving.’","Maintaining a calm expression, Kadir stared at Pope Louis II.","On the surface, he was an elderly man with a benevolent appearance, but a cunning serpent lurked within him.","A serpent ready to devour a person at any moment.","’Every rotten aspect of El Dorado is embodied in this one pope.’","Kadir clicked his tongue inwardly.","Judging by appearances, Kadir looked younger than the pope, but the two were actually around the same age.","He glanced around at the other cardinals. They said nothing, apparently having already become the pope’s obedient hands and feet.","\"Servants of God... What an ambiguous phrase. Then are you saying that the merciless slaughter of the Undying King’s people was also God’s will?\"","\"Do you think we took pleasure in it? We merely followed the instructions given to us.\"","\"Were they instructions from the previous pope, or from God?\"","\"The pope’s words are God’s message.\"","Their constant invocation of God truly was useful in every situation.","Simply claiming that something was God’s will allowed them both to attack and defend as they pleased.","In the distant past, Aris might personally have inflicted divine punishment upon them for their blasphemy.","However, as the ages passed and human civilization developed, the gods ceased interfering with the world.","’Perhaps they left because they were disappointed.’","That was highly likely. Even Kadir, who did not believe in any god, was feeling tremendously disappointed.","No—it had gone beyond disappointment. Hatred was rapidly swelling within him.","Especially because he knew just how noble the previous Hero had been.","\"So God gave you that command... Is that truly what happened?\"","\"Are you suggesting that God failed to make the correct decision?\"","\"No. I’m asking whether you received a divine revelation or prophecy. The Hero told me that it was his homeland, not God, that pressured him into it.\"","\"....\"","That was your doing, wasn’t it? Don’t lie to my face.","I was the Hero’s friend. I even have recently uncovered evidence.","When Kadir asked with those implications behind his words, Louis II’s expression stiffened slightly.","The same was true of the other cardinals. They made no attempt to conceal their discomfort.","Kadir habitually stroked his thick beard and quietly continued.","\"There is a saying in the Central Plains: ’You cannot hide the sky with the palm of your hand.’ Do you truly believe the world will never learn the truth? I would advise you to repent while you still can.\"","\"My apologies, but....\"","\"Ah, of course, you probably weren’t the ones giving orders back then. You would have been the ones receiving them. It would have been wiser to emphasize that fact and apologize. What a shame.\"","\"....\"","If they had not been the ones who issued the orders at the time, Kadir could understand that much.","But if they still refused to apologize, they were irredeemable pieces of filth.","Either that, or their skulls were simply empty.","\"See here. Your words are going too—\"","Just as one of the cardinals could no longer contain his anger, Louis II raised a hand to stop him.","The cardinal had no choice but to swallow his fury.","Louis II then spoke while maintaining his same benevolent smile.","\"I fully understand what you are trying to say, Lord Kadir. However, I hope you will understand that we merely follow the will of God.\"","\"I wonder whether God would truly accept that interpretation of His will.\"","Kadir snorted.","His mocking words implied that people would no longer believe anything they said.","Kadir could ridicule them to their faces only because he was the previous Hero’s companion and possessed fame and power that no one could ignore.","Anyone else would already have been beheaded and had their head displayed on a pike.","However, even Kadir had failed to anticipate one thing.","There was always another level beneath rock bottom.","\"O Mage King, do you know why we—and humanity as a whole—believe in God?\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Because we are ignorant and foolish. We constantly make the wrong choices, so God must guide us. Of course, even God does not always make the correct choice, but His choices are at least far better than ours.\"","To summarize it simply:","[Humanity is made up of mindless animals.]","Strictly speaking, the pope was referring to the people of El Dorado rather than humanity as a whole, but there was nothing wrong with interpreting it that way.","Everyone was supposedly equal before God, so what difference did it make?","Kadir ultimately had no choice but to laugh in disbelief.","He could not tell whether they were shameless or simply insane.","\"I understand your views perfectly now. Thanks to you, I feel as though my eyes have finally been opened.\"","\"I am pleased that we could be of assistance.\"","\"That shameless façade of yours won’t last much longer.\"","Snap!","Kadir snapped his fingers as he spoke. Louis II immediately realized what that action meant.","Kadir had undoubtedly cast a spell.","The pope became visibly alarmed and hurriedly demanded,","\"What have you done...?\"","\"Ah, nothing significant. Just as my eyes have been opened, I merely helped open the eyes of the people as well.\"","\"Do you think you’ll emerge unscathed after doing this?\"","\"Do you even know what I’ve done before saying that?\"","Kadir’s answer was to respond to shamelessness with shamelessness.","Ignoring Louis II’s fury, Kadir leisurely rose from his seat.","Realizing that something was wrong, one of the cardinals hurriedly attempted to summon the holy knights.","\"Your Holiness! We have a disaster!\"","\"What happened?\"","\"A-a video of this meeting is currently being broadcast throughout El Dorado!\"","\"What do you mean?\"","Louis II could not comprehend the messenger’s report.","This was not merely relay magic. A recording of their meeting was somehow being leaked throughout El Dorado.","Unable to understand what was happening, Louis II glared at Kadir.","\"Ah, it’s nothing remarkable. I merely imitated the Gallery that you branded as evil.\"","\"You imitated it?\"","\"The ability to record and replay everything one sees without the assistance of any device... Don’t you think it is a truly fascinating form of magic?\"","Kadir chuckled. It was a thoroughly eccentric laugh.","By the time Louis II’s face had twisted like that of a demon, Kadir leisurely raised a hand.","\"You will have a difficult time for a while. You brought all of this upon yourselves, so don’t resent me for it.\"","\"Do you believe God does not know the truth?! Have you truly become a follower of that Gallery as well?\"","I obtained a book from there and even deciphered it, you bastard.","Kadir firmly suppressed those words. It was not yet time to reveal that.","That was something he needed to disclose only after more time had passed and he was ready to advance to the next stage.","\"The Gallery? I have no idea what you are talking about. It seems you have something weighing on your conscience.\"","\"You...!\"","\"I’ll leave you to deal with this yourselves. I must be going.\"","He had started a fire and was now fleeing the scene. Kadir had tossed a bundle of firewood onto the dying embers.","El Dorado soon became so chaotic that it teetered on the brink of civil war, throwing the entire world into an uproar.","As Kadir leisurely returned to the Magic Tower, he thought,","’This is when we need the Hero... No. Perhaps it’s better that the Hero isn’t here right now.’","The Hero was currently on the run after being falsely branded a traitor.","No matter how violent the protesters became, they would inevitably scatter without a central figure around whom they could rally.","Would the Hero return, or would the Holy See make the first move?","’This is going to be a rather long battle.’","While chaos consumed El Dorado, Kadir quickly returned to the Magic Tower.","Teleportation was easy when one used magic—although that was only because he was Kadir.","The moment he returned to his beloved laboratory, he opened the refrigerator.","\"The blue mushroom I received before... There it is.\"","[Kill them.]","\"Later.\"","Kadir casually ignored the Undying King’s request and closed the refrigerator.","***","The Gallery was ablaze with discussion over the claim that humanity was made up of mindless animals.","To me, it was little more than watching a fire from across the river, so it did not matter all that much.","My reaction amounted to little more than, Huh, something strange is happening in the world.","Nothing I said would be of much help, and the Gallery probably would not help me either.","I merely found it fascinating that the small ball I had set rolling had transformed into a gigantic meteor plummeting toward the world.","’It’s gotten much warmer.’","I could physically feel that the end of winter was approaching.","My thick winter clothing was beginning to feel uncomfortably warm. Still, I would probably continue wearing it until tomorrow.","It was time to start maintaining my home again. The first problem was the ground, which had frozen solid and then thawed.","Rain had fallen, winter had suddenly arrived, and now the warmer weather had thawed the ground once more.","As a result, the earth had become somewhat muddy and difficult to manage.","Still, it was not so bad that my feet sank as though I were walking through a swamp or tidal flat. It was merely annoying.","’I should gather some gravel from the river later.’","When constructing a building, the most important thing was the ground.","Compacting and reinforcing the earth alone had taken more than half of the entire construction time.","Since I planned to build a furnace and an oven soon, I intended to compact the ground thoroughly.","I could gather gravel from the river, spread it over the ground, and press it down firmly.","\"Wonmo, come here.\"","\"Kkyu?\"","\"Uhehehe.\"","It was evening, and the sky was gradually growing dark.","I wrapped my arms around Wonmo and rolled around on the floor with him.","Winter was over and Wonmo had awakened, so we would finally be able to resume our activities in earnest.","Once I finished everything that needed to be done, I could explore the surrounding territory as well.","’As long as that damned yellow dust doesn’t come.’","It might even be a sandstorm rather than ordinary yellow dust.","Then again, unlike spring in Korea, this place might not get any at all.","I had finished laying all the groundwork necessary to prepare for spring.","’Still, I should put up the tent flap just in case.’","Once I covered the cave entrance with the tent flap, I was ready for bed.","I then tossed more firewood into the fireplace to keep the cave warm.","\"Achoo!\"","I sneezed while getting ready. My nose was incredibly itchy.","It was not a cold. My nose had quite literally begun itching all of a sudden.","’What is this? I have a bad feeling about it.’","Should I sleep while wearing my mask, just in case? It would be uncomfortable, but it would not prevent me from sleeping.","I told the speedy sloth staring blankly into the fire to take good care of things, then went to sleep.","Oh, and I did not forget to practice my internal energy cultivation method before falling asleep.","I had to train consistently if I wanted my abilities to improve even slightly.","And so, I spent the night in the cave while eagerly anticipating the arrival of spring.","The next morning—","Whoooooosh!","The moment I pulled aside the tent flap, a bright yellow world greeted me.","So the yellow dust really did come.","I had only just thought that when—","\"Achoo! Achoo! Aaaaachoo!\"","I began sneezing repeatedly. My nose was not merely itchy anymore; it was starting to sting.","I assumed it was because of the yellow dust, but it was strange that I was sneezing rather than coughing.","Even with my mask on, I felt as though something bright yellow was forcing its way through it.","Suspecting the worst, I barely managed to open my eyes.","’Wait. Don’t tell me this isn’t yellow dust, but...’","The pollen that had tormented me every spring.","\"Aaaaaachoo!!!\"","Pollen billowed through the air like yellow dust, dyeing the entire world yellow."]},{"title":"Chapter 148","paragraphs":["Spring (3)","My pollen allergy was not particularly severe.","It only made me sneeze and gave me a runny nose. Nothing more than that.","If I wore a mask, the symptoms practically disappeared altogether.","\"Achoo! Sniff!\"","Fortunately, the pollen in the Forest of Four Seasons affected me in much the same way.","Its concentration was simply incredibly high—comparable not to the yellow dust that reached Korea, but to the yellow dust in China itself. The symptoms were no different.","Once I put on the mask-like face covering that Praise the Sun had given me, I felt considerably better.","There was nothing I could do about the pollen I had already inhaled, though.","’How do the animals survive in an environment like this?’","I alternated my gaze between the speedy sloth and Wonmo.","The speedy sloth was tossing firewood into the fireplace, while Wonmo stared at me with his round eyes wide open.","I wondered how those two had adapted to this awful environment.","’Whatever else happens, having a home is essential.’","It was not optional. It was a necessity for survival.","If I had failed to claim this cave, I probably would have been swept up in one of the disasters and died.","While exploring, it would be wise to search for shelters where I could take refuge from disasters along the way.","’The pollen has... died down a little.’","The pollen storm had almost subsided.","It seemed all the flowers had bloomed simultaneously with the arrival of spring, causing an extreme amount of pollen to fill the air.","As far as I knew, pollen levels normally peaked around April or May, but the Forest of Four Seasons did not care about such things.","Spring had arrived, so all the flowers had apparently gone, Wow, it’s spring! and bloomed together. The end.","’The problem is that it all erupts at once.’","Still wearing my face covering, I headed outside.","My nose remained itchy, but not enough to make me sneeze. I could not do anything about the runny nose, though.","Thinking that I would have to wash the face covering thoroughly later, I armed myself. My first objective was to collect some gravel.","For the first time in a while, I brought the speedy sloth and Wonmo along with me. Neither of them seemed bothered by the pollen.","\"Pchoo!\"","Or maybe not. Perhaps they had merely been holding it in.","Judging by Wonmo’s sneeze, it seemed to vary from one individual to another.","It was a pollen allergy , after all. The difference between having it and not having it was significant.","When we eventually reached the river, I saw that its surface was still frozen.","The ice must have melted underneath, however, because the water was flowing swiftly.","’I should be able to start setting fish traps soon.’","From now on, I planned to set two traps instead of one.","Having experienced how abruptly winter could arrive, I needed to prepare more smoked food.","’Do frogs hibernate too?’","As I gathered gravel and placed it into a sack, I carefully examined my surroundings.","A frog or some other creature might suddenly leap out.","Fortunately, perhaps because spring had only just arrived, there were no animals in sight.","Once I had filled the sack with gravel, I returned to the cave. All I had to do now was spread it over the ground and compact it.","’Why is this mud so sticky?’","However, since the yard covered a fairly large area, I had no choice but to make several trips.","The ground had not been this bad when it first rained. Winter was responsible for its current state.","The earth freezing solid had contributed, but the snow was probably the decisive factor.","Even though I had scattered salt over the ground from time to time, I had still been unable to prevent it from freezing.","’That takes care of the ground. Shall I start building?’","It was time to rebuild the oven and furnace that the avalanche had swept away.","I planned to construct them sturdily enough to withstand any future disasters.","’If I want to anchor them firmly, I should dig into the ground a little.’","I dug out the ground and laid bricks at the bottom.","Then I stacked the bricks one by one, following the same design I had used before.","Between the bricks, I applied mortar made by mixing sand and cement.","Finally, I repeatedly slid the tray in and out to make sure that the dimensions were correct.","The preparations had taken a long time, but the construction itself went quickly since I had already built one before.","’Just in case, I should build a wall behind it.’","Having learned from the avalanche that had descended from behind the cave, I built the oven directly against the cave wall.","Even that did not seem sufficient, so I decided to erect a solid barrier behind the oven as well.","It would be better than having it collapse and rebuilding it every time a disaster struck.","’Hmm... Will this work?’","Somehow, however, I ended up constructing a barricade rather than a simple wall.","The wall surrounded the entire oven, and its thickness was no joke either.","I wondered whether I had invested too much into it, but it was already finished. There was nothing I could do about it now.","’All that’s left is the furnace.’","I built the furnace directly against the cave as well.","As with the oven, I did not forget to erect walls around it.","I had also applied the cement meticulously, so it should not collapse easily.","’Hmm. Perfect.’","With the cave in the middle, the oven and furnace now stood on either side of it.","I left the areas beside them empty to allow for future expansion work(?).","Wearing a satisfied expression, I photographed the front of the cave and uploaded the pictures to the Gallery.","Title: Rebuilt Everything","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the cave’s front)","(Photo of the gravel-covered ground)","(Photo of the forest radiating warmth)","As of today, winter has ended and spring has arrived in the Forest of Four Seasons.","As soon as spring arrived, I rebuilt everything the avalanche swept away.","Time to resume my industrious life.","└ Heavenly Demon: They resemble wings. It seems you possess considerable knowledge of architecture as well.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you, haha.","└ SwordMaster: Did you spread gravel over the ground because of the mud?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. Ordinary rain isn’t too bad, but after winter the ground becomes far too muddy.","└ SwordMaster: A good decision. Incidentally, did you learn to spread gravel like that in the military?","└ Wild Grylls: How did you know?","└ SwordMaster: I did the same thing.","└ The military really teaches you all kinds of things, doesn’t it?","└ That’s because it has all kinds of people. Sometimes you meet someone who makes you wonder, Why is this guy even in the army?","└ The only useful thing I learned was spear fighting. Having a spear makes an enormous difference.","└ Passing Dwarf: Right. Hey, don’t tell me my mold got swept away too.","└ Wild Grylls: I could move the mold, so I brought it inside.","└ Passing Dwarf: That’s a relief. That thing’s expensive, you punk.","└ Wild Grylls: No matter how expensive it is, it can’t cost more than mithril, lol.","└ Passing Dwarf: I’ve got nothing to say to that, damn it. Lolol.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh, can you give me two fish traps? I think I’ll be making a lot of smoked food from now on.","└ Passing Dwarf: I can, but don’t you have anything to give me in return?","└ Wild Grylls: If I find anything that can be made into alcohol, I’ll tell you immediately.","└ Passing Dwarf: Okay, lol.","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: An impressive arrangement. Are those bricks truly that sturdy?","└ Wild Grylls: They’re meaningless before the power of nature, but they are sturdy. Besides, I used cement this time, so they should be even stronger.","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: I see. That may prove useful later. Are you planning to stop after completing those?","└ Wild Grylls: Of course not. I still need to gather firewood and make charcoal.","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: It must be difficult having to build and cultivate everything yourself.","└ Wild Grylls: It is, but completing something is extremely satisfying.","It was difficult to put into words how satisfying it felt to complete something I had designed.","I had built these things out of necessity, but I could not deny the sense of fulfillment they gave me.","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: I see. In that case, are you also planning to farm?","└ Wild Grylls: I might try, but wouldn’t it be difficult?","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: Since this is the Forest of Four Seasons, it might not be as difficult as you think.","└ Wild Grylls: Perhaps you’re right.","└ Grow, Grow, Grow: You’re seriously underestimating farming;; Just plowing a field is exhausting, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: Is it really that hard?","└ Grow, Grow, Grow: Honestly, the quality of the land matters most, but farming there will probably be even harder because the weather is insane. You said the season changes every week, right?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ Grow, Grow, Grow: Then ordinary farming knowledge might be useless. With the weather changing constantly, the plants won’t be able to grow properly.","└ Wild Grylls: Hmm... Understood. I’ll take that into consideration.","└ Master of Fundamentals Robert: So there was such a problem. I only just realized it myself.","They said pleasure came after hardship.","But after hearing the explanation from a registered user who appeared to be an actual farmer, I began to hesitate.","He added that if I was going to gamble in a casino, I would be better off farming instead.","Farming was labor every bit as unpredictable as gambling, and this was the Forest of Four Seasons.","’I’ll need fertilizer, and I’ll have to water everything... There certainly is a lot to consider.’","I already had plenty to do. Adding farming to the list would make things difficult in many ways.","The Forest of Four Seasons was also a region where disasters erupted whenever they felt like it.","I was already busy enough looking after myself. I had no spare capacity to devote to farming.","The only consolation—if it could be called one—was that I was not planning to operate an actual farm. It would be closer to maintaining a small vegetable garden.","’Should I ask the raccoon family to help?’","I immediately discarded that idea.","The father raccoon was busy searching for medicinal herbs.","The mother raccoon would have her hands full caring for the baby raccoons. I could not think of any suitable source of labor.","’Still, I should at least look for an appropriate plot, just in case.’","This was merely preparation for the possibility. I would only start farming if I genuinely had enough free time.","I spent the rest of the morning cleaning everything up. For lunch, I ate the fish that remained in the metal container.","It had been so long since I last ate fish that it tasted even more delicious.","[ Passing Dwarf: Here are the two fish traps. Be careful not to let them get destroyed again.]","[ Wild Grylls: I’ll try. I can anticipate the changing seasons, but I never know when it will rain. Oh, can you give me a barricade too?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Just build a thick wall out of bricks. That would be far better.]","[ Wild Grylls: You think so too?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Yep. No matter how exceptional wood might be, it can’t compare to stone. Unless it comes from the World Tree, I suppose.]","The World Tree.","Come to think of it, I had once seen an incredibly enormous tree.","It was when I experienced an out-of-body state after receiving the second mnemonic verse from the Heavenly Demon.","I could not be certain that it was the World Tree, but it might be worth investigating.","[ Wild Grylls: Is the World Tree really that tough?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Its branches perform better than steel. Need I say more?]","[ Wild Grylls: Damn. Then what about the gloves I received from that elf before? Are the leaves just ordinary leaves?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Yeah. But the silkworm wasn’t an ordinary silkworm either. I don’t know what was going through that knife-ear’s head, but they gave you something genuinely valuable.]","The gloves Planting Trees had given me.","I had been making excellent use of them.","I had given them the Guardian’s Core in exchange, but I had no idea what they were doing with it now.","They occasionally appeared in the Gallery, but as always, all they ever talked about was planting trees.","’World Tree or not, I hope there’s something useful there.’","The place was extremely far away to begin with, making a round trip difficult.","After thanking the dwarf, I examined the fish traps.","Normally, it would have been better to visit the river tomorrow, but food had to be gathered whenever the opportunity presented itself.","I could break the ice myself and install the traps today.","’There’s a grassland across the river this time.’","The region on the other side of the river changed at certain intervals.","I did not know how long those intervals were or what determined the next environment.","Perhaps I needed to uncover that pattern soon. Doing so would expand the range within which I could operate.","\"...Huh?\"","Wait. What was that?","I blinked.","Since it was a grassland, I could accept that it contained various animals.","Therefore, I could overlook the presence of a giraffe. I could even overlook that giraffe fighting back against a predator.","But I could not simply overlook the person riding on the giraffe’s back and swinging a sword.","It was not as though a giraffe were a horse.","Rub, rub—","The sight was so unbelievable that I rubbed my eyes and looked again.","Unfortunately, it seemed to be the exact moment when the region was changing. The grassland across the river blurred like a mirage.","A barren, rocky wasteland then replaced it.","The knight who had been riding the giraffe had vanished without a trace.","’Are there really people here?’","For a moment, faint hope arose within me.","’But he was riding a giraffe.’","He had even fought like a knight while doing so.","Confronted by such an utterly bizarre sight, I could not help feeling confused."]},{"title":"Chapter 149","paragraphs":["Countermeasures (1)","My confusion over the existence of a knight riding a giraffe lasted only briefly. He had already vanished, and there was nothing I could do about it, so I decided to focus on the task at hand.","First, I broke through the ice covering the river and plunged my hand into the water to provoke the golden frog.","Of course, it would be better if the golden frog was still hibernating and did not appear.","Then I would not have to waste any time dealing with it.","Splash—","\"Gaaah!\"","The moment I put my hand in, a strange cry escaped my lips. The water was far too cold.","I had gotten a rough idea of its temperature from the water coming through the hose, but feeling it directly against my skin made it seem even colder.","Still, it was something I had to endure to secure food.","Fortunately, the golden frog must have still been hibernating, because it did not appear.","\"Brrrrr. S-so cold.\"","There was nothing I could do about the cold, though. This was exactly why I had wanted to acquire cold resistance.","Shivering violently from the chill that surged through me the moment I stepped into the river, I installed the fish traps.","All the shoes I had traded for until now were waterproof, but the river was too deep.","That left me no choice but to enter it wearing sneakers.","’Just ten minutes. I only have to endure it for ten minutes...!’","There was a risk of frostbite, but I should be fine. I might not possess cold resistance, but I could wield cold energy.","That should provide a certain degree of protection, so I was not worried about frostbite.","The water was simply mind-numbingly cold.","After installing both traps, I hurried back to the cave.","The first thing I did upon returning was heat some water and soak my feet in it.","I probably would not suffer frostbite, but this was merely a precaution.","As I sat there with my feet submerged, I recalled the scene I had witnessed earlier.","’Was the person I saw across the river really there?’","Not only had he been riding a giraffe, but he had also been wielding a sword like a knight.","Even the predators surrounding him—lions, to be precise—had been unable been unable to approach him easily.","’Wait. Come to think of it, wasn’t his sword glowing?’","The sword the knight had been holding had definitely emitted a green light.","Although the glow had been rather faint, it was unmistakably green.","Only the mythricon I had given away should glow green.","’Then was that Ludwig?’","Ludwig—the holy knight renowned for his upright character.","And the man who posted exceptionally middle-aged-sounding messages in the Gallery.","It was entirely possible that he had been the one swinging a sword from a giraffe’s back.","’Seriously, the timing couldn’t have been worse.’","I thought about it while warming my feet in the heated water.","No matter how I looked at it, the timing was incredibly unfortunate. Why did the region have to change at that exact moment?","If I had been given one more minute—or even just thirty seconds—I could have examined him more closely.","’I really have the worst luck.’","The knight I suspected was Ludwig probably had not noticed me.","He had been locked in a fierce battle with a pride of lions. How could he possibly have spared any attention for the opposite side of the river?","’Come to think of it, didn’t they say giraffes don’t exist in this world?’","I was not completely certain, but that was how I remembered it.","Just in case, I searched the Gallery for \"giraffe.\"","Nothing appeared. There were posts containing the individual syllables, but there was no animal called a giraffe.","Unicorns and pegasi, by contrast, clearly existed. They were apparently regarded as ordinary knowledge.","Of course, giraffes might simply have been known by another name, so I even drew one to confirm.","Title: Does an Animal Like This Exist?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of my giraffe drawing)","Is there an animal with a long neck and legs like the one in this drawing? Where I came from, we called it a giraffe.","└ Heavenly Demon: It is not even a spirit beast. This is my first time seeing such a bizarre animal.","└ SwordMaster: Mine too. I’ve never seen or even heard of such an animal in my life.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Its long neck makes it look kind of sad.","└ Starlight Duchess: How does it eat with such a long neck?","└ Praise the Sun: There’s something... strangely fascinating about it. I want one.","└ Clever Demon: It’s seriously ugly as hell, lololol.","└ Do they use their necks like whips when they fight? Kekeke.","└ Wild Grylls: How did you know? I heard they really do swing their necks to wreck their opponents. Otherwise, they kick with their hind legs.","└ What the hell kind of animal is that? You’ve got one hell of an imagination, lol.","└ What if it breaks its neck while attacking?;;","└ That body is the pinnacle of inefficiency, lol.","Since I was technically an animal as well, my existence probably served as another piece of evidence supporting the hypothesis.","However, while I knew the result, I still could not determine the cause.","’I suppose I’ll have to examine everything carefully.’","The conclusion was that I needed to learn more about this forest.","I had begun to suspect that my arrival here had not been a coincidence either.","Survival was important, but so was exploration. I needed to find clues if I wanted to improve my chances of escaping.","’I’ve been keeping a journal consistently, so only time will tell.’","Now that I had realized the seasons changed every week, I planned to devote more time to exploration.","Originally, I intended to remain in my shelter until I became stronger, but allowing that period to drag on for too long would not be wise.","Besides, winter would force me to rest anyway.","Of course, now that I had discovered evidence of another survivor, I first needed to devise countermeasures.","’I should provide them with something useful for survival.’","└ All-Father: Oh. What a fascinating animal. Something similar existed in the distant past.","└ Wild Grylls: Really?","└ All-Father: Yes. They were monsters called dinosaurs—the ancestors of dragons and drakes. Some dinosaurs had extremely long necks.","└ Did those dinosaurs fight with their necks too?","└ All-Father: According to one theory, they used their long tails like whips. Wyverns are also descendants of dinosaurs.","Was he talking about brachiosauruses?","It was fascinating that dinosaurs had existed in this world too.","No. Before that, it was even more fascinating that these people could not accept the existence of giraffes.","’Then what was the giraffe I saw?’","Had giraffes perhaps lost the struggle for survival and gone extinct?","The Forest of Four Seasons was a place where even herbivores were absurdly powerful, so perhaps they had survived here.","It was a reasonably convincing hypothesis.","If not, then—","’Could they be... connected to Earth?’","Just as I had suddenly fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons, animals from Earth might also have been brought here.","And was Ludwig, the knight riding the giraffe, truly the only person who had entered the Forest of Four Seasons?","I had heard that other people had been forcibly dragged in along with Ludwig.","If they were fortunate, they might still be alive somewhere in the forest, just like him.","However, from my own experience, the Forest of Four Seasons was an exceedingly difficult place to survive without a secure base.","Furthermore, without suitable tools, one’s chances of survival were practically nonexistent.","’Just as the Gallery helped me, I should help them.’","Unless they were me, anyone brought into the Forest of Four Seasons would be unable to access the Gallery.","There was no way to determine their locations either. Even asking the administrator would be useless.","The only thing I could do was throw survival supplies across the river.","Since I had no idea where they were, this was my best option.","’Food is the most important survival resource, but...’","Unfortunately, food was the one thing I could not spare.","Now that I knew winter would return, I needed to begin steadily building up my own reserves.","Conversely, that meant I could provide most things other than food.","’Weapons, for example.’","Weapons were extremely important in the Forest of Four Seasons.","Had I not survived countless crises after receiving the Heavenly Demon’s sword?","I did not know Ludwig’s exact circumstances, but he also seemed to have survived somehow with the mythricon sword.","’I’ll forge swords and throw them across the river. That should work.’","This was the best countermeasure I could devise. Nothing else came to mind.","Actually, there was one other possibility.","The signposts I had erected near the cave.","I could build an enormous sign visible from across the river.","It would be similar to the defector guidance signs installed along the front lines.","’I should have done this from the beginning...’","I had not installed any signposts near the river. That had been a major mistake.","For some reason, I had complacently assumed Ludwig would appear on my side.","Because of that, it had never occurred to me that the sign needed to be visible from across the river.","If I had erected one earlier, Ludwig might already have crossed over.","What a shame.","Learning from that mistake, I planned to write the message in multiple languages.","That way, it would be useful not only to Ludwig but to anyone who entered the forest, regardless of when or where they came from.","’I can ask the Gallery about each country’s language.’","Languages differed by race and nation, but I had the Gallery.","Since the registered users came from various backgrounds, I could simply ask them.","’The sign absolutely has to be large.’","I could construct it in much the same way as I had made the signposts.","However, its sheer size meant it would require a great deal of work. Joining all the pieces of timber together would be particularly difficult.","I constructed an enormous sign by fitting wooden boards one at a time onto long poles.","One might wonder whether that would make it difficult to write on, but there was no need to worry.","’I’ll attach a large sheet of paper to it.’","Attaching paper would make things easy. I would not have to write directly on the sign.","Smiling in satisfaction at the sign, which was clearly visible even from a distance, I accessed the Gallery.","I then purchased a sheet of paper to attach to it and asked the registered users for assistance.","[ Heavenly Demon: Shall I write exactly what you told me?]","[ Wild Grylls: Yes. Please do.]","[ Heavenly Demon: It is not difficult. Wait a moment.]","[ Wild Grylls: Understood.]","[ Heavenly Demon: (Photo of the notice written in the language of the Central Plains) Will this suffice?]","[ Wild Grylls: Thank you! I think this every time I see it, but your handwriting is truly beautiful.]","[ Heavenly Demon: Thank you.]","First, I received the Central Plains version from the Heavenly Demon.","Then SwordMaster, who had briefly decided to play a prank, provided the Messiah Empire’s language.","[ SwordMaster: (Photo of an explanation written in the language of the Messiah Empire) Will this do?]","[ Wild Grylls: Yes! Thank you so much!]","[ SwordMaster: Wait. Let me send you another one...!]","[ Wild Grylls: Huh?]","[ SwordMaster: (Photo of the notice written in the language of the Messiah Empire) Here’s the new one, haha.]","[ Wild Grylls: What did you write the first time?]","[ SwordMaster: I wrote, \"Become stronger and marry me.\"]","[ Wild Grylls: ;;;]","[ Passing Dwarf: Good grief. I never imagined I’d do something like this in my entire life, lol.]","[ Wild Grylls: Try to understand how I feel. I’m desperate too.]","[ Passing Dwarf: Fine. Wait a moment.]","I received the dwarven language from the dwarf.","I also asked Cheonggu Princess, All-Father, Praise the Sun, Planting Trees, Suspiciously, and several others.","Through them, I obtained the languages of various countries and races.","Someone might wonder why I did not simply make a public Gallery post asking everyone at once. I went through the extra trouble because the replies would probably have become too chaotic.","[ Don’t Abandon the Hero: (Photo of the notice written in El Dorado’s language) Will this work?!]","[ Wild Grylls: Thank you. I sincerely hope Ludwig sees it.]","[ Don’t Abandon the Hero: Have you seen Mr. Ludwig?!]","[ Wild Grylls: I think I did, but I’m not certain. He was riding a giraffe and swinging the sword I gave him.]","[ Don’t Abandon the Hero: A giraffe... Do you mean that bizarre animal from your post?!]","[ Wild Grylls: Yes.]","[ Don’t Abandon the Hero: I see! It may be strange, but I’m relieved to hear that he’s alive! Please contact me immediately if you confirm his survival!]","[ Wild Grylls: Understood.]","Finally, I received the El Dorado version from the administrator, who was originally from there.","I copied all the languages I had received from the various nations and races onto the paper.","I used black paint so that the words would contrast sharply against the white background.","’There are so many languages. This is exhausting.’","The paper itself was enormous, and copying foreign languages onto it was difficult work.","I had to use the available space efficiently, so maintaining my concentration was especially important.","Eventually, I finished writing the message in every language.","Smiling, I looked over the completed notice.","Its contents were roughly as follows:","[Gallery registered user Wild Grylls welcomes all survivors!]","[If you can read this, follow the signposts downhill! You will eventually see a cave!]","[We are stronger together than we are alone! Let’s overcome this together!]","How should I put it?","It did not exactly feel like a survival notice.","’It almost sounds like a government advertisement encouraging people to immigrate...’","Anyway, now that the notice was complete, all that remained was to produce the survival supplies.","’Let’s get moving.’","There was no point in constructing the sign if those who saw it could not survive long enough to reach me.","I gripped my pickaxe and began mining the mithril buried within the cave.","And as I did—","’Please survive.’","I desperately prayed that someone would survive long enough to reach me."]},{"title":"Chapter 150","paragraphs":["Countermeasures (2)","Title: Made a Notice","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the notice)","I’m planning to install this where it can be seen from across the river.","I originally wasn’t going to put one near the river, but I saw a person on the other side today;;","It happened too quickly for me to take a picture, but I think it was the person sent by the Holy Kingdom. Yeah.","└ Heavenly Demon: Did you truly see a person?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. He was riding a giraffe and fighting lions.","└ SwordMaster: A giraffe is the long-necked animal you mentioned earlier, correct?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ SwordMaster: It seems like the rider wouldn’t be able to see ahead very well because of its neck;;","└ Wild Grylls: I haven’t asked one myself, so I wouldn’t know.","└ What if the giraffe comes across with him?","└ Lol, then you’ll have another mouth to feed.","└ With a neck that long, would it even fit inside your shelter?","└ That’s one problem, but it might also have a nasty temperament;;","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: That’s a good idea! Other survivors should be able to see it too!","└ Are you sure you didn’t see things? Maybe the Forest of Four Seasons showed you a hallucination.","└ It sounds far too detailed to be a hallucination. We’ll just have to wait and see, lol.","└ What if that person kills Grylls?","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: That would never happen! Mr. Ludwig is a good man!","└ Even a good man can turn evil when his survival is at stake, Admin;;","└ I’m worried about that too. Ludwig might be fine, but what if another survivor arrives and causes trouble?","At first, the responses were exactly what one would expect from the Gallery, but various concerns soon followed.","Suppose there truly were survivors in the Forest of Four Seasons. They might see the notice and cross the river.","But what happened after that? What if a survivor harbored malicious intentions and tried to hurt me?","’It’s not impossible.’","When survival was at stake, every animal was effectively a competitor.","It was no different even between members of the same species.","Moreover, I could not speak the languages of this world, so persuading them would not be easy.","’I’ll have to make full use of the Gallery.’","Even the absurdly powerful sloth struggled to obtain food in the Forest of Four Seasons.","Without the Gallery, I would have starved to death too.","In an isolated place like this, access to the Gallery was an advantage in itself.","I could show it to the survivors and perhaps use it to translate our conversations.","’Recruiting them is still the highest priority. Manpower is what ultimately matters.’","There were things people could do and things only the Gallery could do.","As if on cue, a flood of comments expressing thoughts similar to mine appeared.","Some included insults, but I did not particularly care.","’I should install the notice first.’","Its size was not a problem. I had my subspace backpack.","Before long, I had carefully positioned it so that it could be clearly seen from across the river.","I could inspect its condition whenever I came to collect the fish traps.","’Crossing the river is another problem.’","The river was wide, and the current was far too strong. Crossing it without a boat would be difficult.","I briefly wondered whether a survivor might be able to leap across, but assuming that someone at such a level had survived without suffering any injuries would be overly optimistic.","The more survivors there were, the greater the possibility that one of them had injured legs.","Had I not possessed the elixir, I myself would have been forced to live with a disability.","’I need to build a bridge.’","One might wonder how a bridge could work when the region across the river changed in real time.","However, only the region beyond the river changed. The river itself always remained the same.","That meant there was always land with similar conditions on the opposite bank.","’I should measure the distance first.’","I took a rope from my subspace backpack. I always carried simple tools like that with me.","I then tied a dagger to its end and threw it across the river.","I did not throw it into the changing region itself, only as far as the boundary.","’As expected, it’s quite wide.’","I marked the rope and pulled it back.","I was about to return when I paused and stared at the region beyond the river.","The Forest of Four Seasons displayed all kinds of environments. At the moment, the other side was filled with fog.","What was hidden within that mist?","Could survivors truly be living even in a place like that?","’No matter how I look at it, I was incredibly lucky.’","Gallery access aside, I was fortunate merely to have found myself somewhere that made survival possible.","If I had appeared in the misty region, a volcanic zone, a desert, or even a snowy mountain...","The thought alone was horrifying.","’Where was that person? Don’t giraffes live on grasslands?’","There had also been lions surrounding him. Those were animals native to grasslands.","But I could not be certain of that either. Kangaroos lived not far from here.","As with humans, wherever an animal adapted became its habitat.","’I’ll take my time with the bridge and forge the swords first.’","Even a temporary bridge would take a long time to build. Swords would not.","Besides, I needed to test the father raccoon’s abilities.","Of course, sharpening swords was the dwarf’s specialty, so I decided to ask him for assistance.","[ Passing Dwarf: I think this every time I see you, but you have a tendency to view the world far too optimistically.]","[ Wild Grylls: What are you talking about?]","[ Passing Dwarf: I understand that you’re happy to have seen another survivor, but you should never make decisions recklessly when you’re excited. Think things through at least two or three times.]","His response was painfully sound advice.","At first, I wondered what had gotten into him.","This was the same dwarf who usually traded jokes with me and laughed about everything.","For him to say something like this meant I was making a rash decision. He was giving me a much-needed warning.","’Um...’","I pressed my lips together and considered what the dwarf might be concerned about.","I had planned to throw supplies—specifically, weapons—across the river for the survivors.","I had judged weapons to be more practical than food.","After all, mithril and orichalcum were scattered everywhere around me.","’...Could something like that gorilla end up using them?’","The gorillas might have looked different from humans, but they were effectively comparable to primitive mankind.","Some individuals used crude weapons, and the leader could even manipulate mana.","Imagine if one of them obtained a mythricon sword.","Forget survival—the entire ecosystem would be thrown into chaos.","’Come to think of it, they said monsters exist too.’","Goblins, orcs, gnolls, ogres, and other creatures commonly found in fantasy stories.","Those creatures were even more dangerous because they knew how to use tools.","If even apes could use mana here, why wouldn’t they be able to?","If things went wrong, I would personally be creating an unimaginably dangerous threat.","’Damn.’","A bitter taste filled my mouth.","As the dwarf had suggested, discovering another survivor must have gotten me overly excited.","In the end, I abandoned the idea of throwing swords across the river. The risks were far too great.","Still, I should forge a sword specifically for Ludwig.","It could serve as a spare.","’Before that, I should build the bridge.’","I asked the dwarf about that as well, requesting a suitable method for constructing a temporary bridge.","Since the river might swell when it rained, I wanted to build an arched bridge.","If even the dwarf did not know how, I planned to lay down a simple structure first and gradually reinforce it.","[ Passing Dwarf: There is one method, but I don’t know whether you can manage it alone.]","[ Wild Grylls: What is it?]","[ Passing Dwarf: It’s called a Da Vinci bridge. It’s an old construction method that has been used for ages. The structure is fairly simple, so I believe it was commonly used during wars.]","Da Vinci?","Could it possibly be the same Da Vinci I knew?","The familiar name startled me slightly.","Cement was one thing, but Da Vinci was the name of a famous historical figure, which made it difficult to dismiss.","[ Wild Grylls: Da Vinci? Is that a person’s name?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Huh? All I know is that the method has existed since ancient times.]","It seemed I would be better off asking All-Father.","For now, however, the origin of the name was less important than the construction method.","[ Wild Grylls: Can you teach me?]","[ Passing Dwarf: Teaching you is easy, but building it will be rough. Do whatever you want. By the way, can’t that person just jump across?]","[ Wild Grylls: How could anyone cross a river that way? Besides, he might have injured his legs.]","[ Passing Dwarf: Lol. In that case, you might as well mass-produce elixirs and scatter them around. That would probably work better.]","It was not as though I had never considered that.","However...","A mature mandrake alone was not enough to produce an elixir.","If I asked Starlight Duchess, she would naturally agree to make one for me, but repeatedly asking for favors would be embarrassing.","More importantly, the mandrake population was visibly beginning to decline.","’Now that I’m considering every detail, aren’t I in danger too?’","After thinking things over two or three times, I realized the dwarf’s advice was completely correct.","This was no time for me to act as though I had resources to spare.","My happiness at seeing another survivor must have lowered my intelligence.","’They say not to make decisions when you’re happy. This is exactly what they meant.’","Only twenty-two days had passed.","That was all, yet I already missed human company so much that it was driving me insane.","Seeing another survivor in that state must have briefly short-circuited my brain.","’I can’t afford to be so optimistic.’","After reaching that conclusion, I learned how to construct a Da Vinci bridge from the dwarf.","Naturally, he conveyed the instructions through a Gallery post. The structure itself was not particularly complicated.","The dwarf had even uploaded a video in which he demonstrated the assembly using small sticks. That made it easy to understand.","Understanding it was one thing.","The thought of constructing it out of full-sized timber already seemed overwhelming.","└ Passing Dwarf: If it’s too much of a pain, should I just make it for you?","└ Wild Grylls: No. I need to account for the changing region across the river, so I want to build it myself.","└ Passing Dwarf: Then I’ll give you a hand plane. Use this.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you.","└ Passing Dwarf: By the way, what will you do if an animal crosses instead of a person? Have you considered that?","└ Wild Grylls: The bridge is necessary because of the golden frogs anyway. Those bastards are basically guarding the crossing.","└ Passing Dwarf: Ah. That’s true.","Now that I had also received a hand plane from the dwarf, I began constructing the bridge in earnest.","The first step was logging.","This time, I was not gathering firewood but materials for the bridge.","I did not use mana. The cold energy might cause me to ruin the timber.","Crack!","A large tree toppled over.","All I had to do was process it piece by piece.","I set the smaller branches aside for firewood and charcoal, then cut the massive trunk into appropriately sized sections.","’Doing all of this alone is seriously exhausting.’","When would the region across the river turn back into a grassland?","I hoped it would change soon.","’But a Da Vinci bridge? Could it really be the Da Vinci I know?’","Between that and the cement, there were several strange similarities.","Were they truly the same things I knew, or were the names merely coincidences?","It was worth thinking about, but I decided to set it aside for now.","’Who cares?’","Survival was ultimately what mattered.","***","While Grylls was busily cutting down trees to build a temporary bridge, Ludwig—the holy knight riding the giraffe—found himself in a difficult situation.","The giraffe had not betrayed him.","On the contrary, they had just emerged victorious from their battle with the pride of lions.","Thanks to the giraffe’s extraordinary height, the battle had effectively been a siege.","His reach had not been a problem either, as the mythricon sword Grylls had gifted him had performed splendidly.","The sword reacted strongly to even the faintest amount of mana.","The Forest of Four Seasons possessed an exceptionally high mana density, making mana extremely difficult to use.","However, it was only difficult, not impossible. With sufficient concentration, Ludwig could manipulate it to a limited degree.","The drawback was that it felt like forcing an elephant through the eye of a needle, leaving him unable to exert even five percent of his normal power.","Even so, the mythricon sword’s superior performance had provided Ludwig with tremendous assistance.","\"Urgh...\"","But it inevitably had its limits.","After the fierce battle, Ludwig rested beneath a massive tree.","He groaned as he examined the place where the lions had wounded him.","Fortunately, both arms were unharmed, but a lion had bitten his right foot.","A lion’s bite was already renowned for its terrifying power, and this was a lion native to the Forest of Four Seasons.","It had literally crunched through his steel boot, leaving him severely injured.","’This is bad. I don’t see any medicinal herbs I can use for treatment.’","He had given all his potions and other healing supplies to Reis.","Aside from the mythricon sword, he had effectively entered the Forest of Four Seasons with nothing.","At first, a combination of coincidence and good fortune had made survival relatively easy.","It seemed that luck had finally run out.","’Considering the risk of infection, amputation would be the correct decision, but...’","Contemplating the worst-case scenario, he looked around.","There was nothing but an endless grassland. He could not see anywhere suitable for hiding and resting.","A cave?","Every cave he had discovered thus far was occupied by either a three-headed lion or a monster of comparable strength.","’But was the person I saw earlier merely an illusion?’","Ludwig recalled what had happened.","Across the river, he had seen someone who appeared to be from the Central Plains.","The sight had left him so stunned that he had suffered this injury.","He was fortunate that only his foot had been wounded. Without the giraffe, his life would likely have been in danger.","’If it wasn’t an illusion...’","He turned his head toward the river.","The landscape was different from before.","Previously, he had seen a forest on the opposite bank. Now, there was nothing but desert.","His delight at discovering a source of water had lasted only briefly. Even the region beyond the river had completely changed.","’If the flesh begins to necrotize, I’ll have to amputate.’","Until then, he had no choice but to monitor the wound.","Frowning, Ludwig raised his head.","It seemed he would have to use this enormous tree as a temporary shelter.","In his current condition, traveling anywhere would be dangerous.","’I’ll endure until the forest across the river appears again.’","Having made his decision, Ludwig turned his head.","The giraffe was lying nearby with its body curled up.","’I’ll take that fellow with me too.’","Ludwig was becoming increasingly attached to the giraffe.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 151","paragraphs":["Slave (1)","A bridge that would allow the survivors to cross the river with ease.","To properly understand its structure and underlying principles, I first built a miniature model out of twigs.","Seeing something once was better than hearing about it a hundred times, and doing it once was better than seeing it a hundred times.","Once I had a rough grasp of it, I began constructing the actual bridge.","\"How am I supposed to do this?\"","And I hit a wall the moment I started. Rather than being stuck, I simply felt overwhelmed.","It was all well and good that I’d figured out the structure and principles by making a model.","But once I began the real thing, every conceivable issue cropped up. It wasn’t as simple as planing a few pieces of wood.","I had to cut the felled trees into uniform sizes, and even using a plane was difficult since I had never done it before.","’Not being able to use aura properly is another problem.’","I still couldn’t control the cold very well, so I was avoiding using aura whenever possible.","Instead, I used mana only to reinforce my body and processed the wood without relying on aura as much as possible.","Scrape! Scrape! Scrape!","I split a felled tree cleanly in half, then split each half lengthwise again.","The trunks were so thick that sawing through them required an absurd amount of physical labor.","If I hadn’t even had a saw, I would have given up long ago.","’Whenever I do something like this, I gain even more respect for people from ancient times.’","I might have been able to grit my teeth and endure the sawing alone, but the clouds of sawdust made it even more miserable.","The dust made it hard to breathe, so I ultimately had no choice but to wear the mask I had received in preparation for the yellow dust.","Cutting a single tree, trimming it to the correct length, then using the plane to even out all the finer details...","\"Ugh. When am I going to finish all this?\"","I had barely finished processing one piece, and I nearly cursed aloud.","The sawing was exhausting, dust flew everywhere, and there was an enormous amount of wood to process.","I considered asking the raccoon family for help, but quickly abandoned the idea.","They only had a raccoon’s strength, and I was also worried they might accidentally start a fire.","’Isn’t there anyone around who can work?’","Doing everything alone was far more exhausting than I’d imagined.","I had only just started, yet I was already thinking that way.","I leaned against the pile of wood and drank a cup of water.","Even though it was still a chilly spring, sweat was pouring down my body.","’Processing the wood is one thing, but can I even erect the bridge?’","Worry was already beginning to creep into my mind.","What if I finished processing everything, only to encounter some other problem that made it impossible to build the bridge?","The thought that everything I had done so far might end up being meaningless crossed my mind.","Title: Please, just let one person come here.","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a fully processed piece of wood)","Processing wood is fucking exhausting. Please, somebody come here and help me.","└ Heavenly Demon: Is it still difficult for you to use sword energy?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. It’ll be a pain if the wood freezes.","└ SwordMaster: It must be incredibly difficult to do it with raw physical strength. Still, wouldn’t it make for good exercise?","└ Wild Grylls: My back muscles are twitching.","└ SwordMaster: Splitting firewood is extremely effective for training your back muscles. You should also take this opportunity to improve your raw physical abilities instead of relying entirely on aura.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood.","└ This guy deliberately makes his own life harder every time I see him;;","└ He said he misses people. Let’s be understanding.","└ Isn’t he looking for a slave rather than a survivor?","└ You’re right, lol. He was subtly recruiting slaves all along, lmao.","└ What do you get if you take the job?","└ What do you think you’ll get? Lmao. You’ll just become a real-life forum mod.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. Even I do not find that particularly appealing. That cannot even be called a way to pass the time.","└ Even the forum mod is refusing to become Grylls’s slave, lmao.","└ Passing Dwarf: Is woodworking that difficult? It looked easy when my friend did it, but I guess not.","└ Wild Grylls: Does that person use machinery?","└ Passing Dwarf: Of course he does in this day and age. Who does it all by hand? Lol.","└ Wild Grylls: Damn, I want a machine too.","└ Passing Dwarf: Do you even know how to use one? Would you be able to use it if somebody gave you one? Lol.","└ Wild Grylls: Sigh. Can’t a decent slave fall out of the sky somewhere?","└ Look at this shameless bastard, lmao. Earlier, he floored the accelerator the moment he saw another survivor, lmao.","└ Reality must have hit him hard. He wouldn’t have changed this much otherwise, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: If it’s this hard for me, how much harder must it be for ordinary people? I have newfound respect for them.","└ At least those people don’t do everything alone, Grylls...","└ It’s only like that because you’re alone.","└ What’s the point of humans having such a high ceiling when they’re ultimately strongest only when they work together? Lol.","└ Isn’t that also true for every other race?","└ Why don’t you make the raccoon family do it?","└ Papa Raccoon is already working. He gathers medicinal herbs.","└ What about Mama Raccoon and the baby? Try asking them.","└ You bastard, he’ll get arrested if he does that;;","└ There’s no one there to arrest him, though. Lol.","└ Oh, right. Grylls, let’s use the raccoon family as slaves. Problem solved.","└ Starlight Princess: You people are monsters. How could you even think of such a thing?","└ Wild Grylls: Honestly, I did consider it, but I discarded the idea because I was afraid they might get hurt.","└ Starlight Princess: ...I’m glad you possess at least some conscience.","└ It may be covered in fur, but he has one, lmao.","└ Grylls has a screw loose too whenever you look closely, lol.","I vented—not that it was much of a complaint—but everyone simply said whatever they wanted and left it at that.","I had only entered the Gallery to take a break anyway, so I didn’t think much of it.","└ Try asking the gorillas. Who knows? Maybe they’ll do it if you pay them with fasting pills.","└ What are they, migrant laborers? Lmao.","└ Not migrant laborers—local laborers, lol.","└ I hear beastfolk are excellent workers.","└ Should those things really be called beastfolk? Judging from how they behave, they’re closer to cavemen.","└ That’s what beastfolk are. What else would you call them?","└ Suspiciously: They’re not beastfolk, you bastards...","└ If they have fur, arms and legs, and can speak like humans, they’re beastfolk, lmao.","It wasn’t as if I had never considered hiring the gorillas in exchange for fasting pills.","However, the gorillas were Fast Sloth’s enemies.","They were full of mutual hostility, so there was no way in hell the gorillas would agree to help me.","’I have no choice but to do it myself.’","Grumbling inwardly, I resumed processing the wood.","I cut the logs crosswise, split them lengthwise, and finished by planing them.","Many a little made a mickle, and the number of finished timbers steadily grew as time passed.","’They’ll grow mold if I don’t dry them, but...’","I could fill them in with cement later or gradually replace the bridge with a stone one.","For now, I should focus solely on building the bridge.","\"Phew.\"","After quite some time had passed, I had accumulated a sizable pile of processed timber.","Of course, I was still nowhere near having enough.","In preparation for rain, I moved the timber into the cave.","For a moment, I wondered whether I should build a separate drying room, since I might need a lot of lumber in the future.","Of course, that idea was soon rejected.","’That would require me to expand the cave again.’","Unless more survivors arrived, there would be no further expansion.","Even if someone did come, they might be a person whose profession had little to do with productive labor.","Ludwig was a paladin—in other words, a soldier.","Soldiers were famously far removed from productive occupations.","’At least the inside of the cave is dry.’","The weather was still cold enough for me to keep the fireplace burning. It provided a hot and dry environment.","Naturally, one or two days wouldn’t be enough to dry the lumber completely.","According to the dwarf, it was a process that took at least several months.","It would be easiest to simply think of the wood as a temporary framework.","\"Wow. An entire day just disappeared.\"","I checked the time with an exclamation that was closer to a lament.","I had done nothing but work since lunch, yet evening was already approaching.","The sun was sinking toward the horizon, as though urging me to hurry up and stop working.","An entire day had vanished into the work, and I still wasn’t finished.","I wondered when I would ever complete it, but if I kept at it consistently, the end would eventually come into sight.","Before the sun completely set, I went up to the river. I needed to retrieve my fish traps and check the opposite bank while I was there.","’Hmm. That area is even more wretched.’","The environment across the river was even worse than the fog zone.","The ground looked as if it had absorbed a massive dose of radiation, because everything was green.","For the record, it wasn’t covered in grass. The ground itself was literally glowing green.","’What in the world happened over there to leave it in that state?’","I could only hope that whatever radioactive-looking substance it was wouldn’t affect this side of the river.","I carefully retrieved the fish caught in the traps.","Thanks to having installed two whole traps, I had caught an impressive total of five fish.","\"Kyeng!\"","Not long after I returned, Papa Raccoon came to see me.","He was holding an unfamiliar medicinal herb that resembled wild ginseng.","When I asked the Heavenly Demon, she said it was wild ginseng overflowing with internal energy. We decided to use it as an ingredient for the fasting pills.","Incidentally, the pills were nearly complete and would supposedly be ready by tomorrow morning.","I was happy, but Fast Sloth was the most excited. He certainly loved to eat.","\"You’re unbelievably good at finding wild ginseng.\"","Since he had produced such great results, I had to reward him.","I cooked one of the fish until it looked delicious and presented it to the raccoon family.","The raccoons seemed to enjoy the grilled fish, because they devoured it without leaving a trace.","\"Kiing.\"","\"Kkiing! Kking!\"","Mama Raccoon was the first to place a piece of fish into the baby raccoon’s mouth.","Seeing her feed her child before taking any for herself reminded me that they truly were a family.","’I’m a little jealous.’","Until just a few years ago, my own family and I had eaten together around the same table. A bitter smile naturally appeared on my face.","It still hurt, but I could finally cherish it as a memory. Otherwise, I would only keep tormenting myself.","After eating dinner with the raccoon family, I rested inside the warm cave.","Whoosh—","I didn’t forget to practice the cultivation technique meant to improve my control over the cold.","Although it hadn’t been long, all my effort had made controlling the cold much easier.","The mass of cold energy, which had been no larger than a grain of millet that morning, had grown to the size of a ping-pong ball.","Everything was difficult at first, but once I gained momentum, my progress accelerated rapidly.","’Simply condensing the cold isn’t enough.’","My goal was to use it whenever I wanted, not merely to separate it.","Still, my progress wasn’t bad. Only time was needed.","After finishing the cultivation technique, I connected to the Gallery.","’Nothing has changed.’","It was still ablaze with speculation and arguments about El Dorado.","People were saying that it had practically descended into civil war, but I didn’t pay much attention.","Unless Ludwig and I met and Ludwig dropped an earth-shattering revelation, this was probably as far as things would go.","’There isn’t anyone suitable to take the lead, either.’","Most importantly, there was no one willing and capable of shouldering the burden and becoming the focal point of a civil war.","Things might have been different if the Hero were present, but... Well, what did it matter?","I closed the Gallery and prepared for bed.","Wonmo was already sprawled out asleep, while Fast Sloth was once again staring blankly into the fire.","’Thinking about working again tomorrow is already suffocating.’","Couldn’t an excellent laborer fall from the heavens somewhere?","With yet another pointless thought in my mind, I slowly closed my eyes.","***","Time passed, and dawn drew near.","The crowing of roosters echoed from far away as most animals began preparing for the day.","However, because of the season, the sun had yet to fully rise.","The animals were each making their own preparations to become active.","But as the saying went, the early bird caught the worm.","While everyone else was still preparing, someone was already taking action.","Just like a certain animal staring intently at the sign installed beside the river.","\"Grrr.\"","The sign was written in several languages, and the language upon which the animal was focused was none other than the language of the Central Plains.","The animal stared quietly at those words with blood-red eyes.","It then turned its head and looked toward the place from which smoke was rising.","It was smoke coming from my chimney after Fast Sloth had spent the entire night feeding fuel into the fire.","Unlike the other gorillas, however, this one had white fur and red eyes.","Its eyes weren’t the only part of it that was red.","\"Ooh...!\"","The gorilla’s palms were as crimson as blood.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 152","paragraphs":["Slave (2)","Greetings! What a strong and mighty morning!","If you ask who I am, I’m Grylls!","Scrape! Scrape! Scrape!","And a slave to life, hard at work from the moment I wake up!","\"Ugh. Fuck.\"","I cursed at the clouds of sawdust that flew everywhere whenever I used the saw.","I had started processing the wood first thing that morning. It made me swear, but the pile of finished timber was steadily growing.","’I should’ve just asked the dwarf to do it.’","Since the wood had to be made according to the required width, I had decided that doing it myself would be better.","But that decision had been insane. Doing it alone was astonishingly inefficient.","What irritated me even more was that everything was proceeding exactly as I wanted.","You might wonder why I was angry when everything was going according to plan.","If I made a mistake, I could at least use that as an excuse to quit. But when everything was going well, I couldn’t even do that.","Eventually, I went beyond sheer stubbornness and reached a state of resignation, mechanically processing one piece of wood after another.","\"Kkyuu! Kkyuu!\"","\"Kkiing!\"","While I worked hard, Wonmo and the baby raccoon were busy playing in the yard.","Wonmo seemed to have developed a rough understanding of raccoons, because he played nicely without causing any trouble.","I did briefly wonder how they could play so carefree while their owner was working so hard.","’They’re children, after all.’","It would be strange to criticize children for playing.","Besides, hadn’t I been the one who decided to do this work?","If I got angry at them for no reason, I would be the only one acting strangely, so I had to endure it.","’Being able to work without any interruptions is already good enough.’","The only reason I could afford to work on something like this was because my life had become relatively peaceful.","If I had been fighting desperately for survival every single day, working on the bridge would have been impossible.","Moreover, winter had completely ended yesterday, so I needed to monitor the animals’ movements.","Just before winter ended, the raccoon family had been attacked by an enormous snake.","’Today might be my last peaceful day.’","The Forest of Four Seasons was a place where I had no way of knowing exactly what kinds of animals lived within it.","I had already seen quite a few animals, but an entirely new species could appear at any moment.","A real unicorn might show up, or perhaps something even stranger.","I hoped nothing like that would happen, but that was far too optimistic.","I could simply keep working and prepare myself if I ever got a bad feeling.","Snap!","Like right now, when the sound of someone stepping on a branch rang unusually loudly.","That wasn’t all. The entire forest had fallen silent.","There should have been at least some faint noises, but only a heavy silence hung in the air.","\"...\"","I stopped working and focused on the sound.","To determine whether I had heard it correctly, I also checked the reactions of the other members of my family.","\"Kkyuu?\"","Wonmo, who had been playing excitedly, had frozen in place and was looking around.","Perhaps sensing that something was wrong, he even drew his body slightly backward.","He had entered a defensive stance.","\"Kkiing?\"","\"King. Kiing.\"","The baby raccoon, on the other hand, was probably still too young to understand. It merely tilted its head in confusion.","When the far more experienced Mama Raccoon carried it away, I became certain that we were in danger.","\"Who is it?\"","I cautiously retreated toward the cave while remaining vigilant.","Whoever it was must have been observing our reactions, considering they still hadn’t revealed themselves despite already being detected.","In the meantime, I entered the cave and armed myself. Fast Sloth seemed to realize how serious the situation was, because he climbed onto my back.","Rustle—rustle—","Just as I finished equipping myself...","The bushes along the path leading up to the river shook violently.","The intruder gradually emerged. Apparently, it had no intention of concealing itself.","Rustle—","\"...\"","The intruder finally revealed itself completely.","The first thing that caught my attention was the color of its fur.","Its white fur contrasted starkly with the surrounding environment. It wasn’t the fluffy pale fur unique to an infant. Its fur was simply pure white.","The white fur already made it stand out, but its eyes were even stranger.","Its blood-red eyes looked vicious enough to make me shudder simply by staring at them.","’...A gorilla?’","The animal possessing these unusual traits was a gorilla.","A gorilla with white fur and red eyes—an albino, perhaps.","Albinism was a genetic mutation that appeared not only in animals but in humans as well.","My surprise at the appearance of the mutant gorilla lasted only briefly before I remembered the information the All-Father had given me.","’Lais Kraone was attacked and killed by an albino gorilla.’","I didn’t know the reason, but that gorilla had a history of harming humans.","Naturally, I had no choice but to raise my guard even further.","There was something else I needed to check: Fast Sloth’s reaction.","When he had seen the leader gorilla, he had even frowned, which was rare for him. But he showed no such reaction toward this albino gorilla.","His reaction was closer to, Who the hell is that guy?","Had they never met before?","’Considering it openly revealed itself instead of attacking...’","Had it lost its way, or had it merely come here to investigate?","If it was lost, I intended to threaten it and drive it away.","Meanwhile, the albino gorilla carefully examined every corner of my shelter before looking directly at me.","\"Ha piria ppazua.\"","\"...\"","\"Ni Wild Grylls ia? Wo bini Wibaek.\"","Then, just like the leader gorilla, it spoke in the language of the Central Plains.","I had already seen the leader gorilla speak, but this was hardly a situation I was accustomed to.","I couldn’t help being flustered.","\"...\"","Once again, I asked the Heavenly Demon to translate.","[Heavenly Demon: He says he came after seeing the sign. He will lend you his strength, so he wishes you to lend him yours in return.]","Had he mistaken the sign for a recruitment advertisement?","If a stranger—especially an animal—saw it, I could understand how they might reach that conclusion.","But how could I have known there would be another animal besides the leader gorilla that could read?","After recovering from my bewilderment, I made another request of the Heavenly Demon.","[Wild Grylls: Could you write something asking what he needs help with?]","[Heavenly Demon: Wait a moment.]","As I had done with the leader gorilla, I used the Heavenly Demon’s help to write what I wanted to say on the ground.","The albino gorilla stared intently at the words I had written.","\"...\"","’...Should I learn the language of the Central Plains?’","The situation was enough to make me seriously consider it.","Meanwhile, the albino gorilla continued speaking.","Everything it said was in the language of the Central Plains, so I couldn’t understand a single word.","I therefore asked the Heavenly Demon to interpret it directly.","The Heavenly Demon readily accepted my request and kindly translated(?) for me.","[Heavenly Demon: \"What a magnificent home. Are you Wild Grylls? My name is Wi Baek.\"]","[Wild Grylls: ??? He was introducing himself?]","[Heavenly Demon: It would appear so. Both he and the leader gorilla speak in a rather archaic manner.]","The albino gorilla had introduced himself as Wi Baek.","The mere fact that he had a name was absurd.","Put another way, it meant the leader gorilla probably had a name as well... But the atmosphere had been so hostile back then that I hadn’t even considered asking.","Meanwhile, the albino gorilla, Wi Baek, continued speaking at length in fluent Central Plains speech.","He squinted at the writing for quite some time. He even stretched his head forward to get a closer look.","I wondered if he couldn’t read, but fortunately, my concern proved unfounded when he finally opened his mouth.","Then I asked the Heavenly Demon to translate again.","This process repeated several times.","[Heavenly Demon: He says his hypocritical brother is leading the troop. It appears he and the leader gorilla are brothers.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh... And?]","[Heavenly Demon: He says that if you help him, he will defeat the leader gorilla. If you refuse, he will defeat you and use this place as his base.]","They said you should never take in a black-haired beast, but apparently white-haired ones were no different.","I had been relieved that we could communicate, but a beast was still a beast.","The leader gorilla was better than this guy. At least he had acknowledged my territory.","I snorted and asked the Heavenly Demon a question.","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. Could you teach me how to write \"fuck off\"?]","[Heavenly Demon: I could write down the worst insult in the Central Plains.]","[Wild Grylls: What is it? I want to say it myself.]","If I was going to do this, I wanted to say it aloud instead of merely writing it.","It took a little time, but I somehow managed to learn the pronunciation.","The words that came out of my mouth were—","\"Cao ni ma.\"","\"...\"","It was one of the harshest insults involving someone’s mother in the Central Plains. Their language really did sound similar to Chinese whenever I heard it.","I could tolerate most things, but I couldn’t stand the way he was trying to subjugate me through force.","You might ask what else I expected from a beast, but precisely because he was a beast, I could curse at him as much as I pleased.","’Besides, he’s already harmed a human before.’","That was the deciding factor.","He had a history of attacking humans, so cooperation could go to hell.","Moreover, considering that he wanted to wage war against the gorilla troop, he clearly had no grasp of reality.","Maintaining the status quo was currently my best option, yet he wanted me to destroy that balance.","Huff! Huff!","After being thoroughly insulted, the albino gorilla’s nostrils flared widely.","He looked ready to charge at me at any moment. Then again, insults about one’s mother were difficult to tolerate.","But he was the one who had crossed the line first. There was a limit to how much bullshit someone could pull before it became intolerable.","The albino gorilla’s proposal—no, his demand or threat—had gone far beyond that limit.","\"Zixun silu.\"","He spoke as he assumed a combat stance.","It probably meant something like, You court death.","I snorted and extended my sword and shield in front of me.","At the same time, I carefully observed his movements.","Until now, he had been resting both fists against the ground, so I hadn’t been able to see his palms. Once he assumed his stance, however, they became visible.","I had no idea what had happened to them, but both palms were as red as blood.","They looked ominous at a glance.","’Between his stance and those palms... he may be as strong as the leader gorilla.’","He wasn’t an opponent I could afford to underestimate. Acting rashly would be dangerous.","My only advantage was information.","I had already been thoroughly beaten by the leader gorilla once.","That meant I could respond to their fighting style to some extent, whereas this one knew nothing about me.","Boom!","While I was thinking, the albino gorilla charged at me.","There had been considerable distance between us, but he closed it in a single leap.","An enormous hand flew toward my face.","It was that blood-red palm.","’I can’t block it!’","Even if I tried, I wouldn’t be able to redirect all of its force. I would either be knocked over or leave myself vulnerable to his next attack.","That was something I had learned from fighting the leader gorilla.","Just as his palm reached my face, I swiftly ducked underneath it.","I then thrust my sword at his exposed torso.","Crack! Stab!","Something shattered as the tip of the Heavenly Demon’s sword barely penetrated his abdomen.","Normally, it shouldn’t merely have dug into him. It should have pierced straight through.","However, the albino gorilla’s hide seemed tougher than I had anticipated.","Whoosh—","Blue energy dispersed from the spot where my sword had penetrated.","I had already predicted that he could use mana, and apparently, he had activated some kind of defensive technique.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword possessed such absurd performance that it had managed to penetrate. Any ordinary sword probably wouldn’t have left so much as a scratch.","\"Oooooh!!!\"","Perhaps the albino gorilla hadn’t expected anything to pierce his body.","He cried out in surprise and leaped backward.","The wound wasn’t particularly deep, but the fact that his body had been injured at all seemed to have shocked him considerably.","That lasted only for a moment.","The albino gorilla charged at me again, looking even angrier than before.","Just like earlier, he attacked with a palm strike.","His attacks were surprisingly simple.","However—","Rumble—crash!","\"Ah, fuck.\"","Their destructive power was terrifying in proportion to their simplicity.","I narrowly dodged the attack, but I couldn’t ignore its aftermath.","The timber I had spent the entire morning processing shattered and scattered under the force of his palm strike.","Whoosh! Whoosh!","A series of wild attacks followed the initial palm strike.","Aside from his first blow, his accuracy was abysmal.","He was clearly using some form of martial arts, yet every attack missed.","It felt less like fighting a martial artist and more like dealing with someone desperately thinking, Just let me hit you once.","It was almost anticlimactic.","’What’s going on? Why is he like this?’","Things became even stranger whenever I put some distance between us.","Once we were far enough apart and some time had passed, he would charge and unleash another palm strike.","During those moments alone, his accuracy was remarkably high—enough to make my blood run cold.","Of course, every attack that followed would be terrible.","’It’s almost like he’s blind despite having his eyes open...’","The instant that expression crossed my mind, I stared at the albino gorilla.","His face was tightly scrunched up. Rather than looking angry, it seemed as though he was struggling to see.","’What if the accuracy of his first strike comes from focusing as hard as possible?’","What if his following attacks were so sloppy because he was afraid of being counterattacked?","Most importantly, he was an albino—an animal with white fur and red eyes.","And one of the common characteristics of albinism was—","’Extremely poor eyesight.’","I had discovered the key to defeating him.","’I’ll personally make you my slave.’","I would inflict suffering worse than death upon him.","I gradually accelerated the mana inside my body.","The cold energy that had been condensed into a sphere completely permeated my mana.","Whoosh—","It was time to subdue him."]},{"title":"Chapter 153","paragraphs":["Slave (3)","Let me make one thing clear: discovering his weakness didn’t mean I could take control of the fight.","Even if the albino gorilla was weaker than the leader gorilla, he was still a creature that had survived in the Forest of Four Seasons.","And he had done so despite the immense disadvantages of white fur and poor eyesight that came with albinism.","Either one of those traits would pose a major threat to survival, yet he had survived just fine.","In other words, he possessed something capable of compensating for those disadvantages.","Boom!","When the albino gorilla stomped the ground, a faint tremor spread through the area.","At the same time, his enormous palm flew toward my face.","Fortunately, I narrowly avoided it by turning my head.","However—","Rumble—crash!","The towering trees around us toppled beneath the pressure generated by the strike.","It was less powerful than what the leader gorilla had demonstrated, but still more than strong enough.","If I took a direct hit, my head would explode.","’What is that, the Buddha’s Palm?’","What kind of martial art—no, martial technique—had he learned to leave such devastation in his wake?","The leader gorilla had given me a rough idea of what to expect, but the aftermath was still beyond my imagination.","I clicked my tongue inwardly as I watched the albino gorilla.","Boom!","The moment he finished attacking, he stomped the ground again and threw a punch.","Realizing that his poor eyesight put him at a disadvantage, he seemed to have altered his method of attack to capitalize on his strengths.","He assumed his stance and attacked, then assumed his stance again and launched another attack.","His attacks were both incredibly loud and extremely threatening.","They technically formed a combination, but each strike was so distinctly separated that I wasn’t sure it could truly be called one.","’Still, this won’t last long.’","It was a textbook case of someone relying on the mentality of I only need to land one hit.","If even one of those blows connected by chance, I would be finished.","However, despite the gorilla pushing his body as hard as possible, there was still a noticeable gap between each movement.","Even attempting to overcome his poor vision with a continuous barrage of attacks had its limitations.","If I could exploit that opening somehow, I would be able to counterattack.","’Even if it means breaking my arm, I need to keep my shield raised.’","Against creatures like him, my shield was a means of protecting my life.","I intended to dodge everything if possible, but he might have a hidden trump card.","Besides, I was still more accustomed to wielding my sword with one hand than with both.","I carefully studied the albino gorilla’s attack pattern and waited for my opportunity.","Boom!","The albino gorilla stomped the ground in preparation for another attack.","I seized that opening and slipped inside his reach.","He continued his attack, apparently unaware that I had closed the distance.","In other words, he struck nothing but empty air.","’Just as I thought.’","His weakness remained the same: if his opponent moved quickly right before he attacked, he would miss.","Until now, he had probably fought by constantly pressuring his opponents and never surrendering the initiative.","Stab!","But against an opponent capable of thinking even a little, the method for countering him was quickly exposed.","It was almost miraculous that he had survived this long.","As the albino gorilla struck empty air, I drove my sword into his foot.","The blade pierced straight through the top of his foot and sank into the ground.","That wasn’t all.","Crackle! Crack!","When I released the cold, his foot began freezing.","It didn’t happen gradually. In an instant, the ice spread beyond his foot and reached his knee.","\"Uoh?!\"","The albino gorilla grimaced from the pain of being stabbed, then jumped in surprise.","Judging from his reaction, he had never encountered an enemy with an ability like mine.","This was the perfect opportunity.","I acted before the gorilla could free himself.","Stab!","I drove my sword into his other foot and froze that one as well.","Naturally, both of the gorilla’s legs became trapped in ice.","Considering the strength he had demonstrated earlier, it seemed as though he should have been able to break free easily...","But that wasn’t the case at all.","’As expected, his lower body is comparatively weak.’","It was a physical limitation of gorillas.","They naturally lived with both arms supporting them against the ground.","No matter how much they behaved like humans, walking entirely upright on two legs was difficult for them.","The leader gorilla was well aware of this and had hardly ever used kicks.","The albino gorilla struggled to escape, but breaking through the ice using only the strength of his lower body appeared difficult.","He would have to deal with the ice encasing his legs first.","He raised his massive arms to smash it.","Crunch!","\"Oooargh!!\"","But I was one step faster.","I drove my sword into one of his enormous arms.","Just as it had with his legs, the ice spread across his arm until it reached his shoulder.","The ice was remarkably strong, and even he couldn’t break it easily.","Only one arm remained.","Thanks to the gorilla panicking, I was able to subdue that one just as easily.","\"Oooaaah!\"","\"God, you’re loud.\"","Smack!","He kept struggling to break free, so I struck him across the face with my shield.","He remained conscious after the first blow, so I hit him again.","Only then did he finally quiet down.","The gorilla went limp with his tongue hanging out.","I had struck him with the intention of knocking him unconscious, but the fact that it actually worked was somehow unexpected.","However...","’Would tying him up really be enough to immobilize him?’","I stared at the unconscious albino gorilla and considered the problem.","Like the leader gorilla, this one could use mana.","Moreover, he could perform formidable martial techniques, so ordinary restraints wouldn’t be enough.","Crackle! Crack!","I bound him as tightly as possible with a rope, then froze his entire body except for his head.","I would have preferred to bind him in chains, but there hadn’t been any available at the Auction House.","\"Fast Sloth, I need to check something for a moment. Keep a close watch on him.\"","\"...\"","\"If he looks like he’s about to escape, hit him in the face.\"","Even if the gorilla attempted to escape, Fast Sloth was here, so I wasn’t worried.","Before connecting to the Gallery, I surveyed the devastation the gorilla had caused.","All the timber I had painstakingly processed had been blown away, and the surrounding area had been wrecked.","Fortunately, the cave remained intact, but my workload had increased considerably.","’I want to use him as a laborer somehow...’","I had already devised a method, but I wasn’t sure whether it would work.","Before that, I should post something in the Gallery.","I had plenty of time to think.","(Photo of the albino gorilla frozen while bound with rope)","(Photo of the devastation caused by the albino gorilla)","This bastard suddenly showed up at my shelter and invited me to fight the leader gorilla with him.","When I refused, he tried to kill me. So I subdued him for now, and I’m trying to decide how he should compensate me.","Title: Caught an Albino Gorilla","Wild Grylls","└ Heavenly Demon: Was he considerably skilled?","└ Wild Grylls: Aside from his extremely poor eyesight, he was strong. If I hadn’t encountered the leader gorilla first, I might have been in danger.","└ Heavenly Demon: He appears to have some connection to that leader gorilla. Did you notice anything unusual about him?","└ Wild Grylls: Nothing in particular, except that his palms were noticeably red.","└ Heavenly Demon: Palms as red as blood... His martial technique does not appear to be of particularly good quality.","└ SwordMaster: I agree. Doesn’t something like that usually mean the user is being consumed by a particular energy?","└ Heavenly Demon: You are well informed. Black discoloration would be related to demonic energy, while red would be connected to blood energy... It appears we will need to interrogate him.","└ Wild Grylls: The leader gorilla’s palms looked normal, though.","└ Heavenly Demon: The situation would be different if he had reached a certain realm. It would mean he possessed a deeper understanding of the technique.","That meant the albino gorilla wasn’t weak.","The leader gorilla was simply absurdly powerful.","The albino gorilla was in a similar situation to mine.","Since I had prioritized survival, I had only skimmed the surface of what I learned instead of studying it deeply.","└ Wild Grylls: Before that, I need to decide what to do with this bastard. Is Princess Cheonggu here?","└ Princess Cheonggu: Why do you need me?","└ Why are these gorillas such assholes? Last time they broke into someone else’s house and stole from him, and now some random nobody has shown up, lmao.","└ Isn’t expecting morality from gorillas the real mistake? These bastards are animals;;","└ Fair point. I accept that.","└ The leader gorilla is pretty kind by gorilla standards. He let Grylls live, didn’t he?","└ Put another way, doesn’t that mean having a rotten personality gives you an advantage in survival?","└ Surviving is what makes you strong, lol.","└ By the way, did that nobody gorilla speak too?","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah. He spoke the language of the Central Plains.","└ What did you say when he started spouting nonsense?","└ Wild Grylls: I cursed at him, and he threw a fit.","Princess Cheonggu must have been watching even though she hadn’t left any comments.","I had planned to send her a private message even if she wasn’t watching.","Since she happened to be reading the thread, I decided to handle everything there.","Besides, I could acquire all sorts of useful information, so I continued through the comments.","└ A time-honored insult involving someone’s mother—even works on animals, lmao.","└ Who the hell taught these gorillas the language of the Central Plains?","└ Ask him when he wakes up. I’m curious too.","└ Wild Grylls: Athletes are strictly forbidden from using mana, right?","└ Princess Cheonggu: Of course. They could accidentally kill their opponent.","└ Wild Grylls: Then does that mean there are tools capable of suppressing mana?","└ Princess Cheonggu: Don’t tell me you’re planning to put one on that gorilla?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes.","└ Holy shit, that’s slavery, lmao.","└ I don’t think that’s a very good idea;; So what if he can’t use mana? He’ll just destroy everything with brute strength.","└ No matter how stupid a gorilla is, it can tear a human apart with ease;;","Most people caused an uproar, saying it was insane and that I would get myself killed.","It was true that a gorilla’s physical strength could tear a human apart like kimchi.","Moreover, this albino gorilla was a mana user. His physical abilities were probably far greater than those of an ordinary gorilla.","In other words, merely fitting him with a mana-suppressing device wouldn’t solve the problem completely.","└ Wild Grylls: Don’t worry. I’m in the same situation anyway.","└ How are you in the same situation?","└ Wild Grylls: (Photo of Fast Sloth) This is my master, bastards. Greet him.","└ Ahahahahahahahaha!","└ Lmaoooooooooo!","└ He really was a slave, lmao!","└ I hadn’t even considered that, hahahaha!","└ Grylls, you bastard... You did this because you wanted a friend, didn’t you?","└ Not a friend. A comrade.","But with Fast Sloth around, the situation was different.","The people in the Gallery took it as a joke, but I was half joking and half serious.","If I didn’t consistently offer tribute(?) to this creature, my life would be in danger.","If the albino gorilla tried to threaten me, I could simply leave him to Fast Sloth. The problem would be resolved in no time.","└ Princess Cheonggu: I do have something similar. It’s an old model, though, so it’s a little extreme. Is that all right?","└ Wild Grylls: What does it do?","└ Princess Cheonggu: First, it can’t be removed without the key. And if it detects mana being used, it sends an electrical current through the wearer’s entire body.","└ Wild Grylls: That sounds incredible. I’ll buy it right now.","└ Princess Cheonggu: You don’t need to buy it. I’ll just give it to you. I’ve been struggling to find a use for it anyway.","└ Isn’t that literally a restraint device?","└ I heard they used tools like that back when slavery still existed...","└ Yeah, that’s right. They’re still used on prisoners. Modern athletic mana suppressors were invented using those as the basis.","I received a mana suppressor from Princess Cheonggu.","Its overall shape resembled a dog collar.","It also had sharp spikes designed to prevent the wearer from forcibly removing it.","[Princess Cheonggu: Put this on the gorilla, then hide the key.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. But what is this bracelet?]","Princess Cheonggu had given me not only the suppressor and its key but also a bracelet.","When I asked what the bracelet was for, I received a rather disturbing answer.","[Princess Cheonggu: If the gorilla lays a hand on you, an electrical current will run through him just like before. It’s for your safety.]","[Wild Grylls: Excuse me, but this isn’t actually something that was used when slavery was widespread, is it?]","[Princess Cheonggu: It was invented to protect referees. There used to be a lot of athletes who committed violence against them. It should prove quite useful.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. I’ll put it to good use.]","[Princess Cheonggu: And what do you say when you’re grateful? Hehe.]","[Wild Grylls: Chae-U is divine, and Kone is invincible.]","[Princess Cheonggu: Very good! I have another match in two days, so I’ll be counting on you then!]","I didn’t know exactly what she was counting on me to do, but cheering enthusiastically should be enough.","After learning how to use the device, I fastened the suppressor around the albino gorilla’s neck.","\"Ugh...\"","By coincidence, the albino gorilla regained consciousness just as I put it on him.","I was startled, but the suppressor was already secured, so I decided to see what happened.","The albino gorilla stared at me with a dazed expression.","Because of his poor eyesight, his initial reaction was something close to, Who are you?","That didn’t last long.","\"Ooh! Ooooooh!\"","He became so enraged that he seemingly forgot how to speak like a human.","The beast glared fiercely at me with his blood-red eyes.","Then his body twitched as if he were attempting to use mana.","Bzzzzzt!!!","\"Ookiiaaaah!!!\"","Just as Princess Cheonggu had said, a powerful electrical current erupted from the suppressor around his neck.","No matter how powerful an animal was, all creatures were equal before electricity.","After he had been thoroughly shocked into submission, I spoke to him.","\"Hey, say that again. What was it about turning this place into your base?\"","\"Ugh...\"","He might not have understood my words, but perhaps he could tell I was mocking him.","The albino gorilla glared at me again, but it was pointless.","Bzzzzzt!","Another electrical current flowed from the collar, subduing him immediately.","After being electrocuted twice in succession, the albino gorilla slumped weakly.","I smiled in satisfaction and opened my mouth.","\"What did you say your name was? Wi Baek?\"","\"Ugh...\"","Someone once said that a slave had no need for his former name.","I considered what suitable name I could give him before grinning.","I didn’t know whether he would understand, but it didn’t matter.","I could repeat it until he did.","\"From now on, your name is Kkobong. Understand?\"","Through the Gallery, I had acquired myself a laborer."]}]);
